{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again","id":1291019,"title":"Why are Lunars allowed to combine native charms and martial arts again?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-22T23:33:05-08:00","id":1291019,"title":"Why are Lunars allowed to combine native charms and martial arts again?","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>tl;dr Summary</b></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Allowing Lunar native charms to access martial arts creates not only several major balance concerns but also concerns about making other characters invalidated or eclipsed by Lunars. It makes balancing martial arts from here on out far more difficult when you need to account for Lunar charms gaining access to such a thing, at least not without investing an absurd amount of time.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Introduction</b></span><br /> <br /> Back when we were all shiny eyed and bushy tailed with the Ex3 Kickstarter, we all gathered around and listened with awe-eyed rapture with tales of Ex3. Those new to Exalted were introduced to the wonderful setting while even jaded veterans like myself could only dream of an Exalted game without paranoia combat or taking several hours to inflict a single level of damage on an opponent. It was back then I first heard of ideas being thrown out for the future, one of them being, \u201cLunars will be able to combine MA together with their native charms!\u201d<br /> <br /> I immediately knew this would be a horrific idea. But naysayers shot me down. Saying wait until the charms are out, THEN give your piece of advice on this. So that\u2019s fair. I waited, I waited for a long time. I kept my stance of combining MA and native charms would be a bad idea, but didn\u2019t press it until we\u2019ve seen the charms. I was concerned, but I\u2019ve long since held the belief that if you didn\u2019t observe the material you\u2019re commenting on then any points or concerns you make are flimsy at best.<br /> <br /> But then the Lunar Kickstarter charm packet was released to the backers. And as myself, a proud backer of the deluxe hardcover (Which I can actually afford as I don\u2019t need to worry about finding food to eat anymore) I opened up the charms early in the morning, read through the offensive and defense dexterity charms and...<br /> <br /> Realized every worry and fear I had about native charms and MA working together on Lunars was outright confirmed.<br /> <br /> You may be asking why I\u2019m so worried? I\u2019m worried because outside of a few specific niche builds, this change makes Lunars, bar none, the best martial artists in the entire game. To the point where if you wanted to be another splat focusing on MA then you\u2019d be an idiot to pass up being a Lunar. I\u2019m willing to procrastinate some things such as my Youtube videos for this, so let\u2019s dive into it~<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>DISCLAIMER</b></span><br /> <br /> But let\u2019s make one thing that\u2019s going to remain universally true throughout this entire verbal diatribe: These Lunars are still some of the best Lunar\u2019s we\u2019ve got. Is it worth forsaking an entire splat over the issues raised here? Hell no. I have great confidence that Lunars working within the confines of their own splat have relatively few issues. Some things will break due to how potent some animal traits are when placed on Lunars (Armoured Terror soak reduction, ELEPHANTS) but I think all of us were fully expecting that to happen even from day one. The benefits of getting an actual, working Lunars charmset with people who understand <i>how the system actually works</i> is a benefit that speaks for itself. What I\u2019m concerned is about system trends going forward and showing how such things can be a problem even if you don\u2019t do stupid minmax builds that snap the system in two. No, I\u2019m seeking to show relatively common problems that can show up in casual play.<br /> <br /> Neither do I hate Lunars or Ex3 as a whole. Do I think Ex3 as a whole is flawless? Hell no, I\u2019ve been putting off another essay for quite some time (Aura\u2019s make me wish Elemental surcharges returned). Do I still love the line? God yes! If I didn\u2019t care about the line I wouldn\u2019t have dropped the dosh for a deluxe book, I wouldn\u2019t have written literally hundreds of thousands of words of completely free material, I wouldn\u2019t have bothered writing this essay when I could\u2019ve been playing Nier: Automata. I write this essay because I care deeply for the line and am concerned about some core design choices. If I need to pull off Jim Sterling\u2019s \u201cOne True Zelda fan\u201d then so be it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Martial Arts: History and Raison d\u2019etre</b></span><br /> <br /> My issue involves getting to know some of the more advanced concepts about charms and their balance, and to do that we\u2019re going to need a bit of a history lesson. So what are Martial Arts? I was going to save this for a charm creation tutorial one day but I guess I can bust it out early. The answer to this question lines in the very beginning of Martial Arts: A self-contained set of charms that (most) people in the setting would be able to access. These charms would be powerful effects that, unlike other attack abilities, could be combined with each other! Those who walk the path of the Ebon Shadow could learn the savagery of Tiger style. Not only that, but martial arts allowed one to explore concepts entirely outside the theme of what their splat would normally allow or get mechanics that were not only strange but highly sought after for reasons both In Character and Out of Character. White Veil allowed one to attack in social gala\u2019s undiscovered while Crystal Chameleon allowed one to make stealth rolls while in bonfire. These martial arts are not only cool but opened up entirely new ways to play a character!<br /> <br /> This made an interesting interplay where one could not only gain access to more styles and more powerful, but often required careful research on what styles are compatible. See martial arts have a feature that strictly limits what weapons and armour one may use. This caused those who truly want a martial arts character to start hitting the books. They needed to deeply research details such as what weapon their character would use in order to maximize cross compatibility, what armour to take to determine if they\u2019d need to invest in their splat\u2019s own native toughness charms, and lore connections detailing information about the character\u2019s sifu or how they learned this mystical art.<br /> <br /> From the mechanics point of view this is accomplished by each martial art having very significant deliberately inserted in the style itself. Ebon Shadow is an excellent martial arts style that supplements stealth. It has some tricks to keep you alive, but if you\u2019re hit then you\u2019re going to be feeling it. To offset this a character might decide to go into Tiger Style as well, that way in the off chance he\u2019s discovered or going up against a character that hard counters his stealth then he can still contribute in a tough battle or (more likely) want some additional power and toughness. The Ebon Shadow Stylist could instead learn some Crystal Chameleon charms, granting her the capability to hide not only in shadows but in light. But oh no! Crystal Chameleon has weapons that are compatible with Tiger or Ebon Shadow! (For sake of argument, let\u2019s say this is the case). That means that our martial artist needs to think carefully about his choices. Would the increased flexibility be worth the loss of power from going unarmed? What about the cool evocations the weapon or armour could provide? For people who liked CharOp this was an enjoyable puzzle, trying to figure out which combination of weapons, armour, and native charms would best supplement a chosen martial arts style to make it shine.<br /> <br /> Now the issue with Lunars is that do you see the careful balancing MA charms needed to have with each other? Do you see the time and research needed for checking cross compatible martial arts styles? Take all of that and throw it right out the fucking window. The baby goes out with the bathwater as now Lunars can combine any martial art with a single style that\u2019s omni-applicable to weapons/armour, can fill nearly any hole/niche your martial arts leaves with ease, and trivally do things that even those with the mastery keyword would trade their soul for.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sorry it feels like I\u2019ve stepped back in time to the 2.Xe Exalted patch era, where everyone had their own patch. Allowing MA\u2019s with ability charms was something I\u2019ve seen more than once, but it was shot down multiple times. Trying to seriously argue the merits of this would get you laughed at or a sidelook in disbelief. None better to argue this point is the terror of 2.Xe himself Jon Chung. To those unfamiliar to him he\u2019s a man with extensive system knowledge. He pointed out the issues of Exalted 2e \u2018paranoia\u2019 combat, playtested the 2.5e update, and even made the prototype of the Mastery/Terrestrial keywords we see today in martial arts. He\u2019s a condescending asshole who\u2019s also been banned off multiple forums due to his behavior alone, but just because one\u2019s an asshole doesn\u2019t mean the points are not still valid. I\u2019ll go ahead and quote one of the messages he left about regards of martial arts combining with native charms (with some slight edits):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201c(Respectable person), if you\u2019re going to argue that combinatorial hell is not a thing re-designing charms, in the sense that you do not need to look at every charm (and special use artifact, and hearthstone power, and bullshit merit, and sorcerous buff spell, etc...) that can interact with the one you are writing while you are writing it, I\u2019m (going to find such an undertaking quite humorous).<br /> <br /> The larger the set of difference bits of rules exceptions a given proposed rule exception can interact with, the higher the chances are that some kind of dumbshit broken interaction will exist: see the entire publication history of Exalted, Magic The Gathering, D&amp;D, etc etc for choice examples. In order to reduce the number of dumbshit broken interactions in an exception-based game, said game should there try to keep the number of exception-packets any given exception-packet can interact with with a reasonable minimum, while satisfying other design goals.<br /> <br /> For example, if we want it to be easy to assemble NPC\u2019s on the fly, we can simply use some of the wordcount (from other sections in the book) to make prefabricated competency-packages which can only use the set of native charms and commonly available equipment, take up vastly less space than martial arts styles, and are orders of magnitude easier to balance, as we are creating no new effects and only suggesting sets of already extant effects that work together well to accomplish some goal or satisfy some competency.<br /> <br /> If our only goal is this, going for Martial Arts as collections of universally available, universally interacting splat agnostic charms in order to do it is a madman\u2019s choice. Who has the time to test all those combinations? </div> </div> </div>Note this was called back in March 31, 2015. Nearly four years ago. Chung doesn\u2019t know 3e as well as 2e, but I can tell you right now that passage is still accurate to this day. Chung may have been advocating for removing MA entirely, but even if we kept it we\u2019d still need to deal with some of its ugly issues that crops up for Lunars.<br /> <br /> Not to say it doesn\u2019t exist already. Martial Arts is odd in the sense that certain charms snap it in two while other sets are seen as supplementing it. For example, Dodge is considered when making martial arts as is Resistance. Martial Arts that normally rely on Dodge have an advantage defensively as expand your native charms as you please. Access to say, Melee parry charms, would completely break some of the ideas certain MA\u2019s have, turning them from mid-tier to top tier almost instantly.<br /> <br /> So let\u2019s delve into some of the crunch issues then, shall we?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Lunars and Martial Arts: The Ultimate Team</b></span><br /> <br /> So you\u2019re wondering why I\u2019m proclaiming doom and gloom when I have no shit to back this time. Remember what I said earlier about each MA being tightly contained examples of balance? Let\u2019s use some fun charms from the Lunar set to discuss some wonderful combat examples with Martial arts.<br /> <br /> <b>CRANE</b><br /> <br /> Crane now has access to onslaught and other penalty negators. This now makes it one of the most aggravating styles to fight in the game. The one flaw a mastery stylist of Crane style had, that is piling on onslaught, is now virtually negated. You are now pounding your fists against a 10 defense wall that causes your ST or player to rip their notes in two.<br /> <br /> Crane\u2019s issue of damage is all but completely eliminated as well. Crane was often heavily reliant on using a fan to bounce back damage until your capstone (Which at that point you don\u2019t care what your initiative is so long as it\u2019s a positive number). Even with the fan you were potentially limited by the damage your own opponent could put out. Now we don\u2019t need to worry about that. We can use our strength charms or excellency to boost the damage of our somewhat lacking damage.<br /> <br /> So now we\u2019re shattering the entire action economy across its knee, able to spam cheap counterattacks all day without anything holding them back.<br /> <br /> Lol, Lunars.<br /> <br /> <b>SINGLE SHINING POINT INTO THE VOID</b><br /> <br /> Ah yes the meme style! Which everyone cries about how horrifically broken the style is before they learn the game devouring terror Righteous Devil becomes. Despite cries of how OP this style is you need to realize several things about it, big damn flaws the style has:<ul><li>Its defense options are laughable. Gathering Light Concentration is more of an offense charm as it flips onslaught to the opponent. If you\u2019re hit with this style then you can only rely on your armour.</li> <li>Single Point stylist\u2019s are utterly addicted to their secondary initiative track. This is because the entire style involves specializing against a single opponent until you can overkill them, and two initiative tracks barely gives the opponent time to breathe. If you\u2019re a pure Single Point stylist then you\u2019re going to need that second attack to keep up your pressure, as your recourse for being attacked is extremely limited.</li> <li>Fatal Stroke Flash is one of the strongest damage adders in the game but carries an insane cost if you miss. Those running Single Point should know if an opponent has some sort of perfect defense (IE: One capable of automatically protecting against an attack, such as Seven Shadows Evasion) then chances to activating it without being sucker punched immediately after if you fail is extremely slim. To those pointing out how the capstone Blinding Nova Flare \u2018solves\u2019 this problem, it doesn\u2019t: Clash attacks still exist. All the capstone does is merely give another option.</li> <li>It cannot compete with upper tier accuracy adders. Solar Melee annihilates Single Point in clashes. Hell even Dragonblooded charms stand some good chance at clashing Single Point with its own charms. In terms of attack rolls Single Point offers reliability but not explosive power.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Whether you agree with me or not Single Point being overrated the points I presented are some of the things significantly hindering Single Point style. Even with these flaws it's still a damn good martial arts style. Now what if we took all of these things holding it back and burn all to the ground? That answer is simple: We have Lunars.<br /> <br /> Now we have a way to get two initiative tracks at once! All of those annoy restrictions Flying Silver Dream had in place for minor details such as balance? Out the door! Now you too can have two initiative tracks for the low low price of three charm buy ins!<br /> <br /> And don\u2019t say the form is only worth using as Mastery style. It ain\u2019t. The initiative drip is annoying but hardly crippling to the style as a whole. The sword\u2019s damage being capped by the stylist\u2019s own initiative is more of an important point but even then that\u2019s enough to tear a solid chunk out of someone (Or usually just save it to activate one of the charms that require both attacks).. The only really nasty thing is losing the form when crashed as 10m per pop ain\u2019t cheap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u2019s because its Single Point. The entire style is busted. </div> </div> </div>Not to this extent. Flying Silver Dream would be equivalent to the same shenanigans if it essentially gave a second track. <b>Why are Lunars allowed to get a free pass?</b><br /> <br /> Lol, Lunars.<br /> <br /> <b>SNAKE</b><br /> <br /> Snake Strikes the Heel is incredibly bullshit. Using your withering accuracy dicepool on a clash vs an opponent who probably has a -3 attack penalty on them already? A potential difference of seven dice before charms? Yea good luck. Now what if we made it better! How about we add a charm that rerolls (Essence) dice that didn\u2019t show up as successes? You can with Lunars!<br /> <br /> Lol, Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>DREAMING PEARL COURTESAN STYLE</b><br /> <br /> All of my attacks now have short range? For the rest of the scene? With the only downside being using a Fan/ribbon as my potential non-unarmed weapon forever and capable of being buffed by my native charms? Mm! Yes please!<br /> <br /> Lol, Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>RIGHTEOUS DEVIL STYLE</b><br /> <br /> Because clearly, the one thing this style needed is more damage. So let\u2019s go ahead and give it that. I won\u2019t debate that Mastery is nasty on this style, but Lunar charms only adding damage to a style which is overly rich in options already doesn\u2019t help much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sandact most of the damage charms are not even out yet </div> </div> </div>Then let\u2019s look at other things. Well the style is locked by the range of the weapon! Firewands are short range. Capping range is something important to consider when making evocations that operate with Righteous Devil, so there\u2019s something from stopping it to fi-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u201dRighteous Devil Style\u201d</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, at the beginning of each turn, the Righteous Devil may reflexively aim against any enemy whose Resolve was overcome by the activation of this form, or by a similar influence roll made in combat (even if he resisted).</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Oh...</i><br /> <br /> You know what this means right?<br /> <br /> It means if we ever have a range extender Lunars can now attack medium or longer range virtually all the time. Given that this is a very common charm, it's probably gonna be in it. Fuck it, grab double firewands, become a black horse Lunar and name yourself \u201cThe Outsider\u201d. Have fun kiting everyone ever with them having little chance to catch up if this is ever the case.<br /> <br /> Oh and we have Finding the Needle\u2019s Eye, Striking Mospid Method, and Stinging Ichneumon Scourge to better hit your enemies. Because such things are clearly needed on a style the reflexively and automatically aims at nearly every single enemy once per round with an easy activation condition.<br /> <br /> So now we have one of the strongest style\u2019s in the game (If not the strongest period) have its cap completely blown off by a set that allows infinite expansion and works with not only literally other MA in existence but also supplements your native charms just fine. You don\u2019t need to worry about evocations being locked to a specific weapon and panicking if such a weapon is disarmed from you.<br /> <br /> Lol, Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>STEEL DEVIL</b><br /> <br /> Putting ice cream on top of a pile of garbage still has you eating garbage.<br /> <br /> Lol, Steel Devil.<br /> <br /> <br /> But there is a very important point to consider here! The old Martial Arts were admitted by Vance to be written in a different time. A time when Hungry Tiger Technique cost 1m and didn\u2019t care whenever or not your opponent was crashed or not. It was a time when charms were a bit stronger before being toned down. Sadly (or fortunately) Martial Arts charms didn\u2019t get the same treatment nor did we see Heaven\u2019s Ladder style. But with this knowledge in mind can we just... ignore this problem? The core MA charms could very well have balance issues, so warning people to keep careful eye on them is much easier now that, rest assured, we have knowledge that future MA charms will be a bit more tuned.<br /> <br /> Yes! To a certain point that is true. The Immaculate MA\u2019s do better on Lunars because of their charm sharing than Solars while Golden Janissary and Mantis work but add other problems: The amount of resources needed to use the styles if you\u2019re a non-lunar and the native charm comparisons.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Cost of Mastery</b></span><br /> <br /> The resources needed to purchase martial arts as a Lunar. Well we need the merit to do so, a four dot feat tax. Expensive but all splats (so far) need to grin and bear it, so that\u2019s not as much of a factor, so that\u2019s not much of a factor of determining who\u2019s stronger or weaker here.<br /> <br /> So the main kicker here then is that Lunars are going to pay for MA as if it were unfavored. Martial Arts cost 10 XP per pop and increasing an ability costs are current rating x2. This is compared to the Solar/Dragonblooded cost of (Current Rating x2) -1 and 8 XP per pop since they can be favored.<br /> <br /> What does this mean? It means that to go from MA 0 -&gt; 5 costs 23 XP unfavored and 19 XP favored. Styles with 8-10 charms can run you 80-100 XP unfavored or 64-80 XP favored. This is a difference of 16 to 20 XP. Two favored charms, but honestly if you\u2019re getting proper bang for your buck this isn\u2019t that bad. Evocations cost the same amount, and depending on your weapon choice and character build, its XP well spent.<br /> <br /> So why do people treat this as the devil again? You\u2019re so focused on cost efficiency you\u2019re making a mountain out of a molehill when there\u2019s not too terribly much of a gap to begin with. This is especially true when you can use Splat XP to purchase MA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Sandact! To learn an entirely new MA will cost Lunars more in the long run! </div> </div> </div>Why are you bothering learning another MA as a Lunar?<br /> <br /> You literally have no need to learn another MA as you have an omni-compatible, infinitely expandable \u201cMA\u201d style right at your fingertips. Hell, if you\u2019re matching your style then you don\u2019t even need to go all in that much even! A Snake stylist is likely going to have high Dex so he doesn\u2019t need to spring for a whole new style. He can just buy his native charms to shore up his attack! If you need more damage you\u2019d buy more strength, which even unfavored can potentially bring big gains with smart charm decision to cover any gaps in your MA style.<br /> <br /> Any issue relating to Mastery users needing to buy up other MA\u2019s is utterly laughable in comparison. Not only can you infinitely branch out if you felt the need to, but you don\u2019t need to buy any more dots in a style beyond the first 5 you\u2019d need which post people in the course of the game will get to five in at least one combat ability (If not just starting with it).<br /> <br /> The only reason I see are character reasons or if you REALLY want a specific MA charm (EX: Crane\u2019s wanting Crippling Pressure-Point Strike for methods to take out the opponent that don\u2019t involve resetting) or just specific forms (Crane, Single Point, or Righteous Devil). The latter I predict is going to be far more valuable. Things like Mantis form would be welcome, but you\u2019re probably gonna want other native charms if all you want is a form from something like that. The other, last remaining, alternative is if you picked up a weapon only style and want to branch out a bit by learning some other weapons or learning to fight unarmed in the off chance you find yourself without them (Amazing how many people forget about disarm in the heat of the moment).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Sandact! What about the Mastery keyword! That makes or breaks some charms! It obviously tilts the direction back towards Mastery! </div> </div> </div>Hardly. There are some mastery bonuses which I admit make some charms downright bonkers. Lone Spark Lights the Conflagration\u2019s Mastery bonus clearly sets it apart from its normal form. Caress of 1,000 Hells Mastery bonus is likely going to end the fight by the sheer amount of potential penalties an opponent could take. But again this doesn\u2019t make up for the fact that you get and infinitely expandable charmset to cover and expand such holes. Even if you can\u2019t gain access to some mastery effects you can keep up really damn well. Some cases, such as Snake clashing, you probably even exceed them in such areas.<br /> <br /> So you know where this really hits hard? Feeling that your character is punched in the dick by this. Feeling that another character can get far more bang for the buck compared to you because they can do better in your own niche for a cheaper and easier cost. Not only that, but Lunars can \u201cdouble dip\u201d into their styles with normal native charms and splat XP, amplifying the power of their martial arts charms with their own native charms, compared to Solars which cannot do the same or are forced to buy up an entirely new ability (which the Lunar probably doesn\u2019t need to do).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Sandact! What about Supernal!? </div> </div> </div>Supernal is a hell of a drug, but not everyone is going to be Dawns or Dusk caste\u2019s in a game. By the time people reach Essence 3, which is the real meat of game or where most of them choose as an ending point, Supernal is going to taper off rapidly for martial arts around this point. The only exception being the rare MA that goes beyond ESS 3 such as Crane style. Immaculate MA\u2019s also get a notable mention but some Solars may shy away from it due to having no aura. This also steps into issues of Solars feeling Supernal for MA could very well be a bust because at the moment we don\u2019t have many martial arts that go to essence 5 right now. Beyond the Immaculate styles.<br /> <br /> So yes, enjoy the head start advantage. It's not going to last forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Unison of Soul and Blade</b></span><br /> <br /> Ah yes evocations, the new subsystem in 3e that gives artifacts life beyond a mere pile of stats or gimmicky one-trick ponies. It is no secret that evocations are extremely potent not only in power but function similar to Martial Arts. The open up entirely new ways to play your character, ranging from minor but useful effects to weapons of mass destruction. The beauty of evocations: They can be used with Martial Arts. Combined with an Artifact 5 weapon we have an infinite range to \u2018expand\u2019 our attack set to cover weaknesses our core MA cannot cover.<br /> <br /> It seems like we\u2019ve all but solved our MA problem! An infinitely expandable set in exchange for nearly all your background dots and probably a glare from the Storyteller. Are we finally done with this nightmare?<br /> <br /> Not even close.<br /> <br /> Evocations are powerful but they also often have one big hole inside of them: They cannot outright replace your bread-and-butter charms, only amplify them. Bread-and-butter charms are often the lower essence workhorse charms that drive your set. They\u2019re things that you\u2019ll be using on every attack or every other attack from essence 1 to Essence 5. They\u2019re things such as your Excellent Strike or some basic damage enhancing charms.<br /> <br /> If you want example of what I mean, let\u2019s do an experiment and say every single non-ranged weapon in Arms is a Reaper Daiklave, have all their published evocations unlocked, and had Single Point. Gnomon would give you some additional options to attack, but wouldn\u2019t let you hit overly harder than Single Point already does with its native charms. Forgotten Blade would let you gain some new tricks, but doesn\u2019t outright replace your core combat set. Even if we brought back the leak version of evocations with their greatly expanded set it still does not replace the workhorse charms. At most you\u2019ll probably be getting something like one, maybe two more.<br /> <br /> This doesn\u2019t even account for the major factor that you can only use evocations on styles that have weapons in the first place. If you are using your style unarmed then you are at a significant disadvantage compared to Lunars. After all, for Lunars such charms can be \u2018evocations\u2019 to their primary combat set, for Solars it must be the other way around.<br /> <br /> I use the phrase \u201cMartial Arts are evocations for Lunars\u201d a bit loosely, as some people may think they\u2019re the same but only in a minor bit. Yes, an artifact ranked at 4 and MA are probably going to have the same amount of charms. But this has several flaws: The weapon and Lunars not needing weapons as much.<br /> <br /> The thing that binds the artifact is the weapon itself. The evocations are powerful but the effects are tightly controlled. For example, look at Flying Silver Dream. It can use melee charms but has to jump through significant hoops to do this. Its balanced around this as its set is largely closed or offers power orthogonal to the native charms (That is, increasing the power of the character but in a different path than the character\u2019s native material).<br /> <br /> Doing this with MA\u2019s, as discussed, spoils the tightly considered balance. As discussed before we do have issues with combining bread-and-butter native charms with MA\u2019s. But what we also have is the weapon itself: Lunars can use martial arts unarmed without caring overly much. Why would they? Their native charms allow compatibility with unarmed! This means that a style is Unarmed only and No armour allows a Lunar to treat it as a \u2018set of evocations\u2019 with potent charms inside of it while Mastery units who want to use it as a core combat set either need to have the style be very powerful to match such an offset or take another MA style... which has all of the issues I mentioned previously attached to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Sidereals! </div> </div> </div>I do not give the remotest crap about a splat that\u2019s not only not made yet, but also plagued with unending speculation and what-ifs. I am going to review the product when I see the finished form in front of my face and nothing more. Or maybe a playtest if I have time some day and find an open spot.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Conclusion</span></b><br /> <br /> So yes, this has been the summary of my thoughts for the day. Maybe the newer MA\u2019s won\u2019t have this problem even if we\u2019ll have an unending balance problem of factoring in Lunar charms? It's one of the harder ways, but only time will tell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 02-23-2019, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T23:41:24-08:00","id":1291020,"title":"","content":"I mean maybe just have them count as terrestrials for MA? Would that solve the problem?<br /> <br /> Also, this is going to be fun to read when Sidereals comes out. I'd really need to read lunars more carefully but I do trust your judgement. It seems like only specific charms should be allowed to combo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-23-2019, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T23:56:59-08:00","id":1291021,"title":"","content":"I like it. It's just less hassle than having two sets of different charms that can't be combined. And they cost more, and they're weaker than for Solars.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say I don't see the point here. You probably can build some brutal combos. (But then, offensively, you can do that with MA anyway).<br /> <br /> And certainly, many styles have specific weaknesses built in. Though when that weakness is defence... well, a Single Point stylist can't combo it with Melee, but they can just use Dodge, or Resistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T00:28:39-08:00","id":1291024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291021#post1291021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. It's just less hassle than having two sets of different charms that can't be combined. And they cost more, and they're weaker than for Solars.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say I don't see the point here. You probably can build some brutal combos. (But then, offensively, you can do that with MA anyway).<br /> <br /> And certainly, many styles have specific weaknesses built in. Though when that weakness is defence... well, a Single Point stylist can't combo it with Melee, but they can just use Dodge, or Resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here here!<br /> <br /> My sentiments exactly, it seemed like a pipe dream when people tossed the idea of letting Lunars build off of something like Snake Style natively way back when we only had the 3rd ed core. I\u2019m curious to see how this play out. I was always fond of making Lunars viable Martial Arts Masters, and Solars still have their Mastery, and Sidereals will have their Sutras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T00:34:43-08:00","id":1291025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291021#post1291021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. It's just less hassle than having two sets of different charms that can't be combined. And they cost more, and they're weaker than for Solars.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say I don't see the point here. You probably can build some brutal combos. (But then, offensively, you can do that with MA anyway).<br /> <br /> And certainly, many styles have specific weaknesses built in. Though when that weakness is defence... well, a Single Point stylist can't combo it with Melee, but they can just use Dodge, or Resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still going through the charms but lunars have charms that aren't worse than solars and in some cases better than them in certain situations. We still haven't seen the full charmset. The real issue is just how easy a lunar can get his own native charms and combine them which I can see as a problem because a solar doesn't exactly get that luxury offensively.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T00:46:39-08:00","id":1291028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291020#post1291020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean maybe just have them count as terrestrials for MA? Would that solve the problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would believe that would be an extreme solution to the problem. It would make martial arts very weak for Lunars. Outside of a few handful handful of charms (Crane form) then there's not much of reason to spec into martial arts at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291020#post1291020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, this is going to be fun to read when Sidereals comes out. I'd really need to read lunars more carefully but I do trust your judgement. It seems like only specific charms should be allowed to combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that the Lunar charms in themselves are fine on Lunars. They probably break when interacting with some animals but lets not kid ourselves and pretend this was ever not going to be the case. The problem comes with introducing some problematic Lunar charms to MA's and visa versa. The MA's in Dragonblooded were not only more refined, but probably made with more seamless cross compatibility in mind.<br /> <br /> Locking specific charms would help, but we'd have issues. For example: How do we make interesting parry enhancements to Crane? I damn well tried but I'm not egotistical enough to claim my way is the only one, but even with Golden Tiger Stance means Crane becomes insufferable. Hell, ignoring half of penalties makes it already amazingly good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291021#post1291021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. It's just less hassle than having two sets of different charms that can't be combined. And they cost more, and they're weaker than for Solars.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say I don't see the point here. You probably can build some brutal combos. (But then, offensively, you can do that with MA anyway).<br /> <br /> And certainly, many styles have specific weaknesses built in. Though when that weakness is defence... well, a Single Point stylist can't combo it with Melee, but they can just use Dodge, or Resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually as a side note Single Point is so bad at defense you could simply just ditch using defend with Single Point and use Melee's defense tree. But we still have the issue of needing to pay for a second ability.<br /> <br /> Dodge and Resistance and usually omni-applicable for MA's, but that was almost always made with the intent in mind. Even Brawl greatly welcomes Dodge as it does a much job at defending than Brawl parry does (It has a few tricks but Defense Melee or Dodge it ain't). Resistance almost always has been the holy grail of dedicated martial arts users who are forbidden to wear armour and don't have many options existing in their native styles.<br /> <br /> I have no issue with these. But rather its the styles that rely on parry defense that get somewhat shafted by the far more efficient native cousins. A Lunar with Revolving Crescent Defense is likely only going to pop that charm after being attacked once or twice, as its a method to negate onslaught penalties without needing to jump through hoops and provides a hefty buff on top of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T00:49:43-08:00","id":1291030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291025#post1291025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still going through the charms but lunars have charms that aren't worse than solars and in some cases better than them in certain situations. We still haven't seen the full charmset. The real issue is just how easy a lunar can get his own native charms and combine them which I can see as a problem because a solar doesn't exactly get that luxury offensively.</div> </div> </div> </div>And defensively in terms of styles that rely on parry.<br /> <br /> With Single Point you're most likely going to need to use Dodge. Gathering Light Concentration is more useful in niche circumstances (Especially with the mastery). Lunars have absolutely no issue whatsoever and can treat Single Point as if it were their melee skill in terms of defense. They don't need the extra investment of another ability score.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:08:49-08:00","id":1291033,"title":"","content":"Hmm... okay, Sandact, context. My main game is MA focused: we're all Solars who got called together originally for a Martial Arts tournament, and everyone has a different style. Thus I have some MA knowledge, but MA vs non MA is less my area. I'm no balance-head, I can't engage on all the points you've shown here, but I've a couple of reactions based on stuff I've seen/know<br /> <br /> <b>Crane</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crane now has access to onslaught and other penalty negators. This now makes it one of the most aggravating styles to fight in the game. The one flaw a mastery stylist of Crane style had, that is piling on onslaught, is now virtually negated. You are now pounding your fists against a 10 defense wall that causes your ST or player to rip their notes in two. </div> </div> </div>This was already a problem. If you want a really annoying defence, Crane/White Reaper can provide thanks to Revolving Crescent Defence (with Mastery, a trick Lunars lack). Yeah, you have to sink more dots into using multiple styles, but anyone who wants to optimize won't think twice about doing that. It also provides more damage boost options with Halos and keying to a high Strength. I'd argue the Crane/Reaper has it easier than a Lunar, who needs to spread out across two native charmset trees to get that stuff while the dual stylist has it nice and compact within the WR subsystem<br /> <br /> <b>Righteous Devil</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It means if we ever have a range extender Lunars can now attack medium or longer range virtually all the time. </div> </div> </div>Erm.... RD already <i>has </i>a Range Extender. Blossom of Inevitable Demise. It's the first charm in the style and that effect's not Mastery-Locked. So guess you can ring the alarm bells on that one. The big hits Mastery gives the style are Cloud of Ebon Devils no longer being able to set you up for an Alpha Strike turn one (which'd let you activate the form reflexively) and Kiss of the Sun Concentration getting a debuff. (which is obviated for a master by Phoenix Flies still usually being about as strong). The real hit to the style IMO is the Terrestrial keyword, there's a couple of other Mastery bits but it's Terrestrial that's the big downgrade. I guess Lunar damage boosters could help, but the style already has those: the crazy big hit possibilities you're speculating about seem like they'll drain you pretty fast.<br /> <br /> (Also the sodding Form <i>never</i> works for me, to the point of it almost being a running gag. :P Not being able to combo presence charms into it hurts.)<br /> <br /> <b>Dreaming Pearl</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of my attacks now have short range? For the rest of the scene? With the only downside being using a Fan/ribbon as my potential non-unarmed weapon forever and capable of being buffed by my native charms? Mm! Yes please! </div> </div> </div>Okay, this style hasn't been used much in our game. (though it did cause me a headache briefly) That said I don't get why boosting damage on it is a big deal? The short range weapons stats are locked into mundane: boosting it up will help, but those boost charms could hit an artifact weapon just as easily. Does raw damage really do that much for the DPC?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I am kinda disappointed that Nightengale is not something you noted. Like, IDK if it's more balanced or you just didn't pick it as an example, but I really wish the style that used to be created by a Lunar was good for Lunars to use. As is the lack of Mastery makes it (at a glance) less compelling<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:11:16-08:00","id":1291035,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty weak in theory crafting, but from an &quot;actual play&quot; experience- <b>how much</b> of this will actually matter, at the table with your friends? are we making a storm in a teacup here?<br /> <br /> My Single Point-er also grapples and uses firewands. My ISoB/Melee Sorcerer is unoptimized as fuck. My Zenith Athletics supernal (lol insane rush charms) asked to use a <i>different white wolf splatbook</i> because Ex3 charms are too time consuming and and the combat takes too long for him to actually get the nitty gritty. My Archery-Craft Twilight has made a total of 3 things in 10 sessions because the craft rules are needlessly complicated. <br /> <br /> I don't mean to speak for the entire fandom, but Exalted is simply too much game for us and there's so much going on that honestly, if you doubled your attack pools and killed the Battlegroup in 2 turns instead of 4 while the rest of the Circle is trying to overcome the BBEG's broken ass basic 10 charms in Ride/Melee defense it probably will never matter. <br /> <br /> I love Exalted so much. It's such a goddamn nightmare to play mechanically. Seriously, <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/1z0kMqP.png\" target=\"_blank\">Look At This Chart</a>. If it's broken to increase a step there somewhere, its barely going to affect me because the system to insane. I barely even use Battlegroup rules instead of just giving them a number of bodies equal to HP because why the fuck is a common enemy type spread over 3 pages of rules and more than 5 metrics of crunch. <br /> <br /> I dunno, maybe its me. I love the setting of Exalted and the power scope but it's all too much to make workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:17:42-08:00","id":1291038,"title":"","content":"Because they can't use Martial Arts charms while in a non-human shape. The inability to combine them with their native charmset (which is based on Attributes) would basically make Martial Arts useless and counter-productive to Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:33:26-08:00","id":1291043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291035#post1291035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty weak in theory crafting, but from an &quot;actual play&quot; experience- <b>how much</b> of this will actually matter, at the table with your friends? are we making a storm in a teacup here?</div> </div> </div> </div>For most people, no. But I can see Sandact6's point that some power-gamers will look for brutal overpowered combos, etc, and they shouldn't really be available.<br /> <br /> Also, something else to add, Sandact6:<br /> Martial Arts is supposed to be powerful because you can combine different styles. That's why it needs a 4-dot merit and you have to buy each Style's ability seperately (and... you can buy it with Solar/Lunar/Dragon XP because the designers were worried that it wouldn't be considered powerful enough? Umm...).<br /> Of course, at the beginning you can't really combo a lot, but over time you can pick up a second or third style, and then combo them.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar takes a single Martial Art and doesn't combo it... it's kind of weak. They're buying a 4-dot merit so they can buy an Ability that doesn't combo with being an animal (I can use my Snake Style 5 to punch people, but when I'm sneaking about as a Viper, I'm limited by my Brawl, which is only 3).<br /> <br /> And then the charms themselves are both more expensive and weaker than they would be for a Solar.<br /> Not to mention, of course, that unlike a Dawn, you can only start with about 3 charms from 1 style. Out of 15 combat charms, that's pretty insignificant. So you need to have some other applicable combat charms.<br /> <br /> So, in a sense, the fact that Lunars become powerful martial arts when comboing is a feature, not a bug. It's the only way they can approach Solar competency.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say you can't find some broken combinations, because you can, but generally speaking I think it's better than not letting them combo.<br /> <br /> Of course, like the Solar comboing, this will become more powerful over time. But Solars become more powerful over time at a pretty quick rate, in terms of the power of their high-essence charms, so again... shrug?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean to speak for the entire fandom, but Exalted is simply too much game for us and there's so much going on that honestly,</div> </div> </div> </div>This is partly why I like that Lunars can simply combine Martial Arts and Dex, so you don't have to go &quot;hmmm, I can use my Martial Arts charms to attack or my Dex charms, and then to Parry I can use Martial Arts charms or Dex charms, and if I use these three charms I can't use those two...&quot;<br /> With Solar Martial Artists, combining with Melee or Brawl can be powerful, but is mechanically quite fiddly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I barely even use Battlegroup rules instead of just giving them a number of bodies equal to HP because why the fuck is a common enemy type spread over 3 pages of rules and more than 5 metrics of crunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually ran battle groups a lot when I was running it, because I found them simpler to run than regular NPCs.<br /> Or rather, I'd generally have a battle group and 1-2 normal NPCs together. I found that worked well.<br /> <br /> They're a bit of a hassle to calculate the stats for, but I used this tool: <a href=\"https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-battle-groups/\" target=\"_blank\">https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-battle-groups/</a><br /> It even lets you adjust the size down as you go and re-calculates all the stats for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T02:25:44-08:00","id":1291050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291033#post1291033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Crane</b><br /> <br /> <br /> This was already a problem. If you want a really annoying defence, Crane/White Reaper can provide thanks to Revolving Crescent Defence (with Mastery, a trick Lunars lack). Yeah, you have to sink more dots into using multiple styles, but anyone who wants to optimize won't think twice about doing that. It also provides more damage boost options with Halos and keying to a high Strength. I'd argue the Crane/Reaper has it easier than a Lunar, who needs to spread out across two native charmset trees to get that stuff while the dual stylist has it nice and compact within the WR subsystem</div> </div> </div> </div>Revolving Crescent comes with a weakness: It only lasts next turn until mastery. Otherwise on Lunars its more of a last ditch effort. You'd need to use the parry unarmed (Because Crane and White reaper have no other cross compatible weapons) and reflect the attack using the to turn an attack back on an opponent. On the other hand I've seen some ST's refuse such things under the logic being &quot;You didn't parry with the fan, therefore it doesn't count&quot;. This means that you're probably going to be using White Reaper charms for offense too. This works but is gonna be expensive after a while.<br /> <br /> Crane/Reaper has some benefits, mainly some offense Crane requires if you lack a fan. But as mentioned in my original post Lunars have this cheaper. Why waste the XP buying another ability up to 5 when I can just buy some charms? Willpower? Attributes? By the time I buy several charms I can cover most of the things I'm probably lacking in my original style. I mean accuracy sure as hell won't be an issue anymore.<br /> <br /> Revolving Crescent is good if you're a Solar... but it lags off a bit as a Lunar. The power of the charm is instant. You can use its full power without needing to jump through hoops and you get a large power boost to defense. Otherwise you might stick to your native charms as that 4m 1i tag kind of adds up when spamming it in response to all attacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291033#post1291033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Righteous Devil</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Erm.... RD already <i>has </i>a Range Extender. Blossom of Inevitable Demise. It's the first charm in the style and that effect's not Mastery-Locked. So guess you can ring the alarm bells on that one. The big hits Mastery gives the style are Cloud of Ebon Devils no longer being able to set you up for an Alpha Strike turn one (which'd let you activate the form reflexively) and Kiss of the Sun Concentration getting a debuff. (which is obviated for a master by Phoenix Flies still usually being about as strong). The real hit to the style IMO is the Terrestrial keyword, there's a couple of other Mastery bits but it's Terrestrial that's the big downgrade. I guess Lunar damage boosters could help, but the style already has those: the crazy big hit possibilities you're speculating about seem like they'll drain you pretty fast.<br /> <br /> (Also the sodding Form <i>never</i> works for me, to the point of it almost being a running gag. :P Not being able to combo presence charms into it hurts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Dread Tiger's Symmetry is a permanent charm that works on all intimidation rolls. It helps.<br /> <br /> I forgot about Blossom's dual keyword truth be told. I read the text earlier today and assumed it just fueled decisive attacks. The fact it can do such a thing at such a range makes me sigh even in more disbelief for how strong the style is.<br /> <br /> Lowering an enemy's defense is useful, but against the highest defense opponents (Crane) you'll be welcoming all the accuracy you can get.<br /> <br /> Also its probably going to be compatible with Lunar damage enhancement charms, or at least a solid chunk of them. This style already has one of the highest offensive ratings in the game, why does it need this? I mean there's Sekhem, but that comes its own heap of downsides.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291033#post1291033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dreaming Pearl</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, this style hasn't been used much in our game. (though it did cause me a headache briefly) That said I don't get why boosting damage on it is a big deal? The short range weapons stats are locked into mundane: boosting it up will help, but those boost charms could hit an artifact weapon just as easily. Does raw damage really do that much for the DPC?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding your accuracy to damage is pretty spiffy considering its cost, but that's not the issue. For me its the form. Making all of your attacks short range for the rest of the scene? While making them light artifacts? That you combine with all your native charms?<br /> <br /> DPC seemingly has some interactions but it doesn't have many. Crane shares a form weapon but is armour banned so you can't use DPC's armour charm (ST might let you do the soak boost though), but even if you get past that Crane style is utterly addicted to its form counterattacks. You could bounce back a decisive counterattack, but I don't see why a Lunar wouldn't simply grab their native counterattack charm along with several defense charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291033#post1291033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I am kinda disappointed that Nightengale is not something you noted. Like, IDK if it's more balanced or you just didn't pick it as an example, but I really wish the style that used to be created by a Lunar was good for Lunars to use. As is the lack of Mastery makes it (at a glance) less compelling</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because it didn't have problems I mentioned that affect all the styles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291035#post1291035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty weak in theory crafting, but from an &quot;actual play&quot; experience- <b>how much</b> of this will actually matter, at the table with your friends? are we making a storm in a teacup here?</div> </div> </div> </div>That honestly completely depends on the people at the table.<br /> <br /> Are there going to be people who don't notice or care such a thing.<br /> <br /> Then there's going to be people like me who feel punched in the dick for not picking a Lunar when I want to martial arts, despite how much a Snake girl snake stylist would be fun to play.<br /> <br /> I'm also not going to deny Ex3 is a crunchy game. The Exalted series has always been a crunchy game. If you find it too difficult for yourself and your group then look up replacement systems. Fate Core can run Exalted just fine with some modification (Atomic Robo rules especially help), Chuubo, Godbound, there's options out there for people who haven't memorized the majority of the corebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291038#post1291038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they can't use Martial Arts charms while in a non-human shape. The inability to combine them with their native charmset (which is based on Attributes) would basically make Martial Arts useless and counter-productive to Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>And do we allow the complete opposite by opening the floodgates to all the charms? Despite how much conflict there is in the styles? Despite how it makes other splats feel like chumps?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T02:49:07-08:00","id":1291053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291035#post1291035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty weak in theory crafting, but from an &quot;actual play&quot; experience- <b>how much</b> of this will actually matter, at the table with your friends? are we making a storm in a teacup here?<br /> <br /> My Single Point-er also grapples and uses firewands. My ISoB/Melee Sorcerer is unoptimized as fuck. My Zenith Athletics supernal (lol insane rush charms) asked to use a <i>different white wolf splatbook</i> because Ex3 charms are too time consuming and and the combat takes too long for him to actually get the nitty gritty. My Archery-Craft Twilight has made a total of 3 things in 10 sessions because the craft rules are needlessly complicated.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to speak for the entire fandom, but Exalted is simply too much game for us and there's so much going on that honestly, if you doubled your attack pools and killed the Battlegroup in 2 turns instead of 4 while the rest of the Circle is trying to overcome the BBEG's broken ass basic 10 charms in Ride/Melee defense it probably will never matter.<br /> <br /> I love Exalted so much. It's such a goddamn nightmare to play mechanically. Seriously, <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/1z0kMqP.png\" target=\"_blank\">Look At This Chart</a>. If it's broken to increase a step there somewhere, its barely going to affect me because the system to insane. I barely even use Battlegroup rules instead of just giving them a number of bodies equal to HP because why the fuck is a common enemy type spread over 3 pages of rules and more than 5 metrics of crunch.<br /> <br /> I dunno, maybe its me. I love the setting of Exalted and the power scope but it's all too much to make workable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual mechanical change that the developers need to do is change a single line saying that &quot;you can combine native charms with MA&quot; to &quot;you cannot combine native charms with MA&quot;, which might be the least work any balancing change has ever needed. If your group doesn't like the mechanics and ignores them, that doesn't mean the mechanics should be made bad or not balanced just because you won't interact with them, because a lot of us out here have spent several years exploring every last niche of this system we love and want it to be in the best possible state it can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:06:23-08:00","id":1291054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291050#post1291050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revolving Crescent comes with a weakness: It only lasts next turn until mastery. Otherwise on Lunars its more of a last ditch effort. You'd need to use the parry unarmed (Because Crane and White reaper have no other cross compatible weapons) and reflect the attack using the to turn an attack back on an opponent. On the other hand I've seen some ST's refuse such things under the logic being &quot;You didn't parry with the fan, therefore it doesn't count&quot;. This means that you're probably going to be using White Reaper charms for offense too. This works but is gonna be expensive after a while.<br /> <br /> Crane/Reaper has some benefits, mainly some offense Crane requires if you lack a fan. But as mentioned in my original post Lunars have this cheaper. Why waste the XP buying another ability up to 5 when I can just buy some charms? Willpower? Attributes? By the time I buy several charms I can cover most of the things I'm probably lacking in my original style. I mean accuracy sure as hell won't be an issue anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm. Hard to give a certian evaluation without strength, but my starting one is 'Reaper is comprehensive and stronger'. Plus you need less of it: take Crane up to Form you've got most of its defensive tricks online and you can focus on Reaper. It'd take a Lunar stylist a lot more than a few charms to get a defense package as comprehensive as Crane up to form, I'm gonna guess it'd take most of the tree to approximate Reaper. <br /> <br /> I guess that's my point here. I'm not seeing much a Lunar could do that a Solar with the right style combination couldn't do. Sure, that Solar's had a mildly less efficient way to get there, but he's going to get possibilities with a second style that a Lunar won't have similarly easy access to with their native charms. The benefits Lunars can gain from combos at this point sound akin to an alternate mastery in the main to me. Useful, yes, potentially big... but not game breakingly amazing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dread Tiger's Symmetry is a permanent charm that works on all intimidation rolls. It helps. </div> </div> </div>Have it. Still keep losing. :P I blame Intimacies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I forgot about Blossom's dual keyword truth be told. I read the text earlier today and assumed it just fueled decisive attacks. The fact it can do such a thing at such a range makes me sigh even in more disbelief for how strong the style is. </div> </div> </div>Hey, don't sigh at <i>that</i>. Sigh at the wonderful craziness of a Lunar using Burning Judgement Halo and then shifting to Tyrant Lizard next turn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> AFAICT that won't end the effect, since Halo is instant and has very specific end conditions<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lowering an enemy's defense is useful, but against the highest defense opponents (Crane) you'll be welcoming all the accuracy you can get.<br /> <br /> Also its probably going to be compatible with Lunar damage enhancement charms, or at least a solid chunk of them. This style already has one of the highest offensive ratings in the game, why does it need this? I mean there's Sekhem, but that comes its own heap of downsides. </div> </div> </div>Why <i>does </i>it need that? The style's already damage intensive as it is. Sure, more is better in abstract, but there's a diminishing returns factor here: how many damage boosters do you need when you have Azure Abacus anyway? (plus a ST could make a pretty good argument that it's not compatible with Strength charms since a firewand doesn't use Strength in its damage calculations. You could then maybe use them if you went to melee with the style, but that's a different bundle of worms.)<br /> <br /> Accuracy IMO is probably the style's biggest stumbling block. Yeah, it's got the aims from Form, but even with that it's a mote intensive style and that makes relying on the Excellency for accuracy wretch. Lunars legitimately have some advantages here, but they're not clear cut enough to make me think they've got a significant upper hand. What a Lunar stylist invests into Acc boosts, I can throw into alternate trees like Sorcery or Resistence. I don't think there's anything Lunarshave that is clear cut good enough to make me regret going Solar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Adding your accuracy to damage is pretty spiffy considering its cost, but that's not the issue. For me its the form. Making all of your attacks short range for the rest of the scene? While making them light artifacts? That you combine with all your native charms?<br /> <br /> DPC seemingly has some interactions but it doesn't have many. Crane shares a form weapon but is armour banned so you can't use DPC's armour charm (ST might let you do the soak boost though), but even if you get past that Crane style is utterly addicted to its form counterattacks. You could bounce back a decisive counterattack, but I don't see why a Lunar wouldn't simply grab their native counterattack charm along with several defense charms. </div> </div> </div>Bowing out here: I do not know DPC well enough to comment.(I didn't even remember that the form gave the artifact weapon traits)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's because it didn't have problems I mentioned that affect all the styles. </div> </div> </div>I figured. :P Just kinda depressed that it's not a great style for Lunars and wanted to half-jokingly moan a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:13:48-08:00","id":1291055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291053#post1291053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The actual mechanical change that the developers need to do is change a single line saying that &quot;you can combine native charms with MA&quot; to &quot;you cannot combine native charms with MA&quot;, which might be the least work any balancing change has ever needed. If your group doesn't like the mechanics and ignores them, that doesn't mean the mechanics should be made bad or not balanced just because you won't interact with them, because a lot of us out here have spent several years exploring every last niche of this system we love and want it to be in the best possible state it can be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that line would outright kill Lunar MA since why go spec into something when you don't get mastery and can't favored. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:19:59-08:00","id":1291056,"title":"","content":"Yeah, without that there's nothing good about Lunar MA. You don't get Mastery, it can't be Favoured, it can't be Supernal, it can't be used with animal forms, and without this you couldn't even combo it with Evasion or Soak-boosting charms (which Solars can).<br /> <br /> Solars have some hefty advantages with MA. Lunars have some different hefty advantages with MA. That seems fair to me, but not the same (same would be boring).<br /> <br /> I'm willing to accept that comboing them may, perhaps, be broken. But if it is, then you'd need to give them some other stuff to make it a viable combat build.<br /> <br /> (I saw 2nd ed Solars take MA a lot, but I only saw it taken once with a Lunar and it wasn't that good. Most Lunar &quot;martial artists&quot; just used regular charms and fists or a staff.)<br /> <br /> But I believe that the devs weren't sure whether to do this or not, and found in playtesting that it was actually okay.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:26:54-08:00","id":1291061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact62</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there's going to be people like me who feel punched in the dick for not picking a Lunar when I want to martial arts, despite how much a Snake girl snake stylist would be fun to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then... play that? That's literally the character I'm playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:27:50-08:00","id":1291063,"title":"","content":"Confession of bias here: I did play a Lunar who used MA back in 2E. I don't think she ever got charms in it: instead she combo'd MA for defence and Defend Other-ing with archery and a big essence cannon for her primary attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:34:17-08:00","id":1291065,"title":"","content":"Mastery stacking is also something that happens very quickly and a lot of MA charms have a big difference in their effect if you have Mastery or not which can be a huge thing and a Solar MA supernal will have no problem being able to stack those effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:38:47-08:00","id":1291066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291055#post1291055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that line would outright kill Lunar MA since why go spec into something when you don't get mastery and can't favored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kill it? Would it really? The intention of Martial Arts balance was always that Mastery was about on-par with solar combat ability, that non-mastery non-terrestrial was on par with celestial combat ability, and terrestrial was on par with dragonblooded combat ability. When people here talk about making lunar MA &quot;viable&quot; what you're really trying to say is &quot;as good as solars&quot;. Well, sorry, this is Exalted and different splats are on explicitly different levels of power and lunars are very firmly weaker than the solars are, and shouldn't get mechanical concessions to &quot;fix&quot; this problem. If lunar animal-shaping is so immensely powerful that non-mastery MA without native charms doesnt even come close, that's a sign that the balance there is screwed up, not that they should be made stronger than solars at MA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:42:32-08:00","id":1291068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291063#post1291063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Confession of bias here: I did play a Lunar who used MA back in 2E. I don't think she ever got charms in it: instead she combo'd MA for defence and Defend Other-ing with archery and a big essence cannon for her primary attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, almost every Lunar had the MA ability, for being ananimal. About 75% favoured it. But I only saw 1 guy (whose concept was Tiger-totem Tiger stylist) actually end up buying charms.<br /> The builds I mostly saw were soak-regen, pseudo-Solar dodge or sometimes octo-spam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:51:42-08:00","id":1291073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291068#post1291068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, almost every Lunar had the MA ability, for being ananimal. About 75% favoured it. But I only saw 1 guy (whose concept was Tiger-totem Tiger stylist) actually end up buying charms.<br /> The builds I mostly saw were soak-regen, pseudo-Solar dodge or sometimes octo-spam.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean I bought Infernal Hero, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan and, if it counts, Lunar Hero Style charms for nothing? And Babar's comedy use of Currents Sweep to Sea meant nothing to you? Sadness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm willing to accept that comboing them may, perhaps, be broken. But if it is, then you'd need to give them some other stuff to make it a viable combat build. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why they let Dragonblood combo their native charms with MA after all. Wait...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:54:15-08:00","id":1291075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291066#post1291066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kill it? Would it really? The intention of Martial Arts balance was always that Mastery was about on-par with solar combat ability, that non-mastery non-terrestrial was on par with celestial combat ability, and terrestrial was on par with dragonblooded combat ability. When people here talk about making lunar MA &quot;viable&quot; what you're really trying to say is &quot;as good as solars&quot;. Well, sorry, this is Exalted and different splats are on explicitly different levels of power and lunars are very firmly weaker than the solars are, and shouldn't get mechanical concessions to &quot;fix&quot; this problem. If lunar animal-shaping is so immensely powerful that non-mastery MA without native charms doesnt even come close, that's a sign that the balance there is screwed up, not that they should be made stronger than solars at MA.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that light, look at the Mastery keyword again. Most of the time it provides edge case benefits. There's some uses of it that are very powerful, but usually there isn't <i>that </i>much of a gap between mastery and non mastery. Just as there shouldn't be much of a gap between Celestial Exalted. We can keep the shiny self important such and suches at the top of the heap while leaving mixed games viable, rather than everyone bowing down to the Shiny Ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:57:49-08:00","id":1291077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291066#post1291066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kill it? Would it really? The intention of Martial Arts balance was always that Mastery was about on-par with solar combat ability, that non-mastery non-terrestrial was on par with celestial combat ability, and terrestrial was on par with dragonblooded combat ability. When people here talk about making lunar MA &quot;viable&quot; what you're really trying to say is &quot;as good as solars&quot;. Well, sorry, this is Exalted and different splats are on explicitly different levels of power and lunars are very firmly weaker than the solars are, and shouldn't get mechanical concessions to &quot;fix&quot; this problem. If lunar animal-shaping is so immensely powerful that non-mastery MA without native charms doesnt even come close, that's a sign that the balance there is screwed up, not that they should be made stronger than solars at MA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that is very toxic statement that no Exalt should ever be near as good as a solar charm by charm <br /> and they aren't a solar has much stronger toolkit overall than any exalt. <br /> Non mastery MA is still weaker than Mastery and Mastery effects have been proven being able to outright break the game over and over by Lumi on the Exalted Discord. <br /> A Lunar will never be near that level even if they can combine Naitive and MA since Mastery is that good <br /> <br /> <br /> I will also quote Kelly Pedersen from another thread about Powerlevel <br /> &quot;I think it's important to remember that the &quot;power levels&quot; of various types of Exalts are, in 3e, being considered <i>holistically</i>, rather than charm-by-charm. That means that looking at a single charm and comparing it to the equivalent in another charmset isn't really a useful metric any more. What matters is whether the whole charmset, when considered together, is more powerful. Which means Lunars can legitimately have charms that are more powerful than Solar equivalents, as long as, for instance, a Solar specialized in Melee or Brawl has a pretty good chance of beating a Lunar similarly specialized into Dex or Str. While we obviously haven't seen all of the Lunar charms yet, I think that's still the way things are heading. An equal-Essence Lunar with similar investment in combat charms will give a Melee-Supernal Solar a good fight, but I'm still going to bet on the Solar.&quot; <br /> <br /> Which a Solar supernal Martial art have with Mastery effects that stacks with each other and good toolkits both in resistance, Dodge and Athletic <br /> <br /> But why would I go Lunar Martial art if I have no mastery, I can never favor it. Can't combo it with anything except themselves which is a bigger investment than any Solar will ever have to do. Take much longer since E1 and no supernal. Can't use in animal form <br /> Seems very lackluster to me to even glance an eye to pick Martial art as a Lunar when I have faster progression without it. <br /> A Martial art Lunar that can't combo Martial art will probably be the most dull thing ever with the small amount of offensive charm that can be taken compared to a Dragonblooded that start at E2 and have a faster progression to other Martial art without gimping themselves or a Supernal Solar that will Jumpstart in any Martial art so they can go over to the next one directly out of the gate and start break the game with Mastery effects upon mastery effects<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:15:48-08:00","id":1291078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291075#post1291075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that light, look at the Mastery keyword again. Most of the time it provides edge case benefits. There's some uses of it that are very powerful, but usually there isn't <i>that </i>much of a gap between mastery and non mastery. Just as there shouldn't be much of a gap between Celestial Exalted. We can keep the shiny self important such and suches at the top of the heap while leaving mixed games viable, rather than everyone bowing down to the Shiny Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what is it then? Is Mastery something so good that it's better than applying Excellent Strike, Excellent Strike 2 and Rising Moon Slash, along with the numerous other very powerful native lunar charms to MA attacks? Or is it so little that clearly lunars were always intended to be just a teensy bit weaker than Dawns, and therefore don't need their native charms here? Make your mind up! The answer, though, is in the lore - the solars are stronger than lunars are. Specifically, stronger enough to such a degree that they defined the era they lived in, and their loss permanently and significantly diminished the world. Not just Twilights with their Solar Circle Sorcery, but those big dumb Dawns too!<br /> <br /> For some reason combat ability is the part that solar-haters can never cope with. It's fine if they get a literal circle of sorcery that is exclusive to them, and are the only ones that can make N/A artifice, but you apply a similar distinction in power to combat and it's suddenly a big problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:19:12-08:00","id":1291079,"title":"","content":"maybe because combat is the only thing that activly kills your character straight off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:19:20-08:00","id":1291080,"title":"","content":"Ignoring Evocations for a moment, the Solar needs to invest in another ability to substitute it in when confronted by one of the style's shortcomings.<br /> However, they do pay 1 less xp per MA dot and 2xp less per charm. So it's more a question of how effectively the most appropriate secondary ability papers the style's holes vs. the Lunar charmset and we still don't have a complete picture there for every style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:22:47-08:00","id":1291081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291073#post1291073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean I bought Infernal Hero, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan and, if it counts, Lunar Hero Style charms for nothing? And Babar's comedy use of Currents Sweep to Sea meant nothing to you? Sadness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in 2nd ed (so before you bought Dreaming Pearl; but I didn't know you bought Lunar Hero). But you're right, how could I forget that you bought the first charm of Infernal Monster! There was that great scene where Timid went bonkers on a boat and hopped between boats killing people. (I think they may have actually been bad guys, rather than, say, old servants or something.) Did she ever use that charm again?<br /> <br /> In my defence, Currents Sweep to Sea was rubbish every time, so it's reasonable I forgot about it.<br /> <br /> Oh, I just remembered.<br /> If Lunars couldn't combo Dex charms with Martial Arts charm, they wouldn't even be able to use an excellency to attack. Whereas Solars of course, get to use their Martial Arts excellency.<br /> So it'd be quite difficult to hit people using Dodge or Melee excellencies with your Dreaming Pearl charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fodor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, that's why they let Dragonblood combo their native charms with MA after all. Wait...</div> </div> </div> </div>They can combo with Dodge. And Resistance. And... the first charm of Brawl! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But anyhow, taking Martial Arts is a very viable combat-build for Dragonblood as-is. I don't think Dragonblood players are going &quot;hmmm... martial arts seems like a really rubbish choice.&quot; We play with a Dragonblood character who's got like 3 different styles of Martial Arts (Air Dragon, Snake and... something else, but I forget wht). And he loves mechanics (even if he sometimes has very odd ideas about mechanics), it's not like he just took them because he thought the names of the styles were cool.<br /> <br /> Saying all this, I'm not really invested in Lunars combo-ing their attack and parry charms* with Martial Arts particularly.<br /> But<br /> a)it makes the game a bit easier, and it's complex enough as-is,<br /> b)it makes sense; you roll Dex+Martial Arts, so obviously Dex and Martial Arts charms are applicable in the way that Brawl isn't, just like how you can't use Brawl charms for, say, Sailing or Crafting,<br /> c)if Martial Arts charms cost 10xp, are overall a bit weaker than Lunar charms, and require an Ability that's useless with shapeshifting, I think Lunar martial artists are not going to be very popular. People are more likely to just take Brawl and Lunar charms, because Lunar charms are cheaper, and overall a bit better.<br /> <br /> *They obviously should get to combo it with Resistance and Evasion, because everyone else does.<br /> <br /> Now, obviously I've already started playing a Snake Stylist (with a few other martial arts charms; oh man, the damage you can get on Withering by combo-ing Martial Arts charms is enormous), so, were the Devs to turn around and say &quot;nah, you can't combo MA with native charms&quot;, I'd still be playing a Martial Artist (and I'd probably just buy into more Martial Arts, rather than Lunar combat charms). So it wouldn't make me un-play a Snake stylist. And you presumably wouldn't go and ask the ST &quot;Dreaming Pearl is rubbish, can I un-buy it&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I think would make Lunar martial artists unpopular generally, and that'd be sad, because Exalted is supposed to be a game full of martial artists.<br /> <br /> There are other ways to make it a decent option though. It doesn't have to be the combo-ing. If that in particular is overpowered, maybe there's some alternative ways.<br /> <br /> I just like the ease, lack of hassle, and the concept that Solars are more straight-up powerful with MA while Lunars are more flexible (which is its own strength). So that a Solar Martial Artist and Lunar Martial Artist are both viable but different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-23-2019, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:23:44-08:00","id":1291082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291080#post1291080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring Evocations for a moment, the Solar needs to invest in another ability to substitute it in when confronted by one of the style's shortcomings.<br /> However, they do pay 1 less xp per MA dot and 2xp less per charm. So it's more a question of how effectively the most appropriate secondary ability papers the style's holes vs. the Lunar charmset and we still don't have a complete picture there for every style.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is also a combination of different abilities since you don't only attack, you either need to dodge or parry/soak those attacks which Solars still do good with few charm investment same as a Lunar will have to do in other trees in Dex/Stamina <br /> But a solar at chargen as The Wizard of Oz if I remember correctly (correct me if I am wrong) has at least 5 5s in their abilites compared to a Lunar that atleast have 1 5 in one ability and the rest is at 3 and sure that is just 1-2 in parry/Evasion but the Solar will have their attributes covered to increase the Parry/Evasion to max if needed if we go by minmaxing of course <br /> But I agree with you whole heartly even if it might not come up in my text ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:40:13-08:00","id":1291084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291078#post1291078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what is it then? Is Mastery something so good that it's better than applying Excellent Strike, Excellent Strike 2 and Rising Moon Slash, along with the numerous other very powerful native lunar charms to MA attacks? Or is it so little that clearly lunars were always intended to be just a teensy bit weaker than Dawns, and therefore don't need their native charms here? Make your mind up! The answer, though, is in the lore - the solars are stronger than lunars are. Specifically, stronger enough to such a degree that they defined the era they lived in, and their loss permanently and significantly diminished the world. Not just Twilights with their Solar Circle Sorcery, but those big dumb Dawns too!<br /> <br /> For some reason combat ability is the part that solar-haters can never cope with. It's fine if they get a literal circle of sorcery that is exclusive to them, and are the only ones that can make N/A artifice, but you apply a similar distinction in power to combat and it's suddenly a big problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm not fond of those other things too. But we were talking about Martial Arts. (And 'Solar Haters'? Really? :|)<br /> <br /> Mastery is an advantage, useful but not unbeatable. So is comboing native charms with MA, at least as far as I can tell. Most effects a Lunar can get with this, a Solar can get through either other abilities as Sandact points out. I focused on combing with other styles but Athletics, Brawl, Resistance and Dodge are all valid ways to combo and patch a MA style too. Solars can do pretty much the exact same thing Lunars can. There's a few tricks Lunars can pull that Solars can't but it does not seem like enough to flat out say 'Lunars are better at MA than Solars'. <br /> <br /> If you want to enforce your power tiering you could argue that a Lunar is too close to a Solar in what they can do, that it doesn't make Solars as clearly above the other Celestials for your take. That's fine. However I for one do not care about enforcing the tiers: so long as min max exploitative combos are kept to a minimum, I'll be happy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:40:45-08:00","id":1291085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291080#post1291080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring Evocations for a moment, the Solar needs to invest in another ability to substitute it in when confronted by one of the style's shortcomings.<br /> However, they do pay 1 less xp per MA dot and 2xp less per charm. So it's more a question of how effectively the most appropriate secondary ability papers the style's holes vs. the Lunar charmset and we still don't have a complete picture there for every style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, DEX charms are out, so we can say certain things for sure. We can say that Lunars are more accurate than solar melee with every combat ability, for one, and that this includes Martial Arts. There is no mastery effect that provides equivalent power to this. This is a problem that actually came up a long time ago, with the sidereal QC excellency - people would use it to stat up a martial artist, they pick Snake Style, and then found that this utterly broke the game because SStH became an unbeatable defence. Lunar accuracy is absurdly high, and this is the case here too. There is no mastery effect in Snake Style that is as strong as making SStH unbeatable.<br /> <br /> On XP, I don't think that having to pay a few XP extra to be massively powerful is a concern for anyone in any real game. I've played a lot of Exalted, and as the game goes along you always end up with loads of spare solar XP. I'm playing an eclipse, for instance, who has mastered a martial art, bought a large number of evocations, maxed out all her abilities + bought a few unfavoured ones, learned numerous spirit charms, and I still have a pile of unspent solar XP. The gap between a solar and lunar mastering a full MA is (assuming 9 charms like most MAs are) 18xp. Not much at all. I would trade mastery for the lunar dex charms in a heartbeat and we haven't even seen how STR breaks things even further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:46:27-08:00","id":1291086,"title":"","content":"I should probably also add something else that occurred to me.<br /> <br /> The more powerful offensive styles (Righteous Devil, Single Point) are generally the least combo-able. Sure, you can have two katanas and use Single Point/Steel Devil, but why would you bother when you can just take Dodge or Resistance... or even Melee defence charms? (Attack with Single Point, parry with Melee). And Righteous Devil can't be combo'd with any styles at all.<br /> <br /> Whereas I think the ones that are easier to combo are generally either not the most powerful offensive styles (all those unarmed styles; sure, you can build plenty of combos, but they don't include the most brutal charms generally). Or they do stuff that doesn't go together all that well; yes, Black Claw and Tiger can be combo'd, but they don't really help each other that much. And Ebon Shadow's defence is mostly about Evasion, which a Solar can use Dodge charms with anyway.<br /> <br /> So anyway, I think the ability to combo, say, Snake, with Lunar attack charms, isn't really that much better than combo-ing with other Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> (Armour-Penetrating Fang Strike, Striking Fang Technique, Eyes of the Wood Dragon, Falling Scythe Flash, Searing Edge Flash... your unarmed withering damage is 7+Strength+Strength+Perception+Dexterity, ignoring soak, and if you do even 1 damage they lose another Essence initiative. Pricy, but so brutal. I can't see that replacing one of those charms with a Lunar strength charm is going to make much difference.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, combo-ing Single Point or Righteous Devil with Lunar charms could be absolutely brutal. Normally there's no way beyond Evocations (and some of the effects in Sirrush kind of overlap with Righteous Devil. Sekhem's good though. And I guess Stormcaller, but I haven't really looked at that with Single Point).<br /> <br /> Saying that... I wouldn't be shocked if most of the Lunar damage charms in Strength are applicable to Single Point, but not to Righteous Devil. After all, you don't actually add your Strength to the damage of firewands, so it'd make sense that you couldn't apply damage-boosting Strength charms.<br /> <br /> I guess there could be a tree off Bombardier Spittle Alchemy, but that'd be in Dex.<br /> So, if you're wondering about Lunar damage charms with Firewands, I suspect it's all already there.<br /> <br /> They might have damage charms for ranged weapons in Perception, but I suspect that it's just the ones from Dex that are Totemic for the eagle-eyed. Not sure though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you can do some pretty good stuff with Dex-based ranged charms and Righteous Devil, but you've got to pay for it (as opposed to spending that XP on, say, Solar Dodge or Resistance), and you're not getting the strong Mastery effects of Cloud of Ebon Devils, Kiss of the Sun Concentration, and Caress of the 1000 Hells.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:51:56-08:00","id":1291087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291084#post1291084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I'm not fond of those other things too. But we were talking about Martial Arts. (And 'Solar Haters'? Really? :|)<br /> <br /> Mastery is an advantage, useful but not unbeatable. So is comboing native charms with MA, at least as far as I can tell. Most effects a Lunar can get with this, a Solar can get through either other abilities as Sandact points out. I focused on combing with other styles but Athletics, Brawl, Resistance and Dodge are all valid ways to combo and patch a MA style too. Solars can do pretty much the exact same thing Lunars can. There's a few tricks Lunars can pull that Solars can't but it does not seem like enough to flat out say 'Lunars are better at MA than Solars'.<br /> <br /> If you want to enforce your power tiering you could argue that a Lunar is too close to a Solar in what they can do, that it doesn't make Solars as clearly above the other Celestials for your take. That's fine. However I for one do not care about enforcing the tiers: so long as min max exploitative combos are kept to a minimum, I'll be happy</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I just posted one such exploit. Snake Strikes The Heel, when combined with an effect to increase withering accuracy, is a huge problem. This isn't something hard to do. This is something that any lunar with 3 charms can do. 3 native charms, that's all. This is not something that MA grants in any way. There is no way for a solar to do this.<br /> <br /> That is just one effect lunars can combo into MA. As Sandact ALSO pointed out, the lunar charmset is effectively, for lunars, a full MA with no restrictions. You can combo it with any MA whatsoever. Excellent Strike? Stick it on snake style, righteous devil, single point, anything you like. And again, this is only the DEX charms! Even with just these, lunar MA is capable of numerous very, very powerful things that utterly eclipse mastery effects! How much are you willing to bet that STR charms will not have anything at all that's better than mastery? Here's a free prediction: lunars will have, in STR, charms relating to grappling. These charms will, unlike solar brawl, combo with Mantis and Tiger Style. The result will be that lunars are significantly stronger with both of these styles.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;solar haters&quot;, I really mean Dawn Haters, as every Exalted community has people who can't stand that Dawns are stronger in combat than their pet splat and want to see the big mean fighter taken down a peg and solars relegated to being Wizards or Leaders or whatever nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","user":"Clownpiece","date":". 02-23-2019, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:55:09-08:00","id":1291088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291082#post1291082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is also a combination of different abilities since you don't only attack, you either need to dodge or parry/soak those attacks which Solars still do good with few charm investment same as a Lunar will have to do in other trees in Dex/Stamina<br /> But a solar at chargen as The Wizard of Oz if I remember correctly (correct me if I am wrong) has at least 5 5s in their abilites compared to a Lunar that atleast have 1 5 in one ability and the rest is at 3 and sure that is just 1-2 in parry/Evasion but the Solar will have their attributes covered to increase the Parry/Evasion to max if needed if we go by minmaxing of course</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they won't always of course. Different people build differently<br /> <br /> But a Solar<i> can</i> start with up to 7 abilities at 5, plus Dexterity 5 (it's technically possible to start with Strength and Dexterity 5, but I think hardly anyone does that, except maybe nutty white-room min-maxers).<br /> I find taking 7 abilities at 5 to be very rare, but most have a fair few. Certainly all the ones they really care about.<br /> <br /> Getting Dex 5 is easier for a Lunar, but for a combat Solar it's hardly difficult anyway.<br /> Getting a combat ability to 5 is harder than for a Solar, but I think the majority of people who really want to play a combat Lunar will start with a combat ability at 5 anyway (I didn't, but I think most will).<br /> Having a whole bunch of Abilities at 5 is impossible for a Lunar (you can get 3 if you're a stupid min-maxer).<br /> Having even 2 is pretty difficult, but doable if you're desperate for, say, Brawl 5 and Dodge 5 or something.<br /> Personally I think it's better to just go for Brawl 5, Melee 5 or Martial Arts 5 and not bother with any other 5s until much later in the game when you've got lots of spare Lunar XP.<br /> <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, Lunars will have more high attributes and mostly low abilities, while Solars will have a handful of high attributes and quite a few high abilities.<br /> Which makes them, in a game generally, roughly similar. I think it's pretty fair.<br /> <br /> But if we're looking purely at white-room combat, a Dawn caste is going to have higher dice pools most of the time. (He just probably can't do much beyond that, while the Lunar can.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T04:57:54-08:00","id":1291089,"title":"","content":"Clowpiece, you said you'd swap Mastery for being able to buy Dex charms to go with your style (which style is it, out of interest?).<br /> <br /> Would you also be willing to lose Supernal, some of your mote pool at high essence (which sounds like what you're playing), and have less dots at character gen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-23-2019, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T07:51:55-08:00","id":1291129,"title":"","content":"Lunars combining their own Charms with Martial Arts was something introduced as provisional, pending the results of playtesting.<br /> <br /> We know that Lunars have been extensively playtested, and now the version of the book being shown to backers still has that capability.<br /> <br /> So I think one ought to consider why the developers allowed that. Does one think that they're really bad at their jobs? Or that they found a lot of these theoretical applications actually functioned reasonably in play? Or that they didn't really come up so often practically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T08:41:21-08:00","id":1291143,"title":"","content":"My option on this issue can be summed up by the only house rule I've come up with for Lunars so far.<br /> <br /> I will allow Lunars to use Martial Arts in animal form so long as it's a thematically appropriate Style. A Lunar damn well can use Tiger Style while in the form of a Tiger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:26:13-08:00","id":1291152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291143#post1291143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will allow Lunars to use Martial Arts in animal form so long as it's a thematically appropriate Style. A Lunar damn well can use Tiger Style while in the form of a Tiger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's something that they said playtesting <i>did</i> eliminate as non-viable. It really was something the developers considered and tried to make work, and ultimately concluded that it didn't function (I'm guessing that Protean effects, and possibly the benefits of animal Merits and special attacks and latent abilities, pushed it over the edge). That's honestly more of a pursuit than I would have made.<br /> <br /> Besides, how is a snake going to practice Snake Style?<br /> <img src=\"http://33.media.tumblr.com/66611e00e92f42ae32425f867acdfc7b/tumblr_nc7mew6K9z1ruu0mwo1_250.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-23-2019, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:37:30-08:00","id":1291156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291066#post1291066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kill it? Would it really? The intention of Martial Arts balance was always that Mastery was about on-par with solar combat ability, that non-mastery non-terrestrial was on par with celestial combat ability, and terrestrial was on par with dragonblooded combat ability. When people here talk about making lunar MA &quot;viable&quot; what you're really trying to say is &quot;as good as solars&quot;. Well, sorry, this is Exalted and different splats are on explicitly different levels of power and lunars are very firmly weaker than the solars are, and shouldn't get mechanical concessions to &quot;fix&quot; this problem. If lunar animal-shaping is so immensely powerful that non-mastery MA without native charms doesnt even come close, that's a sign that the balance there is screwed up, not that they should be made stronger than solars at MA.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe if I remember correctly, mastery is supposed to be a bit stronger or more versatile than native solar (to offset the buy-in and general high cost of charm acquisition) while the terrestrial keword was supposed to make it about as good as typical terrestrial charm but grant effects outside their normal purview or be slightly better than usual for the same reason as solar charms. I don't remember where I remember reading this. super helpful I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:39:56-08:00","id":1291158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291152#post1291152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that's something that they said playtesting <i>did</i> eliminate as non-viable. It really was something the developers considered and tried to make work, and ultimately concluded that it didn't function (I'm guessing that Protean effects, and possibly the benefits of animal Merits and special attacks and latent abilities, pushed it over the edge). That's honestly more of a pursuit than I would have made.<br /> <br /> Besides, how is a snake going to practice Snake Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the advantages of house rules. I can play fast and loose with them to suit my needs.<br /> <br /> How does a snake practice snake style? Attacks are intended to emulate snake bites, so there is that. Otherwise, not my problem, the players are the ones doing the stunting not me so it's their problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:51:25-08:00","id":1291162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291158#post1291158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the advantages of house rules. I can play fast and loose with them to suit my needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted it to be added to the record, for the benefit of anybody who might have presumed that the disconnect constituted laziness or indifference on the part of the developers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291158#post1291158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">How does a snake practice snake style?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Does my gif there give the impression that my priority was making a martial arts point? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:02:58-08:00","id":1291167,"title":"","content":"My biggest concern is actually with charms like Thousand Claw Affliction and Octopus and Spider Barrage. They're really straight forward charms that let you get a bunch of attacks in a turn that combo well with lots of styles that maybe shouldn't do that. Like you can use Birds-Fall-From-Flock Targeting to AoE target, then Octopus and Spider Barrage attack with Righteous Devil against everyone in the area. Or Thousand Claw Affliction with Steel Devil's Triple Attack Technique.<br /> <br /> Oddly though I gave a cursory look through the Immaculate styles to see what I could break with that, and I didn't come up with anything obvious. So damn, good job! Or bad on me for missing it, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:21:32-08:00","id":1291172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291167#post1291167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest concern is actually with charms like Thousand Claw Affliction and Octopus and Spider Barrage. They're really straight forward charms that let you get a bunch of attacks in a turn that combo well with lots of styles that maybe shouldn't do that. Like you can use Birds-Fall-From-Flock Targeting to AoE target, then Octopus and Spider Barrage attack with Righteous Devil against everyone in the area. Or Thousand Claw Affliction with Steel Devil's Triple Attack Technique.<br /> <br /> Oddly though I gave a cursory look through the Immaculate styles to see what I could break with that, and I didn't come up with anything obvious. So damn, good job! Or bad on me for missing it, lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is the simple tag <br /> Thousand Claw is simple, so is Triple attack from Steel Devil. <br /> Very important to note that <br /> <br /> and being able to BFFFT you need to aim and if you want to do that reflexivly and then use Octopus spider barrage that will be atleast 3 wp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:23:38-08:00","id":1291174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291167#post1291167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest concern is actually with charms like Thousand Claw Affliction and Octopus and Spider Barrage. They're really straight forward charms that let you get a bunch of attacks in a turn that combo well with lots of styles that maybe shouldn't do that. Like you can use Birds-Fall-From-Flock Targeting to AoE target, then Octopus and Spider Barrage attack with Righteous Devil against everyone in the area. Or Thousand Claw Affliction with Steel Devil's Triple Attack Technique.<br /> <br /> Oddly though I gave a cursory look through the Immaculate styles to see what I could break with that, and I didn't come up with anything obvious. So damn, good job! Or bad on me for missing it, lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some good stuff in there but I don't think it's broken. BFFF-T is a great charm, but Dancing Devil Trigger Finger gives RDs an alternative version in the style proper. Also unlike that charm in Solar Melee, OASB and TCA don't explicitly say that one activation of a supplimental charm hits all of their attacks. (plus they've got some limiters in place that shouldn't leave them too devestating)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:35:12-08:00","id":1291179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291129#post1291129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars combining their own Charms with Martial Arts was something introduced as provisional, pending the results of playtesting.<br /> <br /> We know that Lunars have been extensively playtested, and now the version of the book being shown to backers still has that capability.<br /> <br /> So I think one ought to consider why the developers allowed that. Does one think that they're really bad at their jobs? Or that they found a lot of these theoretical applications actually functioned reasonably in play? Or that they didn't really come up so often practically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did everything get tested though? Every style and every possible interaction? It's a pretty tedious task especially with the increasing amount of styles. I mean if something turns out to be an issue the easiest thing to do would be to say that X charm can't interact with MA on a case by case basis.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:35:57-08:00","id":1291180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291172#post1291172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is the simple tag</div> </div> </div> </div>There was something... something that somebody, I think a playtester, once said about Lunars being inclined towards the Simple type, but I can't remember what it was... was it to offset the variety they were given at Essence 1 (or in general)? Your point about it being useful for Martial Arts is good in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:37:11-08:00","id":1291181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291179#post1291179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did everything get tested though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask the developers. {points up}","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:42:17-08:00","id":1291183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291152#post1291152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that's something that they said playtesting <i>did</i> eliminate as non-viable. It really was something the developers considered and tried to make work, and ultimately concluded that it didn't function (I'm guessing that Protean effects, and possibly the benefits of animal Merits and special attacks and latent abilities, pushed it over the edge). That's honestly more of a pursuit than I would have made.<br /> <br /> Besides, how is a snake going to practice Snake Style?<br /> <img src=\"http://33.media.tumblr.com/66611e00e92f42ae32425f867acdfc7b/tumblr_nc7mew6K9z1ruu0mwo1_250.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense.<br /> <br /> As for the last part well the snake uhhh snoutbutts your pressure points and uhhh fangs are like hook swords? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:45:54-08:00","id":1291184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291174#post1291174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's some good stuff in there but I don't think it's broken. BFFF-T is a great charm, but Dancing Devil Trigger Finger gives RDs an alternative version in the style proper. Also unlike that charm in Solar Melee, OASB and TCA don't explicitly say that one activation of a supplimental charm hits all of their attacks. (plus they've got some limiters in place that shouldn't leave them too devestating)</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication I think is that they don't, because you roll X number of attacks rather than just one and it doesn't specify that its an exception to the way supplemental charms usually function (namely they supplement a single roll or action).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T10:48:54-08:00","id":1291185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291172#post1291172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is the simple tag <br /> Thousand Claw is simple, so is Triple attack from Steel Devil. <br /> Very important to note that <br /> <br /> and being able to BFFFT you need to aim and if you want to do that reflexivly and then use Octopus spider barrage that will be atleast 3 wp</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow I never knew triple attack was simple and I had both a primary antagonist and PC in one campaign use them. I gues it just doesn't feel like a simple charm to me, but the style doesn't have a lot of other withering attack things so it makes sense.<br /> <br /> I still feel like there's some style that I'm forgetting that applies a bonus penalty or detonation charge or something when you land an attack, but not having free activations on all attacks should help keep that at least expensive. Expensive doesn't always mean balanced though, it just helps a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:54:11-08:00","id":1291209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291089#post1291089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clowpiece, you said you'd swap Mastery for being able to buy Dex charms to go with your style (which style is it, out of interest?).<br /> <br /> Would you also be willing to lose Supernal, some of your mote pool at high essence (which sounds like what you're playing), and have less dots at character gen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, supernal MA is kind of... not that appealing, already, so yes, absolutely. This is a whole different issue to what this thread is about, though. Suffice to say that until we get martial arts that have high essence effects, supernal MA is a kinda lacklustre choice for dawns (Crane has an Ess 4 effect, but that's one charm! ONE!). So... probably until the sidereal book gives us SMA to really make this supernal feel great. As for the mote pool, it's higher for lunars until ess 3 and the gap is only notable at ess 5, which is very far into a game, and I don't think lunars should only start being a weaker choice for MA at such a long time into a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:05:48-08:00","id":1291211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291209#post1291209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, supernal MA is kind of... not that appealing, already, so yes, absolutely. This is a whole different issue to what this thread is about, though. Suffice to say that until we get martial arts that have high essence effects, supernal MA is a kinda lacklustre choice for dawns (Crane has an Ess 4 effect, but that's one charm! ONE!). So... probably until the sidereal book gives us SMA to really make this supernal feel great. As for the mote pool, it's higher for lunars until ess 3 and the gap is only notable at ess 5, which is very far into a game, and I don't think lunars should only start being a weaker choice for MA at such a long time into a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless SMA can't be supernalled. Though most of the best effects in trees are at E3. <br /> <br /> Speaking of when do lunars get broken combos? Because they start at E1 or possibly 2 and they don't have supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-23-2019, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:07:06-08:00","id":1291212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291209#post1291209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, supernal MA is kind of... not that appealing, already, so yes, absolutely. This is a whole different issue to what this thread is about, though. Suffice to say that until we get martial arts that have high essence effects, supernal MA is a kinda lacklustre choice for dawns (Crane has an Ess 4 effect, but that's one charm! ONE!). So... probably until the sidereal book gives us SMA to really make this supernal feel great. As for the mote pool, it's higher for lunars until ess 3 and the gap is only notable at ess 5, which is very far into a game, and I don't think lunars should only start being a weaker choice for MA at such a long time into a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Immaculate style has at least one Essence 5 effect. One of them allows you to punch people's souls off. Sure you don't get a mastery bonus or an aura keword effect but... you get to punch people's souls off or turn into an invincible stone idol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:09:42-08:00","id":1291214,"title":"","content":"I'm asking because I think it's all holistic; yes, at character gen a Full Moon can combo MA charms with Dex or Strength charms, but they can only take 2-4 MA charms anyway. Whereas the Dawn could start with the whole style.<br /> I was only able to take 3 charms from Snake Style at character gen. And only 2 accuracy charms from Dex, actually. Because as a Lunar, I'm restricted to Essence 1.<br /> If I couldn't combo them, I'd have one good damage charm, one crap speed-bump Evasion charm, a scene-long soak buff that's decent but can't be improved (unlike how a Solar can)... and no excellency.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not the same for an Eclipse, but I don't imagine most Eclipse players, if they've already bought a whole style, needing to buy many more offensive chsrms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:18:11-08:00","id":1291216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291209#post1291209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, supernal MA is kind of... not that appealing, already, so yes, absolutely. This is a whole different issue to what this thread is about, though. Suffice to say that until we get martial arts that have high essence effects, supernal MA is a kinda lacklustre choice for dawns (Crane has an Ess 4 effect, but that's one charm! ONE!).</div> </div> </div> </div>And what do you think of the actual effects of the Martial Arts Charms?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:19:08-08:00","id":1291217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291212#post1291212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every Immaculate style has at least one Essence 5 effect. One of them allows you to punch people's souls off. Sure you don't get a mastery bonus or an aura keword effect but... you get to punch people's souls off or turn into an invincible stone idol</div> </div> </div> </div>I was really hoping that immaculate styles would be good for solar MA, but they've been very specifically designed to be as offputting as possible for solars. No mastery effects and you're literally worse than a dragonblooded at using them, and they're so long that you have to buy 12(!!!!!!) charms to get Soul Mastery. Which you won't even use, as it relies on the rest of the style to function.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:23:50-08:00","id":1291219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291211#post1291211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless SMA can't be supernalled. Though most of the best effects in trees are at E3.<br /> <br /> Speaking of when do lunars get broken combos? Because they start at E1 or possibly 2 and they don't have supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence 2 you have most of any MA and the simple bread and butter accuracy trinity of the lunar dex setup, so from that point on, easily. At ess1 it depends on the MA, some MA outright suck at essence 1, but, also, it's worth noting that only MA supernals are getting ess2 effects at ess1. Most solars with MA are not a supernal MA character, and should still be better at MA than the equivalent lunar is. And, at ess1, solar dodge/resistance dont do very much at all while lunars still get to apply Excellent Strike to their MA attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:25:55-08:00","id":1291220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291219#post1291219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essence 2 you have most of any MA and the simple bread and butter accuracy trinity of the lunar dex setup, so from that point on, easily. At ess1 it depends on the MA, some MA outright suck at essence 1, but, also, it's worth noting that only MA supernals are getting ess2 effects at ess1. Most solars with MA are not a supernal MA character, and should still be better at MA than the equivalent lunar is. And, at ess1, solar dodge/resistance dont do very much at all while lunars still get to apply Excellent Strike to their MA attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the supernal. Though I'm personally not a fan of the keyword. Kind of boring just having all the charms you'll need for one ability at start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:36:02-08:00","id":1291222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291216#post1291216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what do you think of the actual effects of the Martial Arts Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for tripleposting but I have no idea how to do multiple quotes on this forum software. Anyway, it varies by MA but the ones I love I really love. It's just not worth a supernal. Essence 2 is where the meat of most MA are already - as an example, Black Claw (my favourite MA) has only 2 essence 3 charms. I could go supernal MA for heart-ripping claw at chargen, arguably, but when you look at Melee and Brawl and Archery and even Thrown you begin to think &quot;I sure got the short end of the stick here&quot;. One neat effect sorta-early. So that's fine, you can buy up another MA, and surely want to! But by the time you've gotten together the SXP to buy up another MA you're already almost essence 3 anyway. The time discount, as it were, that supernals bring just isn't anywhere near high enough for MA without there being proper high essence effects to truly make it worthwhile. Which SMA are going to bring, so it's all good. MA Supernal will end up the best possible dawn supernal by the end of the line I bet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:45:19-08:00","id":1291226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291217#post1291217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was really hoping that immaculate styles would be good for solar MA, but they've been very specifically designed to be as offputting as possible for solars. No mastery effects and you're literally worse than a dragonblooded at using them, and they're so long that you have to buy 12(!!!!!!) charms to get Soul Mastery. Which you won't even use, as it relies on the rest of the style to function.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get bigger excellencies, have more motes, and can combo them with better Dodge and Resistance charms than Dragonblood can.<br /> <br /> Charm-for-charm, Dragonblood are better, but overall I don't think a Dragonblood using, say, Air Dragon and Dodge, is more powerful than a Solar using Air Dragon and Dodge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the supernal. Though I'm personally not a fan of the keyword. Kind of boring just having all the charms you'll need for one ability at start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a few trees only have a few charms at Essence 1, and I think, for your concept, it's fine to have 6 or 7 charms from your signature ability.<br /> <br /> But it's maybe a bit too attractive to get a whole tree, and then find you have nowhere to go.<br /> On the other hand, if that's what people choose, that's what they choose.<br /> On the other, other hand, a combat supernal Dawn in a circle of people with only a handful of combat abilities is pretty difficult for an ST to balance an encounter against.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:03:24-08:00","id":1291227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291212#post1291212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every Immaculate style has at least one Essence 5 effect. One of them allows you to punch people's souls off. Sure you don't get a mastery bonus or an aura keword effect but... you get to punch people's souls off or turn into an invincible stone idol</div> </div> </div> </div>And you get to do that from <i>chargen </i>even! Also it lets you disguise yourself very well as an Immaculate if you want. So yeah, still appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:07:37-08:00","id":1291231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291061#post1291061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then... play that? That's literally the character I'm playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed the point I was trying to make.<br /> <br /> I shouldn't have to feel like I'm playing with a foot removed because I made a different character choice. Which is, as I said, the case with Lunars. I feel like I lose out a lot by not playing as a Lunar vs a Solar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291065#post1291065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mastery stacking is also something that happens very quickly and a lot of MA charms have a big difference in their effect if you have Mastery or not which can be a huge thing and a Solar MA supernal will have no problem being able to stack those effect</div> </div> </div> </div>I addressed this in my post.<br /> <br /> Mastery is powerful, but aside from a few select charms you wouldn't miss out on much. At least not anything your native charms couldn't do (Even just by looking at DEX so far).<br /> <br /> And I agree with you that if you bar ALL Lunar charms from accessing MA. Until we get an idea set the only thing I can think of is making charms have something like a &quot;Martial-Ready&quot; keyword, allow Dodge but not parry on defense charms, or expand the MA set until this is no longer as much of an issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291080#post1291080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring Evocations for a moment, the Solar needs to invest in another ability to substitute it in when confronted by one of the style's shortcomings.<br /> However, they do pay 1 less xp per MA dot and 2xp less per charm. So it's more a question of how effectively the most appropriate secondary ability papers the style's holes vs. the Lunar charmset and we still don't have a complete picture there for every style.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a minor XP gap yes, but getting a single combat ability from 0 -&gt; 5 is just the cost of doing business in most games. It would be the same if the Lunar decided to go Brawl, Melee, Archery, or Thrown. This truly only becomes significant when one wants to buy up multiple abilities. Which in the case of Lunars you probably don't need to do this again. Maybe if you really want some ranged options.<br /> <br /> And as mentioned before, paying 10 XP per charm isn't game breaking. If you buy a full MA style you're losing out on 2.5 charms at most, and as with evocations this cost could be very well worth it if you style it around your build.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291081#post1291081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just like the ease, lack of hassle, and the concept that Solars are more straight-up powerful with MA while Lunars are more flexible (which is its own strength). So that a Solar Martial Artist and Lunar Martial Artist are both viable but different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the rest of what you've said. Trying to fix this is going to be a bit problematic itself, at least not without downsides and concessions. Likewise I fully admit some game tables will probably never encounter this problem.<br /> <br /> But as I pointed out it goes beyond flexibility. Trying to balance future MA's (let alone current) with Lunar charms is going to be a pain in the arse because you always have the spectre hanging over you. It also doesn't only make Lunar martial artists more &quot;flexible&quot;, nor does it only give them other options to approach MA with. Those I don't mind. What I do mind is that Lunar martial artists become flat out better for the majority of cases in martial arts for the sheer number of expansion charms they can get.<br /> <br /> You want an example? Snake Strikes the Heel. Even IF we decided to balance it a bit by saying something like &quot;When declared both opponents do not use weapon accuracy&quot;, it still benefits from Lunar clash charms. If you want to get better at this as a Solar you either learn an entirely new MA for probably just a single clash enhancers or be told to get screwed. Meanwhile Lunars have several readily available in the Dex tree and do not need to invest in another MA at all (Plus if you're playing snake you're likely a Dex character).<br /> <br /> And before you say if one charm is important like this? It is. Its one of the better charms of the style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291085#post1291085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not much at all. I would trade mastery for the lunar dex charms in a heartbeat and we haven't even seen how STR breaks things even further.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can get far more use out of basic dex charms over mastery in some cases. Why? Because as I mentioned MA's don't give a full &quot;Bread and butter&quot; charmset. At most they might give a smattering of them which then require you to delve into other MA's.<br /> <br /> Mastery allows some funky things in most circumstances, but they're not going to beat the raw mathematical efficiency, scope, and ease of use your native charms are going to afford you compared to another MA style (Barring specific circumstances).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291129#post1291129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars combining their own Charms with Martial Arts was something introduced as provisional, pending the results of playtesting.<br /> <br /> We know that Lunars have been extensively playtested, and now the version of the book being shown to backers still has that capability.<br /> <br /> So I think one ought to consider why the developers allowed that. Does one think that they're really bad at their jobs? Or that they found a lot of these theoretical applications actually functioned reasonably in play? Or that they didn't really come up so often practically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Appeal to authority.<br /> <br /> I've also known several playtesters who had these exact same issues I mentioned. The developers are not infallible. There is already heavy talk of altering the way Solar Bond works in 3e for example after the feedback received from the kickstarter.<br /> <br /> If people literally did not encouter the problems I found then that would be a failure of playtesting. I think they probably did but for some reason ignored it.<br /> <br /> But even if they DIDN'T think it was an issue, how are my other points invalidated?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:14:04-08:00","id":1291234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291217#post1291217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was really hoping that immaculate styles would be good for solar MA, but they've been very specifically designed to be as offputting as possible for solars. No mastery effects and you're literally worse than a dragonblooded at using them, and they're so long that you have to buy 12(!!!!!!) charms to get Soul Mastery. Which you won't even use, as it relies on the rest of the style to function.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, without the aura effects, they are very comfortably solar tier effects. Especially the low essence charms honestly which I feel give you a lot of bread and butter utility, plus you can switch between Melee or Brawl and MA for styles like fire dragon which demand a huge initiative lead (or use your own awareness boosting effects) to fuel your decisive offense. Soul Marking Strike, for instance, is an insanely useful charm even without aura effects. Soul Marking Strike is a really good one, Rippling water Strike is another really decent charm as is searing edge. The Air aspect charms aren't as useful unless you want to play a stealth character but not buy many stealth or athletics charms (they are more useful to a terrestrial). But in generaly, solars get a lot of mileage from the Immaculate styles, not a s much as terrestrials, but they a) aren't supposed to and b) immaculate martial arts are a quantum leap up for terrestrials, it would be a bit silly if they also were incredibly potent for solars and sidereals. It would mean that all the other styles were just worse by comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:23:36-08:00","id":1291238,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's say we didn't let Lunars use native charms with Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> That means, for Lunars;<br /> They can't use an excellency to attack when using the Martial Arts ability (unlike Solars, Dragonblood, etc)<br /> They can't combo Martial Arts with Evasion-boosting abilities (unlike Solars, Dragonblood, etc)<br /> They can't combo Martial Arts with Soak-boosting abilities (unlike Solars, Dragonblood, etc)<br /> They pay 10xp per Martial Arts charm (unlike most of the Solars, Dragonblood, etc, who are taking Martial Arts, and also unlike their native charms)<br /> <br /> As I said, if it is broken, I'm not utterly invested in this set-up. I don't think, generally, Lunar martial artists are better than Solar ones, but I can believe that<br /> <br /> But if the solution is just to take away their ability to use native charms with Martial Arts, then they're going to need some other fixes, or Martial Arts becomes a pretty suboptimal build for Lunars.*<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I'm going to feel like I'm playing with a foot removed for making a different character choice (focusing on Martial Arts with a Lunar), which, as you said, isn't really what you want. All character choices should ideally be balanced and interesting.<br /> <br /> *Someone earlier said that we were trying to make them more powerful than Solars, or at least as good. That's not what I'm talking about. I'm talking about Martial Arts on a Lunar being a competitive build vs Lunar native charms+evocations, or Lunar native charms+shapeshifting, or even Lunar native charms+combat sorcery. I don't think Lunar native charms+Martial Arts is OP compared to Lunar native charms+evocations, or Lunar native charms+shapeshifting.<br /> But if it is, sure, nerf it a bit... but not too much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:27:08-08:00","id":1291239,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Immaculate styles; dunno if this is quite the same, since I don't get Mastery, but I'm comboing Snake with a bit of Fire Dragon, a bit of Earth Dragon, and a bit of Wood Dragon.<br /> Expensive (as you have to buy up the different abilities) but stacking all those withering-damage enhancers and a few different soak enhancers together is hot.<br /> <br /> Even without Mastery, they've got some very good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:29:56-08:00","id":1291240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291234#post1291234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As written, without the aura effects, they are very comfortably solar tier effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean that they're better than Solar charms with aura? I don't think they're comparable to 'solar tier effects' at all, with or without aura, besides Bottomless Depths Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:41:23-08:00","id":1291243,"title":"","content":"I'd say without the aura they're equivalent to the less powerful Solar charms, and with it quite powerful ones.<br /> <br /> They vary a lot though, charm-by-charm. The first 2-3 charms of Earth, Fire and Wood are really decent, whereas the first few of Air and Water are less impressive to me. But obviously Water has Bottomless Depths later.<br /> I think Air really needs to be combined with Dodge though. Probably Fire too.<br /> <br /> Also, they have a lot of effects that give you (Essence) dice, etc, which obviously are pretty meh at Essence 2 and hot at Essence 5. But Dragonblood take a lot longer to reach Essence 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:42:34-08:00","id":1291244,"title":"","content":"I'd honestly peg the Immaculate styles as Celestial power with DB costs.<br /> <br /> They're strong, but some charms are way too expensive for their own good. Its like they went &quot;Oh shit, dragonblooded learn this, we need to up the cost&quot; but went to far in the other direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T13:51:42-08:00","id":1291247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291244#post1291244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd honestly peg the Immaculate styles as Celestial power with DB costs.<br /> <br /> They're strong, but some charms are way too expensive for their own good. Its like they went &amp;quot;Oh shit, dragonblooded learn this, we need to up the cost&amp;quot; but went to far in the other direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that only account for earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T15:13:31-08:00","id":1291265,"title":"","content":"My two obols on the matter: Lunars with MAs are indeed strong but when you invest in MAs in general, your fighting style is usually geared towards that. It means being restrained to the weapons and armor of that style, having charms that help you in its thematics, and so on.<br /> <br /> This is more limiting to a Lunar than for a Solar, if you ask me. You'll probably never again fight in animal forms, unless you <i>really </i>need to. DBT is strong alongside MAs, but its activation is a Simple charm so it can disrupt the flow of your actions. What if you can't manage the special activation of your Form charm, for instance?<br /> <br /> Your MA is not gonna be good in all situations, either.<ul><li>Mantis is really good for restraining single opponents, what with the grappling and disarms and stuff, but it's gonna have a heck of a harder time against multiple enemies, battle groups, and such.</li> <li>By contrast, White Reaper's full potential is only displayed fighting against battle groups - a single strong opponent will usually be much tougher than an army.</li> <li>Styles dependent on weapons like Righteous Devil and Single Point are pretty strong but offer less combo potential with other styles, and Luna help you if you get disarmed.</li> <li>Golden Janissary is amazing at its mission statement: killing creatures of darkness, but outside of that it shines rather less.</li> <li>White Veil, Black Claw, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan and Crane are all fairly strong but either require you to be unarmed, or have a social context they're strongest in - you'll have a harder time facing monsters who dont care for social interactions or nonsentient creatures.</li> </ul>You probably get my point. Lunars have a lot of inherent flexibility that makes facing them hard and you become a bit more predictable if you choose to become a martial artist, which I think is a fair trade-off.<br /> <br /> I'm not gonna claim that I think I'm absolutely correct or anything, but I do think this is being blown a bit out of proportion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24165-parabola","name":"Parabola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T15:52:05-08:00","id":1291276,"title":"","content":"I'm really novice-level at Exalted. I tried, but could never find a group or anything. I'm only really paying attention for this 3e. So forgive me if this question clangs on everyone's nerves, but...<br /> <br /> Maybe Lunars shouldn't worry so much about MA? Why would a Lunar want to have it anyway? <br /> <br /> See, it seems from reading the Charms so far that other Exalts <i>do</i> Martial Arts but Lunars <i>are</i> Martial Arts. It seems like Martial Arts was started to imitate the way animals move, and well, Lunars don't have to <i>imitate</i> a damn thing. So for a Lunar to use Martial Arts is like a high-essence Solar trying to become a god-it's kind of a big step down and to the left. Yeah, they're shifting back and forth between animal and human a lot, but I kind of thought that was the point? <br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong and overlooking something simple and practical. In fact, I'd bet money I am. but please tell me so that I know for the future. And thank you in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:23:22-08:00","id":1291287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291222#post1291222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for tripleposting but I have no idea how to do multiple quotes on this forum software.</div> </div> </div> </div>Press the Quote button on every post which you want to quote. Scroll up to the top of the page to find the Post Reply button with the number of quotes that you selected in brackets. Press that. The text box will be filled with those quotes. Edit and reply as you wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 02-23-2019, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:52:48-08:00","id":1291299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291043#post1291043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in a sense, the fact that Lunars become powerful martial arts when comboing is a feature, not a bug. It's the only way they can approach Solar competency.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, wait, that's no good either, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Part of the problem of &quot;Martial Arts are ridiculously good for Lunars&quot; isn't how it compares to other splats - part of the problem becomes &quot;is it ever reasonable to play a combat-oriented Lunar and <i>not</i> take Martial Arts?&quot; To me, that's a far more serious problem than dick-measuring contests between splats.<br /> <br /> As I understand it, a huge part of the reason why other splats don't get to combine MA with their native charms is because if they could, then absolutely every combat-oriented character would 100% want Martial Arts. Splitting them off ensures that you have to actually specialize in Martial Arts to get full benefit from it, and discourages a Melee character from grabbing one strong early MA charm purely for power reasons (because if you allow that, everyone will do it and MA will lose its unique meaning.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that line would outright kill Lunar MA since why go spec into something when you don't get mastery and can't favored. </div> </div> </div>I feel like that could be solved by more subtle changes. For instance, just choose an Attribute and say &quot;if you favor this, then you can also treat MA charms as favored.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:10:02-08:00","id":1291311,"title":"","content":"Yes. The MA problem is bad for lunars, too, because its a power multiplier. Every lunar has 2 choices: pick the most broken animal shape you can (and there's a few) or invest in MA. If you care about combat, you have to do this or you are missing a huge gulf of potential power that adds on to your other power. You don't have to give up evocations for this, either: Righteous Devil is the strongest martial art and lets you have a weapon and armour.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;dick-measuring contest&quot;, though, it must be stressed that Solars really are the strongest and the mechanics should support this, at all levels. For all castes. Even the Dawn Caste. In fact, the gap between a Dawn and a Full Moon should be the same as that of a Twilight and a No Moon, the gap between solar circle sorcery and celestial circle sorcery. The Dawn Caste is just as much a solar as the Zenith and Twilight, no matter how much people desperately want to beat one in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:14:36-08:00","id":1291312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291311#post1291311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. The MA problem is bad for lunars, too, because its a power multiplier. Every lunar has 2 choices: pick the most broken animal shape you can (and there's a few) or invest in MA. If you care about combat, you have to do this or you are missing a huge gulf of potential power that adds on to your other power. You don't have to give up evocations for this, either: Righteous Devil is the strongest martial art and lets you have a weapon and armour.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;dick-measuring contest&quot;, though, it must be stressed that Solars really are the strongest and the mechanics should support this, at all levels. For all castes. Even the Dawn Caste. In fact, the gap between a Dawn and a Full Moon should be the same as that of a Twilight and a No Moon, the gap between solar circle sorcery and celestial circle sorcery. The Dawn Caste is just as much a solar as the Zenith and Twilight, no matter how much people desperately want to beat one in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>It absolutely should not be that different. Celestials in 1e were fairly close to one another and solars could still lose to other celestials. The uncertainty of the win should still be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:17:09-08:00","id":1291313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291299#post1291299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, a huge part of the reason why other splats don't get to combine MA with their native charms is because if they could, then absolutely every combat-oriented character would 100% want Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the intention of the designers really that fighting focused PCs should not pick up some martial arts, if their main strength is in another ability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:19:18-08:00","id":1291314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291238#post1291238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the solution is just to take away their ability to use native charms with Martial Arts, then they're going to need some other fixes, or Martial Arts becomes a pretty suboptimal build for Lunars.*</div> </div> </div> </div>Months and months ago, I pointed out this same idea in regards to Sorcery. Want to be a Lunar Sorcerer? No Tier 3 for you! (but you get Necromancy tier 2). So ok, the Lunar theme is &quot;versatility and occasional brute-forcing our shapeshifting abilities in contrast to Solars' Do Everything Awesomely style. <br /> <br /> Just on a meta-overview level, if we are taking away <i>the thing that makes Lunars work</i> the entire design philosophy of Lunars mechanically falls apart. They just become &quot;Animal People stuck forever in 2nd place but you should still play one because how neat is it that your mechanically inferior abilities let you turn into a fox amirite?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:21:29-08:00","id":1291316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291314#post1291314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Months and months ago, I pointed out this same idea in regards to Sorcery. Want to be a Lunar Sorcerer? No Tier 3 for you! (but you get Necromancy tier 2). So ok, the Lunar theme is &quot;versatility and occasional brute-forcing our shapeshifting abilities in contrast to Solars' Do Everything Awesomely style.<br /> <br /> Just on a meta-overview level, if we are taking away <i>the thing that makes Lunars work</i> the entire design philosophy of Lunars mechanically falls apart. They just become &quot;Animal People stuck forever in 2nd place but you should still play one because how neat is it that your mechanically inferior abilities let you turn into a fox amirite?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you care about being mechanically first place then there's a splat that's designed around being mechanically first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","user":"bboat","date":". 02-23-2019, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:27:16-08:00","id":1291320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291314#post1291314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Months and months ago, I pointed out this same idea in regards to Sorcery. Want to be a Lunar Sorcerer? No Tier 3 for you! (but you get Necromancy tier 2). So ok, the Lunar theme is &quot;versatility and occasional brute-forcing our shapeshifting abilities in contrast to Solars' Do Everything Awesomely style.<br /> <br /> Just on a meta-overview level, if we are taking away <i>the thing that makes Lunars work</i> the entire design philosophy of Lunars mechanically falls apart. They just become &quot;Animal People stuck forever in 2nd place but you should still play one because how neat is it that your mechanically inferior abilities let you turn into a fox amirite?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of things you can do with sorcery though. Being the best at sorcery was never much of an issue because each tier had their own pros and cons. If you want to get Solar sorcery you could ask your ST if you could acquire something of similar power as the mantle of brigid. Which yes is N/A but half of exalted is finding such things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:31:01-08:00","id":1291323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291312#post1291312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It absolutely should not be that different. Celestials in 1e were fairly close to one another and solars could still lose to other celestials. The uncertainty of the win should still be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should it not be that different, exactly? What part of the setting suggests this? Was the first age just the age of Twilights? Are they the only caste allowed to be significant in-setting? The jade prison just broke, and 30 dawns - THIRTY dawns are returning to the world, and they are just as important and just as threatening to the status quo as those 30 twilights or 30 zeniths. They are not &quot;a full moon but a little better&quot;, they are the greatest at what they do, to such a degree that their release is the defining moment of the era. Lunars are not a splat about being Fighters, with solars as Wizards. Lunars can socialise and wield sorcery very well. Just think about how bizarre this argument is. It's not a problem at all that solars can break a man's will with the force of their speech or call upon Ligier to walk Creation for the first time in 2 millenia, but when combat prowess is mentioned, suddenly there's a great shuffling of paper and tugging of beards and &quot;well, I suppose we can let them be a teensy bit stronger than a full moon is, maybe&quot;. We've come so far from DnD, but people are still stuck in a mindset that combat prowess = how important you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:37:14-08:00","id":1291325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291312#post1291312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It absolutely should not be that different. Celestials in 1e were fairly close to one another and solars could still lose to other celestials. The uncertainty of the win should still be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, pretty sure &quot;Take the gap between Celestial and Solar spells, then somehow extrapolate back to Ability X Charms&quot; is not part of the design philosophy for Charms or Solars that any of the developers will ever use. The design has always been around trying to make them work out like the kind of heroes they are, in genre, and have a fun game to play (which includes uncertainty and challenge).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291320#post1291320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of things you can do with sorcery though. Being the best at sorcery was never much of an issue because each tier had their own pros and cons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes again; sorcery isn't really a zero sum conflict such that a Solar who uses sorcery will tend to be just better in a general sense, and instead there's a broad canvas of spells that can be bought, trade offs between what each tier is best for, cleverness in using them, etc. Sorcery just isn't a very good analogy for combat at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:39:09-08:00","id":1291327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291325#post1291325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes again; sorcery isn't really a zero sum conflict such that a Solar who uses sorcery will tend to be just better in a general sense, and instead there's a broad canvas of spells that can be bought, trade offs between what each tier is best for, cleverness in using them, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar Circle is the best and most powerful one, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:43:24-08:00","id":1291329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291314#post1291314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Months and months ago, I pointed out this same idea in regards to Sorcery. Want to be a Lunar Sorcerer? No Tier 3 for you! (but you get Necromancy tier 2). So ok, the Lunar theme is &quot;versatility and occasional brute-forcing our shapeshifting abilities in contrast to Solars' Do Everything Awesomely style.<br /> <br /> Just on a meta-overview level, if we are taking away <i>the thing that makes Lunars work</i> the entire design philosophy of Lunars mechanically falls apart. They just become &quot;Animal People stuck forever in 2nd place but you should still play one because how neat is it that your mechanically inferior abilities let you turn into a fox amirite?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if you've read this yet, but there have been 400 lunars active in Creation for 1500 years after the usurpation. Imagine for a moment that, say, 1/10 of them are sorcerers of enough might to reach the third circle, in this alternate world where lunars get solar circle sorcery. Now, the lunars are all part of the Silver Pact, which is an organisation united around the destruction of the Realm. Actually around the destruction of the Shogunate, but they got beat to the punch there. Let's ignore the Scarlet Empress establishing an empire over the course of 100 years with none of them killing her or stopping this. Let's also say that only 1/4 of these sorcerers want to fight the Realm, the other 3/4 are... I mean, they're solar circle sorcerers, they're erecting wonders only seen since the First Age, the entire setting is so radically altered by this change to mechanics as to be unrecognisable. But let's just ignore this too. These 10 remaining lunars who are both ready and willing get together and say &quot;We're going to fight the Realm&quot;. All 10 of them conjure up a 3rd circle demon from the pits of Malfeas. How does the Realm still exist after this as anything but a smouldering ruin?<br /> <br /> To put it another way, there is a very good reason why the strongest things in the setting are locked behind a group of ~10 people who have spent 1.5 millenia being spawn-camped out of terror over what they'll do if left alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:04:26-08:00","id":1291335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291323#post1291323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should it not be that different, exactly? What part of the setting suggests this? Was the first age just the age of Twilights? Are they the only caste allowed to be significant in-setting? The jade prison just broke, and 30 dawns - THIRTY dawns are returning to the world, and they are just as important and just as threatening to the status quo as those 30 twilights or 30 zeniths. They are not &quot;a full moon but a little better&quot;, they are the greatest at what they do, to such a degree that their release is the defining moment of the era. Lunars are not a splat about being Fighters, with solars as Wizards. Lunars can socialise and wield sorcery very well. Just think about how bizarre this argument is. It's not a problem at all that solars can break a man's will with the force of their speech or call upon Ligier to walk Creation for the first time in 2 millenia, but when combat prowess is mentioned, suddenly there's a great shuffling of paper and tugging of beards and &quot;well, I suppose we can let them be a teensy bit stronger than a full moon is, maybe&quot;. We've come so far from DnD, but people are still stuck in a mindset that combat prowess = how important you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery is completely different than the nature of charms. It's an extrinsic power and one that makes solars better than other celestials with magic. However, that doesn't mean that there's a leap between celestials and solars. Solars are pretty inferior at using MA compared to sidereals but much better at wielding Sorcery but that doesn't mean that a fight between a celestial and a solar is going to be a guarantee. This isn't just in combat but also every other facet of the game. Other celestials have powers that are almost as good if not sometimes better than what solars have in niche situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:12:40-08:00","id":1291337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291335#post1291335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery is completely different than the nature of charms. It's an extrinsic power and one that makes solars better than other celestials with magic. However, that doesn't mean that there's a leap between celestials and solars. Solars are pretty inferior at using MA compared to sidereals but much better at wielding Sorcery but that doesn't mean that a fight between a celestial and a solar is going to be a guarantee. This isn't just in combat but also every other facet of the game. Other celestials have powers that are almost as good if not sometimes better than what solars have in niche situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The versatility and power of the Solar toolset means that they are the most excellent in every niche, unless you count shapeshifting or jiggling fate around as niches, which I don't. It's not a matter of having powers that Solars have no way to access that let them do things in ways that Solars can't do things - that's true and its a big reason to play something that is not a Solar (Solars are not my favorite splat by a long shot). But the fact is that there is a very substantial leap between Solars and Celestials, because Solars are much better in every single niche than Celestial Exalts. It's why it was so hard to put them all in a jar and it's the central conceit of the setting - everything has gone to shit because nobody is as good as they were!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","user":"bboat","date":". 02-23-2019, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:24:09-08:00","id":1291341,"title":"","content":"Remember sorcery in 3e is not the same, quite. You can achieve Solar results *as a mortal*, via workings albeit it is very difficult.<br /> <br /> Lunars are not so disadvantaged, reaching up a circle, so they largely only miss out on formal spells. You just have to be happy with Magma Krakening things as opposed to Death Ray.<br /> <br /> Solar circle is a bunch of nukes. You don't need nukes every day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:25:00-08:00","id":1291342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bboat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291337#post1291337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The versatility and power of the Solar toolset means that they are the most excellent in every niche, unless you count shapeshifting or jiggling fate around as niches, which I don't. It's not a matter of having powers that Solars have no way to access that let them do things in ways that Solars can't do things - that's true and its a big reason to play something that is not a Solar (Solars are not my favorite splat by a long shot). But the fact is that there is a very substantial leap between Solars and Celestials, because Solars are much better in every single niche than Celestial Exalts. It's why it was so hard to put them all in a jar and it's the central conceit of the setting - everything has gone to shit because nobody is as good as they were!</div> </div> </div> </div>But the only huge leaps are Crafting and Sorcery and crafting is due to sorcery. However, nothing stops a celestial from creating First Age Artifice. Lunar's other ability charms are still fairly equal to solars and they have better disguises due to shapeshifting. Solars are overall better but celestials still have their own ways and abilities that solars have no clear parallel towards. The reason the setting is the way it is, is due to the fact that there are exalts who want to keep creation in a lower technological civilization. Sidereals could have helped maintain a better level of technology than what currently exists but chose not to because it was easier on them and lunars decided to raze down to prevent others from having it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:26:14-08:00","id":1291344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291342#post1291342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals could have helped maintain a better level of technology than what currently exists but chose not to because it was easier on them and lunars decided to raze down to prevent others from having it.</div> </div> </div> </div>whyhat lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:26:46-08:00","id":1291345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291335#post1291335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are pretty inferior at using MA compared to sidereals</div> </div> </div> </div>Play one of The Solar Exalted if you want<br /> \u2022 to be a master of martial arts, sorcery, or Evocations.<br /> <br /> This is what I'm talking about, before. You're thinking of sidereals as &quot;the MA splat&quot; and, therefore, those solars don't get to be as good at it. But this is untrue. This is not what the setting is. There are things sidereals can do that solars cannot! A solar can't shuffle around fate to make a city walk 10 miles away. They can't show someone a vision of their own death that is then destined to come true. They can't touch a friend and turn them into a flying mount, forever breaking their mind in the process. But what they CAN do is master the martial arts like no-one has for millenia, and the moment some rebel in Heaven lets them in on it, they're mastering those SMAs just as well as the ancient agents of heaven can.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:29:58-08:00","id":1291347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291342#post1291342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, nothing stops a celestial from creating First Age Artifice.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're totally incapable of producing it to any level or in any amount that appreciably affects the setting. That's why it's called First Age Artifice and not First Age and Age of Sorrows Artifice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","user":"bboat","date":". 02-23-2019, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:35:14-08:00","id":1291350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291345#post1291345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Play one of The Solar Exalted if you want<br /> \u2022 to be a master of martial arts, sorcery, or Evocations.<br /> <br /> This is what I'm talking about, before. You're thinking of sidereals as &quot;the MA splat&quot; and, therefore, those solars don't get to be as good at it. But this is untrue. This is not what the setting is. There are things sidereals can do that solars cannot! A solar can't shuffle around fate to make a city walk 10 miles away. They can't show someone a vision of their own death that is then destined to come true. They can't touch a friend and turn them into a flying mount, forever breaking their mind in the process. But what they CAN do is master the martial arts like no-one has for millenia, and the moment some rebel in Heaven lets them in on it, they're mastering those SMAs just as well as the ancient agents of heaven can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they can't master SMA. They never could. They can't use sutra effects. They'll always be second best in MA because of this. Sidereals have the ability to get Mastery on normal MA but solars can't get Sutra effects on SMA. They might be physically stronger and brawl is insane but they'll never be better than Sidereals at Martial arts. Because it'll always be imperfect mastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:35:15-08:00","id":1291351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291342#post1291342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the only huge leaps are Crafting and Sorcery and crafting is due to sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the huge leaps are in every possible aspect of human endeavour. Otherwise Sol Invictus is pretty fucking stupid for not just making 300 Twilights and letting Luna and the Maidens handle everything that didn't involve reading a book or hitting shit with a wrench. He's the god of many things, and being a nerd is not chief among them, and it's not the <i>zenith </i>of Solar Excellence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:36:49-08:00","id":1291352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291341#post1291341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember sorcery in 3e is not the same, quite. You can achieve Solar results *as a mortal*, via workings albeit it is very difficult.<br /> <br /> Lunars are not so disadvantaged, reaching up a circle, so they largely only miss out on formal spells. You just have to be happy with Magma Krakening things as opposed to Death Ray.<br /> <br /> Solar circle is a bunch of nukes. You don't need nukes every day.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need nukes every day, no. However, you have a nuke, and no-one else does, and this warps the setting around you. Everyone in their right mind is looking at you - you, the sorcerer who has just turned a city to molten slag, or a a desert into a lush paradise, with a wave of their hand. Celestial sorcery... cannnot do this. At all. It does not reach anywhere near this. There are definitely situations where magma kraken is more useful than rain of doom. In fact most fights, I'd imagine, it's more useful. But one of these is far more impactful on the setting. This is what the difference between a dawn and a full moon should signify as well - this blind swordsman or street fighter or escaped slave or whoever they are, this Fighter, is JUST as important and impactful on the setting as the Wizard is with their fancy spells and artifacts. This is not DnD! The fighter does not have to be worse and less important than the wizard! They can matter too, damnit, and they do matter, and mechanics are important for affirming the lore because this is a very, very crunch-heavy system, not some abstract storygame. The returning Dawn is going to warp the setting around about them, they are going to cleave armies and complacent, ancient monsters down, and their return will herald the changing times every bit as much as the twilight or zenith or eclipse does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:36:50-08:00","id":1291353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bboat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291351#post1291351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the only huge leaps are in every other possible aspect of human endeavour. Otherwise Sol Invictus is pretty fucking stupid for not just making 300 Twilights and letting Luna and the Maidens handle everything that didn't involve reading a book or hitting shit with a wrench. He's the god of many things, and being a nerd is not chief among them, and it's not the <i>zenith </i>of Solar Excellence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, a solar is slightly better. The level of difference isn't the difference between a celestial and terrestrial. have you actually read lunar charms because there are some things lunars do amazingly well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:38:13-08:00","id":1291354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291353#post1291353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, a solar is slightly better. The level of difference isn't the difference between a celestial and terrestrial. have you actually read lunar charms because there are some things lunars do amazingly well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes you wonder why the 400 instantly-reincarnating Lunars didn't overrun the ravaged Terrestrials after the Great Contagion, or why the Solars returning to the world is a big deal at all, if you look at it like that. Pretty stinking odd!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:40:16-08:00","id":1291355,"title":"","content":"Oh my god, the Solars have returned! They're slightly better than Lunars in some areas and there's less than half as many of them! But a couple dozen of them might have Craft or Occult!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:41:07-08:00","id":1291356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291350#post1291350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except they can't master SMA. They never could. They can't use sutra effects. They'll always be second best in MA because of this. Sidereals have the ability to get Mastery on normal MA but solars can't get Sutra effects on SMA. They might be physically stronger and brawl is insane but they'll never be better than Sidereals at Martial arts. Because it'll always be imperfect mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those who remember the Sidereals of old agree on one<br /> thing: they were martial artists whose genius was without<br /> compare. Only the Solar Exalted could boast equal<br /> prowess, and then only under the tutelage of a Sidereal<br /> mentor. <br /> <br /> Like, again, this is the corebook. It's right there. Equal prowess. Huh. Not &quot;second best&quot;, weirdly! It keeps saying equal prowess and mastery and other things totally different to what you're saying!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:41:09-08:00","id":1291357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bboat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291354#post1291354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes you wonder why the 400 instantly-reincarnating Lunars didn't overrun the ravaged Terrestrials after the Great Contagion, or why the Solars returning to the world is a big deal at all, if you look at it like that. Pretty stinking odd!</div> </div> </div> </div> That's because ten thousand dragon blooded and the sidereals who have helped them stay out on top have stopped them.<br />","sig