nar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291360#post1291360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The core book says a lot of things but the devs have already said solars won't get sutra effects so they'll never have it at the same level as sidereals. It's just a setting facet that's been around since the beginning of 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars being the pinnacle of excellence is quite an important facet of the setting, but one that seems to have evaded you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:46:44-08:00","id":1291362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bboat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291358#post1291358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have an inkling that there might not have been ten thousand Dragonblooded around to stop the Lunars directly after the Great Contagion. Something tells me the Sidereals might have had some stuff on their plate too.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were millions of dragon blooded before the contagion and only a few thousand afterwards but the lunars were also dealing with stuff because the great contagion also brought balors crusade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:46:58-08:00","id":1291363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291357#post1291357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because ten thousand dragon blooded and the sidereals who have helped them stay out on top have stopped them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A small group of ragtag solars brought down an entire Great House. Sidereals were involved in trying to stop this happening. Their collapse is one of the major events of the era.<br /> <br /> I actually don't like the Bull much at all, because he exalts as a solar 5 minutes before you and breaks an entire great house and it feels like it distracts a little from the significance of you doing so as a solar yourself. But it's important, in the end, because it sets a very clear example of what a group of returning solars means for Creation. It means the status quo is about to be given the people's elbow (perhaps People's Elbow Prana) in a way that those 400 lunars just couldnt manage for the last 1500 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:48:57-08:00","id":1291364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bboat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291361#post1291361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solars being the pinnacle of excellence is quite an important facet of the setting, but one that seems to have evaded you.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they are and it's represented as Solar Brawl. An non-formalized set of abilities which give solars powerful unarmed techniques. Which isn't Martial Arts but I guess that distinction only matters to the person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:51:01-08:00","id":1291365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"