onyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291371#post1291371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of the word used, the point is that while lunars are strong they've always had others to oppose them. The newly returned solars represent unexpected and unpredected change which could change creation but it might not either.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think that there's even a slight possibility that the Solar Exalted returning to Creation will not change it in enormous ways then you have a very odd and withered view of the setting that I don't want to examine in case I catch something. I don't know it could possibly be a fucking 50/50 to you and I hope that views like this and the belief that Solars are just slightly better than some splats in some ways are not as common as they seem to be, or I don't have a lot of hope for the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","user":"bboat","date":". 02-23-2019, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:07:37-08:00","id":1291377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291366#post1291366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason house tepet lost that fight was because every other great house sabotaged them because they wanted tipet to suffer massive losses. It's in the dragon blooded book. Yeah, the bull did win but he had the massive advantage of the realm underhandedly destroying their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Well, you must be right. A circle of solars would never ever stand a chance against a few dozen dragonblooded. Which begs the question of who the real villains of the usurpation are. After all, if it's that easy to kill the solars, sounds like the dragonblooded - whose numbers were, you said earlier, in the millions - were simply power-hungry villains slaughtering a group of craftsmen and sorcerers. Hell, you said it yourself, 1v1 those siddies will kick their ass. Isn't it fun to think about the setting implications of the solars not actually being the greatest of all the exalted by a significant margin?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:11:25-08:00","id":1291380,"title":"","content":"why didnt they put the fucking luanrs in a jade doghouse if theyre just as strong lmao<br /> <br /> Back on topic: Lunar attack enhancers being able to combine with MA is silly. The flurries are kind of silly too. I think they should be allowed their defensive charms but it probably takes a lot of annoying keywording. That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:11:29-08:00","id":1291381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291377#post1291377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Well, you must be right. A circle of solars would never ever stand a chance against a few dozen dragonblooded. Which begs the question of who the real villains of the usurpation are. After all, if it's that easy to kill the solars, sounds like the dragonblooded - whose numbers were, you said earlier, in the millions - were simply power-hungry villains slaughtering a group of craftsmen and sorcerers. Hell, you said it yourself, 1v1 those siddies will kick their ass. Isn't it fun to think about the setting implications of the solars not actually being the greatest of all the exalted by a significant margin?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are only 100 sidereals versus 300 solars and 400 lunars. 300 solars who were doing whatever they wanted as a ruling class. I think you're taking this way to personally.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:13:19-08:00","id":1291382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291381#post1291381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are only 100 sidereals versus 300 solars and 400 lunars. 300 solars who were doing whatever they wanted as a ruling class. I think you're taking this way to personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>The millions of DBs are probably what tipped it right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:15:23-08:00","id":1291384,"title":"","content":"This isn't a question or a statement that needs answering or anything, I just thought that you should know that you said earlier that the Sidereals were capable of maintaining the infrastructure of the First Age but chose not to out of indolence, but you also seem to understand that theres only 100 of them, and you probably also understand that theyre not all e5 with 5 dots in Craft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:18:22-08:00","id":1291386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bboat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291382#post1291382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The millions of DBs are probably what tipped it right</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how powerful DBs are compared to Solars now, the idea that millions of them even considered overthrowing Solars dangerous is laughable.<br /> <br /> The main reason that the return of the Solars is such an upset is because there\u2019s like 150 of them and the Lunar war currently balances on a knife edge. It would be like having a hockey game where one team has an extra three players. At a professional levels where all players are reasonably equally talented the team with 3 men down gets wrecked no contest.<br /> <br /> The fact that they\u2019re more powerful helps with that, but it\u2019s half countered by the fact that they\u2019re all freshly exalted where most Lunars aren\u2019t.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:18:36-08:00","id":1291388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291381#post1291381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are only 100 sidereals versus 300 solars and 400 lunars. 300 solars who were doing whatever they wanted as a ruling class. I think you're taking this way to personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the million dragonblooded? You stated pretty clearly that a legion - a few dozen dragonblooded - would beat a circle of solars without outside interference. Also, why are you assuming that these 400 lunars were all on the solars side? If they were, why weren't they put in the jade prison too? Why were solars the ruling class in this world where they clearly had no way to enforce it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:21:49-08:00","id":1291389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291386#post1291386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering how powerful DBs are compared to Solars now, the idea that millions of them even considered overthrowing Solars dangerous is laughable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very.<br /> <br /> I think the majority of Lunars are pretty fresh-faced too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:24:46-08:00","id":1291390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291388#post1291388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the million dragonblooded? You stated pretty clearly that a legion - a few dozen dragonblooded - would beat a circle of solars without outside interference. Also, why are you assuming that these 400 lunars were all on the solars side? If they were, why weren't they put in the jade prison too? Why were solars the ruling class in this world where they clearly had no way to enforce it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we really arguing things that were laid out? The lunars were also attacked because they were too close to the solars and their exaltations were too mercurial for capture. The jade prison was constructed to explicitly house solar essence. Also, celestials live longer and in their age acquire more power. The Bulls group were a bunch of low essence solars against a group that contained several veteran dragon-blooded. The situation wasn't the same.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm kind of just done with this. That's not what this topic is about and it feels like you are taking this way too personally for my taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:25:07-08:00","id":1291391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bboat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291389#post1291389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very.<br /> <br /> I think the majority of Lunars are pretty fresh-faced too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah majority probably are, not as fresh probably just because there might be a lot in the 10-20 years exalted range where Solars are less than five. There\u2019s definitely more in the 500-1,000 year range as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:30:18-08:00","id":1291392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291386#post1291386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering how powerful DBs are compared to Solars now, the idea that millions of them even considered overthrowing Solars dangerous is laughable.<br /> <br /> The main reason that the return of the Solars is such an upset is because there\u2019s like 150 of them and the Lunar war currently balances on a knife edge. It would be like having a hockey game where one team has an extra three players. At a professional levels where all players are reasonably equally talented the team with 3 men down gets wrecked no contest.<br /> <br /> The fact that they\u2019re more powerful helps with that, but it\u2019s half countered by the fact that they\u2019re all freshly exalted where most Lunars aren\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's wonderful to know that the war against the Realm is a foregone conclusion. The setting is solved, we can all go home. We've finally nailed the exact thematics and role of the Solars in the Age of Sorrows: 150 extra lunars to help the Silver Pact win their easy war.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:34:05-08:00","id":1291394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291392#post1291392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's wonderful to know that the war against the Realm is a foregone conclusion. The setting is solved, we can all go home. We've finally nailed the exact thematics and role of the Solars in the Age of Sorrows: 150 extra lunars to help the Silver Pact win their easy war.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the 150 Solars all decided to join the Silver Pact, and there weren\u2019t any Lunars who had serious problems with that, and the Realm didn\u2019t start immediately taking it way way more seriously than their inner politics, yeah it would pretty much be over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:37:20-08:00","id":1291395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291394#post1291394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the 150 Solars all decided to join the Silver Pact, and there weren\u2019t any Lunars who had serious problems with that, and the Realm didn\u2019t start immediately taking it way way more seriously than their inner politics, yeah it would pretty much be over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So it's an easy victory, unless the solars fuck it up. Much better.<br /> <br /> This is the world into which the Solar Exalted have<br /> returned \u2014 but will they save the world, or will they<br /> destroy it? Really it's pretty simple, just join the Silver Pact. They've got this under control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:43:55-08:00","id":1291399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291395#post1291395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. So it's an easy victory, unless the solars fuck it up. Much better.<br /> <br /> This is the world into which the Solar Exalted have<br /> returned \u2014 but will they save the world, or will they<br /> destroy it? Really it's pretty simple, just join the Silver Pact. They've got this under control.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Silver Pact has literal baby-eating monsters though, so like, some Solars might have an issue with that. Also even in the Pact there\u2019s infighting over what victory even means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T21:38:45-08:00","id":1291424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parabola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291265#post1291265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My two obols on the matter: Lunars with MAs are indeed strong but when you invest in MAs in general, your fighting style is usually geared towards that. It means being restrained to the weapons and armor of that style, having charms that help you in its thematics, and so on.<br /> <br /> This is more limiting to a Lunar than for a Solar, if you ask me. You'll probably never again fight in animal forms, unless you <i>really </i>need to. DBT is strong alongside MAs, but its activation is a Simple charm so it can disrupt the flow of your actions. What if you can't manage the special activation of your Form charm, for instance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Losing out on animal form is a thing yes, but one of the problems of past editions was having One True Build Lunars, with DBT Lunars being a distant second.<br /> <br /> And if you can't manage the reflexive activation of your form charm? Activate it manually. Its a bit painful but it can be done. DBT likewise is strong, but isn't supposed to be the &quot;Be all end all&quot; in combat either. If you're a Lunar with low STR and taking MA then likely you're not gonna pick up DBT.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parabola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291265#post1291265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your MA is not gonna be good in all situations, either.<ul><li>Mantis is really good for restraining single opponents, what with the grappling and disarms and stuff, but it's gonna have a heck of a harder time against multiple enemies, battle groups, and such.</li> <li>By contrast, White Reaper's full potential is only displayed fighting against battle groups - a single strong opponent will usually be much tougher than an army.</li> <li>Styles dependent on weapons like Righteous Devil and Single Point are pretty strong but offer less combo potential with other styles, and Luna help you if you get disarmed.</li> <li>Golden Janissary is amazing at its mission statement: killing creatures of darkness, but outside of that it shines rather less.</li> <li>White Veil, Black Claw, Dreaming Pearl Courtesan and Crane are all fairly strong but either require you to be unarmed, or have a social context they're strongest in - you'll have a harder time facing monsters who dont care for social interactions or nonsentient creatures.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>White Reaper is still amazingly strong even against single opponents. True it likes have multiple opponents, but the core charms themselves are still pretty beefy and things you'd rather not be hit by.</li> <li>Single Point and Righteous Devil are offset by its outright insane offensive power both can provide, some say a little too much. But yes disarming them works quite well.</li> <li>Golden Janissary does do lackluster against non-CoD's yes.</li> <li>DPC gets a small nerf but can do fine against emotionless creatures. The others are not as lucky though.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parabola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291265#post1291265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not gonna claim that I think I'm absolutely correct or anything, but I do think this is being blown a bit out of proportion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what's good in most situations? Native charms or getting an MA style that lets you expand your fighting style a bit. You know who does that more easily with far less investment? Lunars.<br /> <br /> So no, that combined with the other issues I have makes me believe I am not blowing it out of proportion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T01:26:32-08:00","id":1291453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291395#post1291395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. So it's an easy victory, unless the solars fuck it up. Much better.<br /> <br /> This is the world into which the Solar Exalted have<br /> returned \u2014 but will they save the world, or will they<br /> destroy it? Really it's pretty simple, just join the Silver Pact. They've got this under control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually... Sort of yes.<br /> <br /> One of the themes of Exalted is that the Exalted Host has the power to solve the world's problems... If they work together.<br /> <br /> But of course, they don't.<br /> <br /> If all 400 Lunars and 150 Solars worked in unison, they could defeat the Realm, though it'd be bloody.<br /> <br /> If 400 Lunars, 150 Solars, 80 Sidereals and 25000 Dragonblood worked together, as they did in the High First Age, they could build a great society.<br /> <br /> But the Lunars barely work together as it is (look at Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi), while the Solars aren't even organised at all. Solars may find Lunars horrifying, Lunars may be suspicious of Solars.<br /> <br /> In the game I play, the party is Essence 5. We're facing an invasion by 2 Realm Legions. We've got 4 Solar PCs (Essence 5) including a Solar Sorceress and a general with every published war charm. We've got armies of Tiger Warriors. We've got 2 Lunar PCs (Essence 5). We have the support of the common people. We've got 4 more Solar NPCs staying at our base, and 3 Lunar NPCs. We've got a warstrider.<br /> <br /> All of this is easily enough to defeat two Realm Legions.<br /> But I think we will either fail, or take heavy losses before winning. And there's no way we'll liberate the Realm satrapies.<br /> Why? Because all these Solars and Lunars just won't work together!<br /> The general and sorceress hate each other. The spy master and priestess hate both of them. The priest hates the general. No one believes the prophetess. The sorceress considers everyone else useless. A lot of others think she murdered the Night Caste recently. The rabbit-Lunar hates the sorceress and the 3 Lunar NPCs. No one trusts the gang boss, or the Lunar lieutenant. Another Lunar said that he'd join us if the rabbit-Lunar asked, but she doesn't trust him.<br /> <br /> If all the Solars and Lunars worked together, we'd beat the Realm. The problem is getting very different people with strong beliefs and a ton of ego to work together.<br /> <br /> <br /> To put it another way: Imagine the Lunars as the USSR, Britain, and various guerilla resistances. We'd been fighting the Reich for years (2 years, to be exact), it was bloody, and brutal, and devastating. They'd conquered most of central Europe, but we'd managed to keep them out of the periphery at great cost. Their internal problems (bad economy, a mad leader) may have meant that, eventually, we'd have beaten them, or at least kicked them back to their core territories. Or not. Maybe we'd have just fought them to a stalemate. Maybe they'd have conquered us eventually. Very difficult to tell.<br /> What we really needed was the USA to help us. As powerful as Britain and the USSR were, we could not land a decisive blow on the Reich. Defending the periphery, and causing economic damage with raids, was about all we could manage.<br /> But would the USA help us? We didn't have similar ideologies. The USA had strongly opposed the USSR during its formation.<br /> But then, well, the Reich declared war on the USA, they declared war on the Reich, all the Reich's enemies decided to put aside their differences and work together. And together, we won.<br /> <br /> Obviously, in this example, the Solars are the USA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-24-2019, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T01:54:13-08:00","id":1291456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291424#post1291424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">getting an MA style that lets you expand your fighting style a bit. You know who does that more easily with far less investment? Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it costs them 10xp instead of 8, so...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T02:43:24-08:00","id":1291470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a huge part of the reason why other splats don't get to combine MA with their native charms is because if they could, then absolutely every combat-oriented character would 100% want Martial Arts. Splitting them off ensures that you have to actually specialize in Martial Arts to get full benefit from it, and discourages a Melee character from grabbing one strong early MA charm purely for power reasons (because if you allow that, everyone will do it and MA will lose its unique meaning.) </div> </div> </div>I mean... maybe that's part of it, but that's not the main reason.<br /> <br /> The main reason is that they're just different abilities.<br /> <br /> When you roll Intelligence+Sail, you can't use Charisma or Archery charms. You can use Intelligence charms or Sail charms.<br /> <br /> When you roll Stamina+Resistance, you can't use Manipulation or Bureaucracy charms. You can use Stamina or Resistance charms.<br /> <br /> When you roll Dexterity+Brawl, you can't use Appearance or Melee charms. You can use Dexterity or Brawl.<br /> <br /> When you roll Dexterity+Martial Arts, you can't use Perception or Brawl charms. You can use Dexterity or Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> The special rule of Martial Arts isn't that you can't throw in other Abilities (why would you be able to? You can't use Melee on Brawl rolls).<br /> It's that some Martial Arts can be used to enhance Evasion, and can be comboed with Dodge.<br /> <br /> Other than that, it's rules as normal.<br /> <br /> Now, obviously I recognise that Lunars (and Alchemicals I guess, and some Exigents) are the only ones who have both Attribute and Ability charms, which gives them more options on a Dex+Martial Arts roll than a Solar, who only has Martial Arts charms.<br /> But I'm just saying, there is a mechanical reason that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291299#post1291299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem of &quot;Martial Arts are ridiculously good for Lunars&quot; isn't how it compares to other splats - part of the problem becomes &quot;is it ever reasonable to play a combat-oriented Lunar and <i>not</i> take Martial Arts?&quot; To me, that's a far more serious problem than dick-measuring contests between splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a very reasonable point.<br /> <br /> And it's kind of a point I made elsewhere, though in the opposite way.<br /> <br /> What I'm worried about, is that if you <i>don't</i> let Martial Arts work with native charms, then Martial Arts are a rubbish choice for Lunars.<br /> <br /> Native charms are cheaper, have the same overall power level (I think they include less really powerful effects, but less weak charms too; obviously this is a bit difficult to work out as we only have Dex, plus it's just difficult generally), and are just as combo-able (I mean you can combine most of the Dex tree with most of the Strength tree, just like you can combine all those unarmed styles).<br /> <br /> They also can be used with any weapon style. This means a)you have more tactical options, b)you can take Brawl, which you can also use in animal style, and c)you have a lot more options for evocations.<br /> <br /> Currently, I think that Martial Arts is not an auto-pick for Lunars.<br /> <br /> I think the combat builds are:<br /> Native charms including DBT for general accuracy/damage/defence<br /> Native charms for inflicting poison<br /> Native charms for ranged (some of these charms are the same as above, some are different)<br /> Native charms including DBT+Martial Arts<br /> Native charms focused on shapeshifting<br /> Native charms+Evocations<br /> Native charms+Martial Arts+Evocations (but it really only works in very specific combos. So far, the only way is Frost-Thorn Knuckles and Tiger, but there'll probably be a handful more when we get the artefacts from Fangs at the Gate)<br /> Native charms+Combat sorcery<br /> <br /> Looking at these, I don't think I would definitely choose Martial Arts. Admittedly, I did make a Lunar martial artist, but just because my concept of &quot;Snake-totem doctor who uses snake style&quot; is one I've had for a while.<br /> But I think there's plenty of other good options for combat. If I hadn't gone for Martial Arts, I think I'd have invested big in grappling and poison. Actually, I kind of want to invest in poison, but it doesn't really combo well with Snake's Martial Arts-produced poison, I think (we'll see; but Adder Fang Method doesn't. Nor do the Mutations). The ranged attack charms seem interesting (we'll see if Perception has more of them), and the Moonsilver Bow from the Core is just... well, OP, honestly. And there's always the traditional regenerating soak berzerker, though we'll see how good that is (I suspect... still good).<br /> Not to mention turning into a giant snake! Or a tiny, stealthy snake, to sneak up and bite people, though that's really just for the first round. (I can still do that, but I've only got Brawl 3, so it's not that great. If I wasn't into Snake Style, I'd have Brawl 5).<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, if, hypothetically, Martial Arts was the One True Build, then I would agree with you. But I don't think the Martial Arts charms are more powerful than Lunar native charms (which are cheaper), so there's no need to combine them when you can just take more native charms.<br /> <br /> Or, if you want to take Martial Arts because you can buy it with Lunar XP, well you could also spend that on all those mediocre Abilities you have, or Evocations.<br /> Because if you're not running DBT, and you're not into shapeshifting (and if you're into shapeshifting, you can't use MA anyway; spend your Lunar XP on latent abilities), then Evocations are a strong choice; the Resonant effects are, after all, kind of Solar-tier.<br /> <br /> In fact, there's a whole thread on this forum on shapeshifting and the powerful, efficient builds you can go for with it.<br /> <br /> Basically, as it is, I don't think Martial Arts is the One True Build for Lunars.<br /> And if they can't combo Native charms and Martial Arts, I think it will be the One Rubbish Build. You'll get the occasional Lunar using the more powerful offensive styles (Single Point, Righteous Devil) and just defending with Lunar charms anyway (the same way Single Point stylists parry with Melee, and Righteous Devils use Dodge), but not much in the way of Tiger, Snake, Crane... Monkey, Mantis, Centipede, Falcon, White Reaper...<br /> Ie the styles lots of Lunar characters should, genre-wise, be using.<br /> <br /> I mean, fluff players are going to play Tiger-totem Tiger-Stylist, it's just that they'll then find it's really not that good.<br /> <br /> <br /> As I said, I can accept that there may be certain combos of native charms+MA are broken. Snake Strikes the Heel with accuracy and re-roll charms is one Sandact6 brought up. Perhaps there are others. I suspect comboing Black Claw with Manipulation and Appearance charms is going to get brutal, though I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> But if we nerf Lunars by taking away all the combos (adding an extra layer of hassle to combat, incidentally), then we need to do something to make Martial Arts a viable choice for Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aquillon is the only one who's made a suggestion for this so far, which is Lunars should get to favour Martial Arts. I'd like to hear other people's suggestions, and I'd like them to consider that, if Lunars can't combine native charms and Martial Arts;<br /> What about excellencies?<br /> How come everyone else in the game gets to combine Martial Arts' Evasion-boosters and Soak-boosters, but not Lunars?<br /> Would you choose Martial Arts over those tasty Lunar charms?<br /> Which styles would you choose? Which styles wouldn't you choose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-24-2019, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T02:50:06-08:00","id":1291471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Losing out on animal form is a thing yes, but one of the problems of past editions was having One True Build Lunars, with DBT Lunars being a distant second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely DBT-Silver Claws-Moonsilver Carapace-Halting the Scarlet Flow <i>was</i> the One True Build?<br /> <br /> Two Full Moons in my party ran that, and they were basically unkillable. Once they fought each other, and after an hour neither of them had any damage, or were down any motes, so I had to say &quot;you fight for a day until you drop dead of exhaustion.&quot;<br /> <br /> They even beat Sidereals with Citrine Poxes of Contagion and Charcoal March of Spiders (Lunars are immune to the worst bad-touch effects anyway, and they had huge Sta+Res pools for all that poison and disease).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T02:56:06-08:00","id":1291473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291314#post1291314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Months and months ago, I pointed out this same idea in regards to Sorcery. Want to be a Lunar Sorcerer? No Tier 3 for you! (but you get Necromancy tier 2). So ok, the Lunar theme is &quot;versatility and occasional brute-forcing our shapeshifting abilities in contrast to Solars' Do Everything Awesomely style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Sorcery isn't relevant until the end of the game anyway.<br /> <br /> Vance was considering spells being 10xp each, which was a bigger problem, but after playtesting they kept it at 8xp if you favour Intelligence.<br /> <br /> But saying this, Lunar sorcery doesn't really have any competition in the Lunar charmset anyway. I don't think anyone's going to say &quot;Lunar sorcerers are chumps, I'm going to take completely different Intelligence charms&quot; because, well, those charms make you good at completely different things.<br /> <br /> If you want to summon monsters to serve you, sorcery's the only way to go about it.<br /> <br /> Whereas if you want to be really good at fighting, there's a variety of different ways to do it, which do need to be somewhat comparable (each with advantages and disadvantages of course, but overall roughly the same level).<br /> <br /> <br /> Either way, they went with favoured costs for sorcery. And you can combo it with native charms (like excellencies, not to mention the sorcery-specific charms).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T03:49:30-08:00","id":1291484,"title":"","content":"I think the Lunar vs Solar martial artist issue only really comes about when you isolate it to a single style, in which case sure by comboing lunar dex charms and MA charms the lunar will outperform the solar offensively who can only use those styles charms to atttack, but MA styles have short charm trees anyway so if you wanna be the pinnacle of solar martial arts you should have some other styles anyway, which the lunar wouldn't have because they bought dex charms instead.<br /> <br /> Having said that I do see two main issues, firstly there is a risk of particularly broken combo's and i can see the potential problems with having a looming shadow over every future MA style. The second issue is that MA seems like way too an attractive lunar exp dump for any combat orientated character, yeah they could could make themselves better rounded with ability investments but most combat characters tend to focus on anything that makes them better at killing imo. Being able to combo native and MA charms just kinda makes it a no brainer as there is literally no drawback to grabbing some with your &quot;spare&quot; exp and is gonna make you always better than a non-MA combat lunar because you have all the same charms plus some more.<br /> <br /> The best solution seems to be to limit the the comboing to defensive charms only, the same as other exalted, although its as inelegant as crap and would involve keywording every combat charm in the book (personally id just houserule it either way but i know people like an official stance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T11:38:50-08:00","id":1291567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291470#post1291470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, obviously I recognise that Lunars (and Alchemicals I guess, and some Exigents) are the only ones who have both Attribute and Ability charms, which gives them more options on a Dex+Martial Arts roll than a Solar, who only has Martial Arts charms.<br /> But I'm just saying, there is a mechanical reason that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I originally had my Alchemical homebrew to make Alchemicals use MA's and their native charms like Lunars could. I tested the entire set for nearly four years. Do you know what I discovered? Nearly everything outlined in my opening post. Even IF MA charms cost 10 XP a pop it was still very well worth it for them, even when I removed such things as charm attunement costs and slots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Charms are a rubbish choice for Lunars then! </div> </div> </div>So does that make people who choose MA as their primary combat style idiots? After all your native charms are often stronger and more flexible. Even for Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> I'm also utterly amazed that you think I'm suggesting an all or nothing type deal here. Let's say that Lunars would get the same deal others would on MA. Let's say they can use their defense charms for Dodge only and their Resistance-ish/soak charms also work just fine. The same deal with Solars. What breaks?<br /> <br /> We get a charmset which gives Lunars potentially more or unique methods of fighting, some of which cannot be done in their native set.<br /> <br /> What utter horror. You're now on the same level as everyone else.<br /> <br /> The tradeoffs of whenever or not these things would be as good if not better than your native charms? You'd have to make the same decisions like every other splat in the game decides to take martial arts. And no, lack of the mastery keyword doesn't overly and automatically make the style's instantly useless. They still have pretty damn solid effects for the most part that should make a person consider their cost over native charms.<br /> <br /> I do not consider the 10 XP per charm of MA that big of a deal either, but if forced you could make either DEX or STR count as buying MA charms favored depending on the style (DEX for Finesse based, STR for power based styles).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291470#post1291470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if, hypothetically, Martial Arts was the One True Build, then I would agree with you. But I don't think the Martial Arts charms are more powerful than Lunar native charms (which are cheaper), so there's no need to combine them when you can just take more native charms.<br /> <br /> Or, if you want to take Martial Arts because you can buy it with Lunar XP, well you could also spend that on all those mediocre Abilities you have, or Evocations.<br /> Because if you're not running DBT, and you're not into shapeshifting (and if you're into shapeshifting, you can't use MA anyway; spend your Lunar XP on latent abilities), then Evocations are a strong choice; the Resonant effects are, after all, kind of Solar-tier.<br /> <br /> In fact, there's a whole thread on this forum on shapeshifting and the powerful, efficient builds you can go for with it.<br /> <br /> Basically, as it is, I don't think Martial Arts is the One True Build for Lunars.<br /> And if they can't combo Native charms and Martial Arts, I think it will be the One Rubbish Build. You'll get the occasional Lunar using the more powerful offensive styles (Single Point, Righteous Devil) and just defending with Lunar charms anyway (the same way Single Point stylists parry with Melee, and Righteous Devils use Dodge), but not much in the way of Tiger, Snake, Crane... Monkey, Mantis, Centipede, Falcon, White Reaper...<br /> Ie the styles lots of Lunar characters should, genre-wise, be using.<br /> <br /> I mean, fluff players are going to play Tiger-totem Tiger-Stylist, it's just that they'll then find it's really not that good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again you're doing an excluded middle here. Lunar charms that work with currently established paradigms (EX: Allowing Defense charms to work with dodge and access to soak charms) are things I have little problems with. Even if we expanded them to parry then the only style that becomes aggravating is Crane so one of out all the MA's having this issue is a pretty good metric.<br /> <br /> But again some people don't want to do that. Some people would think that Laughing Monster fits their backstory perfectly. We don't know for sure, but let's say Laughing Monster cannot combine with shapeshifting (You never know with unreleased material). Should that person be laughed at for not picking the better battle build of shapeshifting? Do we laugh at Solars picking MA over one of the four combat abilities? After all, the core charmset for Solars are going to be better than whatever MA can do even with the tricks MA can do.<br /> <br /> And what the heck are you going on about. Crane, Snake, and White Reaper are amazing styles even without their mastery keywords. They don't get to the utter bullshit that Righteous Devil or Single Point can pull off but they're fairly respectable styles in their own right. Do you know how many people would give their left nut to be able to make reflexive counterattacks all day? Do you know how useful Snake is for allowing you to end most battles without ever needing to reset init? White Reaper having fairly solid all around charms even without using the halos on the form?<br /> <br /> Yes, I think they're definately things a Lunar would pick without them feeling as if they were kicked in the nuts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291470#post1291470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if we nerf Lunars by taking away all the combos (adding an extra layer of hassle to combat, incidentally), then we need to do something to make Martial Arts a viable choice for Lunars.<br /> <br /> Aquillon is the only one who's made a suggestion for this so far, which is Lunars should get to favour Martial Arts. I'd like to hear other people's suggestions, and I'd like them to consider that, if Lunars can't combine native charms and Martial Arts;<br /> What about excellencies?<br /> How come everyone else in the game gets to combine Martial Arts' Evasion-boosters and Soak-boosters, but not Lunars?<br /> Would you choose Martial Arts over those tasty Lunar charms?<br /> Which styles would you choose? Which styles wouldn't you choose?</div> </div> </div> </div>My immediate thoughts:<ul><li>Having Lunar defense charms work with Dodge defense only and stack soak as normal. Every other splat gets this, I wouldn't exclude Lunars.</li> <li>Excellencies will work for Lunars and MA the same way as any other ability does.</li> <li>Have DEX/STR favor specific MA's depending on type as mentioned above. I figure this even makes sense as DEX Lunars will need to branch into STR for most damage adders with their natural charms and STR Lunars will need some DEX for finesse charms anyways.</li> <li>Depending on the style and the character I might have in mind? Absolutely.</li> <li>Virtually any of the MA styles are good picks. The only one I wouldn't pick is Steel Devil as lol Steel Devil.</li> </ul><br /> If you want other ways of fixing this then I have others that leap to my mind.<ul><li>Allow every splat to combo their native charms and MA's. Some things break (Single Point and Righteous Devil) but largely everyone will be in the same playing field in terms of balance and fairness. Do the current devs want to do this? Who knows. Would they be barred from doing so even if they wanted? Absolutely, because a charm letting Lunars attack with STR exist as a workaround.</li> <li>Continue the current status quo and let Lunars practice their MA's and native charms together. In exchange people can infinitely expand MA styles as if they were ability charms. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1276727-the-expanded-lotus-padoru-preview-expanded-ma-homebrew\">Of course no one would be stupid enough to do this.</a></li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T12:58:51-08:00","id":1291581,"title":"","content":"Hey, I got an idea but I'm not sure how great it is. Give lunars a surcharge for combining native charms with martial arts styles that require specific weapons.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's any coincidence that Single Point Shining Into the Void and Righteous Devil are two of the strongest styles in the game. I wager the developers knew that since these were locked behind specific weapons you can't combine them freely with the dozens of other martial arts out there to increase their output or cover gaps in the style, and so they needed to be strong enough to stand on their own without relying on outside elements. Any seriously broken combinations I can see are probably going to come from those two (with steel devil honestly just needing another pass)<br /> <br /> Most of the other potentially troublesome things you listed seem kinda trivial. Snake Strikes the Heel has a willpower cost so it's not something you can spam as you please, and has the additional factor of withering clashes not giving you any initiative and so at best is damage control for an incoming decisive, and spending a bunch of motes to do that doesn't seem busted at all, and the decisive version can only be used on gambits.<br /> Crane style doesn't have any native penalty negators for parry specifically, since that's what you're using for defend other, but I don't see anything stopping it from combining with dodge charms if you just full defense every round. <br /> And the short range boosting from Dreaming Pearl Courtesan is something you can already add to with any existing martial art, so I don't actually see how this is a lunar specific problem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:04:50-08:00","id":1291583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291364#post1291364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they are and it's represented as Solar Brawl. An non-formalized set of abilities which give solars powerful unarmed techniques. Which isn't Martial Arts but I guess that distinction only matters to the person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars have to choose between MA and Brawl. Is your intent that MA should be a strictly weaker option for them, in combat?<br /> <br /> What about if a Solar martial artist has a Sidereal tutor? The Sidereal trains them diligently, even passing on the forbidden techniques of Sidereal Martial Arts; then the Solar has a duel with an equally-experienced master of Solar Brawl. Do you believe the Solar Martial Artist (with a Sidereal tutor, which is supposed to be a huge deal!) should be at a disadvantage against the master of Brawl?<br /> <br /> There isn't an easy answer to this! It's haunted Martial Arts, SMA, Sidereals, and Solars since 1e. There's a lot of contradictory requirements, and it seems like you're only considering some of them:<br /> <br /> 1. Sidereal Martial Arts is the distinctive top-shelf combat ability of the Sidereal Exalted. They need to be (in some way) uniquely good at it. Having a Solar come along and (even with a Sidereal tutor) use your very best combat powers exactly the way you do is lame.<br /> <br /> 2. At the same time, Sidereals are also peerless teachers of martial arts, and their ability to pass on Sidereal Martial Arts to Solars exemplifies this. Learning SMA from a Sidereal should be a Big Deal for a Solar's development. I don't think it's sufficient for it to just add more options (Evocations, Sorcery, and CMA already add options), at least if those options are going to be noticeably weaker than Solar Brawl. Having a Sidereal tutor should be a character-defining thing for a Solar.<br /> <br /> 3. Solars are, on average, a bit better at combat than Sidereals, <i>even when the Sidereal is using SMA</i> (although in the modern day, Sidereal SMA masters tend to be massively more experienced than any Solar and will have a sharp advantage over them due to that.) SMA allows Sidereals to cheat in various ways - it's like one of the more cheaty Jojo's Bizarre Adventure stands - so &quot;advantage&quot; is a nebulous term here, but it's always been part of the game's design.<br /> <br /> 4. The combination of 1 + 3 means that a Solar who practices Sidereal Martial Arts really shouldn't be better at it than a Sidereal (or even use it <i>identically</i> to a Sidereal.) The combination of 2+3 means that a Solar who uses Sidereal Martial Arts has to be at least comparable in power to a Solar whose combat skill took a different path, though... and that &quot;typical&quot; Solar is a bit stronger than an equally experienced Sidereal. These things contradict each other.<br /> <br /> Of course there's some ways around this. A Solar's power can be represented by more motes, larger dice pools, better &quot;engine&quot; charms from their native charmset, and so on. For example, if the defenses offered by Sidereal Martial Arts tend to, overall, not be quite as good as its offense or utility - ie. more on par with native Sidereal charms, while the other charms in SMA tend to be better than native Sidereal charms - a Sidereal using SMA will remain somewhat fragile compared to a Solar. Then you can even give Sidereals flavorful Sutra effects that emphasize attack or utility while keeping their glass cannon theme.<br /> <br /> Another consideration is how Sidereals access Mastery benefits - I suspect that they'll get them in some way, but they may have to jump through some hoops rather than just getting them the way a Solar does. This could create a gap to give Sidereals those unique Sutra benefits, while keeping SMA as a reasonable option for combat oriented Solars. (This doesn't even require Mastery benefits in SMA, which could lead to issues with requirement 1 - Solars can benefit from easier access to normal MA Mastery benefits, and combine these stronger baseline MAs with SMA. But this requires some caution, because you still want SMA to be something that Solars <i>want</i> per point 2.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:13:23-08:00","id":1291587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291470#post1291470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aquillon is the only one who's made a suggestion for this so far, which is Lunars should get to favour Martial Arts. I'd like to hear other people's suggestions, and I'd like them to consider that, if Lunars can't combine native charms and Martial Arts;<br /> What about excellencies?<br /> How come everyone else in the game gets to combine Martial Arts' Evasion-boosters and Soak-boosters, but not Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>You asked for other people's suggestions, but I have another one!<br /> <br /> Specific charms can be whitelisted to work with MA. This is a much &quot;safer&quot; option, mechanically, than whitelisting everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Allow every splat to combo their native charms and MA's. Some things break (Single Point and Righteous Devil) but largely everyone will be in the same playing field in terms of balance and fairness. </div> </div> </div>The issue with this is that allowing unlimited cross-ability combination makes it really hard to balance future charms. Already, with Lunars, this change means that all new MA charms need to consider how they play with every single Lunar charm; spreading it to everyone would make the problem worse. This is another reason the restriction existed in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:29:49-08:00","id":1291590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291583#post1291583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars have to choose between MA and Brawl. Is your intent that MA should be a strictly weaker option for them, in combat?<br /> <br /> What about if a Solar martial artist has a Sidereal tutor? The Sidereal trains them diligently, even passing on the forbidden techniques of Sidereal Martial Arts; then the Solar has a duel with an equally-experienced master of Solar Brawl. Do you believe the Solar Martial Artist (with a Sidereal tutor, which is supposed to be a huge deal!) should be at a disadvantage against the master of Brawl?<br /> <br /> There isn't an easy answer to this! It's haunted Martial Arts, SMA, Sidereals, and Solars since 1e. There's a lot of contradictory requirements, and it seems like you're only considering some of them:</div> </div> </div> </div>In previous editions, solars still got hosed for getting SMA. Yes, they could use them but without sutra benefits they were impractical and too costly to use out of a few charms. More motes didn't matter when you were afflicted by willpower and mote loss. I don't know if it'll be this way but there's a distinct difference between sidereals having to jump through hoops and solars just not getting sutra effects. Even with native charms. Brawl and Martial arts are also two different beasts and I don't know where SMA factors into this. Almost no Solar is going to get SMA, they can't pass it on nor can the create them themselves they can only learn it from sidereals, so it'd be better not to treat it as Solar MA's end all be all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-24-2019, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:15:05-08:00","id":1291607,"title":"","content":"That's kind of a suboptimal thing from previous editions where the best Solar is clearly the guy who buys Melee, and there wasn't really much commitment to expecting much else, so it didn't really matter and no one cared too much, while 3e is intended to support a more diverse panel of Solar specialists.<br /> <br /> That said, I thought the meta was that Solars were already supposed to be very viable and comparable with Celestial Martial Arts against a Brawl / Melee specialist already in 3e? If so, they don't really *need* a power boost from SMA, and also probably shouldn't get one (as Solar with SMA overpowering a Brawl Solar is at least as bad as underpowering them!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:18:15-08:00","id":1291608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291590#post1291590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous editions, solars still got hosed for getting SMA. Yes, they could use them but without sutra benefits they were impractical and too costly to use out of a few charms. More motes didn't matter when you were afflicted by willpower and mote loss. I don't know if it'll be this way but there's a distinct difference between sidereals having to jump through hoops and solars just not getting sutra effects. Even with native charms. Brawl and Martial arts are also two different beasts and I don't know where SMA factors into this. Almost no Solar is going to get SMA, they can't pass it on nor can the create them themselves they can only learn it from sidereals, so it'd be better not to treat it as Solar MA's end all be all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Appealing to the mechanics of older editions should not be how we decide on the best options for this one. In previous editions, a deathlord could just execute any of their deathknights at a moments notice. This was an awful mechanic, and isn't going to be returning. We are not bound by the specific mechanics of past editions.<br /> <br /> Any solar who cares about MA and knows sidereals is going to be giving serious thought to SMA. It's the ultimate peak of martial arts, how can you state as if its a fact the bizarre notion that solars - people driven, explicitly, to reach as high and far as they can - aren't going to be enticed by these mystical techniques? With how much of Exalted is rooted in Wuxia, this is a ridiculous notion. Furthermore, the people PLAYING exalted are going to go &quot;Holy shit, this MA lets me phase through walls and punch people into trees!&quot; (or whatever Charcoal March of Spiders ends up looking like, SMA were notoriously busted) and they will want to get these on their solar to use them. Hell I can think of a half-dozen PCs from games I've been in or ran that would grab SMA in a heartbeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:20:35-08:00","id":1291609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291607#post1291607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of a suboptimal thing from previous editions where the best Solar is clearly the guy who buys Melee, and there wasn't really much commitment to expecting much else, so it didn't really matter and no one cared too much, while 3e is intended to support a more diverse panel of Solar specialists.<br /> <br /> That said, I thought the meta was that Solars were already supposed to be very viable and comparable with Celestial Martial Arts against a Brawl / Melee specialist already in 3e? If so, they don't really *need* a power boost from SMA, and also probably shouldn't get one (as Solar with SMA overpowering a Brawl Solar is at least as bad as underpowering them!).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a balancing concern for WHEN they get it, not something to determine IF they get it. It's right there in the corebook. The solars can learn SMA and use them just as well as the sidereals can. They require a sidereal sifu, so hell it ain't easy to get them, but they can and will.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:24:47-08:00","id":1291610,"title":"","content":"Sure, but I'm replying to Aquillion's point about there being a problem if Solar MA are weaker than Solar Brawl, and SMA are not there to 'make up the gap', as it were.<br /> <br /> If there's no gap to be made up, there's not really that same problem if Solars get no significant boost from SMA and aren't really more effective with them (or are even less effective with them in straight up combat than they are with Celestial MA, their less esoteric and therefore more stylistically appropriate form of MA).<br /> <br /> (I mean, perhaps it could be a problem inasmuch as fealty to a single line in the corebook could be concerned, but I'm less bothered about that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:57:24-08:00","id":1291623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291587#post1291587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specific charms can be whitelisted to work with MA. This is a much &quot;safer&quot; option, mechanically, than whitelisting everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:05:43-08:00","id":1291626,"title":"","content":"You don't actually need to whitelist anything, if you think about it. Evasion is dex+dodge/2, you don't use MA to evade. Resistance effects are the same, they don't involve MA. All you have to do in fact is just say they can't use their native charms on MA attacks and parry. That's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:21:19-08:00","id":1291631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291609#post1291609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a balancing concern for WHEN they get it, not something to determine IF they get it. It's right there in the corebook. The solars can learn SMA and use them just as well as the sidereals can. They require a sidereal sifu, so hell it ain't easy to get them, but they can and will.</div> </div> </div> </div>They explicitly cannot use them as well as sidereals. It's a setting facet that's been around since the first edition and it's jot getting changed this one. SMA has always been a bunch of unique but mixed bag that completely needs sutras to be usable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:56:55-08:00","id":1291639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291323#post1291323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should it not be that different, exactly? What part of the setting suggests this? Was the first age just the age of Twilights? Are they the only caste allowed to be significant in-setting? The jade prison just broke, and 30 dawns - THIRTY dawns are returning to the world, and they are just as important and just as threatening to the status quo as those 30 twilights or 30 zeniths. They are not &quot;a full moon but a little better&quot;, they are the greatest at what they do, to such a degree that their release is the defining moment of the era. Lunars are not a splat about being Fighters, with solars as Wizards. Lunars can socialise and wield sorcery very well. Just think about how bizarre this argument is. It's not a problem at all that solars can break a man's will with the force of their speech or call upon Ligier to walk Creation for the first time in 2 millenia, but when combat prowess is mentioned, suddenly there's a great shuffling of paper and tugging of beards and &quot;well, I suppose we can let them be a teensy bit stronger than a full moon is, maybe&quot;. We've come so far from DnD, but people are still stuck in a mindset that combat prowess = how important you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solars coming back is a<i> really</i> big thing but you are kind of overselling them here. They aren't single handedly overturning the entire status quote while everyone stares on in helpless awe unable to do anything in the face of their might. Shit has hit the fan in a lot of different ways in a very short period of time and as mighty as they are solars can't claim credit for a lot of it. The Scarlet Empress has vanished and with her gone the vast majority of the settings dragon blooded have turned their efforts to playing Game of Thrones as the White Walkers lick their chops, the Deathlords and their Deathknights have begun to move (including using a mountain sized maggot riddled abomination to conquer Thorns), the Bronze Faction are in a tizzy because their leader is about to kick the bucket as he reaches at last the end of a sidereal's extremely long life span right as their greatest asset in maintaining dragon blooded rule is falling to in fighting, the Yozi are doing something or another with the infernal exalted that hasn't been elaborated on yet, etc.<br /> <br /> And shit hitting the fan aside they are also going to be building on the efforts other exalts have been making while they were gone like the Lunars taking chunks out of the Realm and Sidereals, Rakan Thulio rounding up a posse and declaring war on Heaven, the Gold Faction sidereal having happened to already been setting up a ready made cult and otherwise being eager to assist them in their efforts, and etc.<br /> <br /> TLDR: There is a lot going on that makes it possible for Solars to currently have a huge chance of making huge setting shaking changes and its not them being OP super exalts that nobody else is able to even remotely compete with in any way like it was in 2 ED. They are the strongest but its not such a huge margin that other exalts might as well just stop showing up to work because the <i>real</i> exalts are back now and its going to be their way or the highway. If they were really <i>that</i> great then how did they get dunked on at the absolute height of their power in the first place and chucked into the Jade Prison despite having a bunch of the Lunars on their side and all the resources and wonders of the First Age at their beck and call (and there being 300 of them instead of getting cut in half to donate to the creation of Abyssal and Infernal exalts)?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Appealing to the mechanics of older editions should not be how we decide on the best options for this one. In previous editions, a deathlord could just execute any of their deathknights at a moments notice. This was an awful mechanic, and isn't going to be returning. We are not bound by the specific mechanics of past editions.<br /> <br /> Any solar who cares about MA and knows sidereals is going to be giving serious thought to SMA. It's the ultimate peak of martial arts, how can you state as if its a fact the bizarre notion that solars - people driven, explicitly, to reach as high and far as they can - aren't going to be enticed by these mystical techniques? With how much of Exalted is rooted in Wuxia, this is a ridiculous notion. Furthermore, the people PLAYING exalted are going to go &quot;Holy shit, this MA lets me phase through walls and punch people into trees!&quot; (or whatever Charcoal March of Spiders ends up looking like, SMA were notoriously busted) and they will want to get these on their solar to use them. Hell I can think of a half-dozen PCs from games I've been in or ran that would grab SMA in a heartbeat. </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters they are going to have to find a Sidereal that is willing to even consider teaching it to them then convince them to go for it. Though I guess some STs are going to make that easier then others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-24-2019, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T16:17:18-08:00","id":1291648,"title":"","content":"Not sure if that was excessive or not but I just really hate the idea of us ever even remotely going near the old 2E standard of 'only solars or things made by tweaking a solar exaltation matter nobody else can compete and how the hell did they lose in the first place then but please try to ignore that plot hole'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T17:18:48-08:00","id":1291658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291648#post1291648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if that was excessive or not but I just really hate the idea of us ever even remotely going near the old 2E standard of 'only solars or things made by tweaking a solar exaltation matter nobody else can compete and how the hell did they lose in the first place then but please try to ignore that plot hole'</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. Most of the answer to Clownpiece seems off topic to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:27:53-08:00","id":1291688,"title":"","content":"Going off topic is a proud forum tradition when lunars are involved.<br /> <br /> But on topic, I'd think we should wait to see the strength and stamina charms first before we really get into how good being able to combo native charms and martial arts are. But I trust the current set of Devs to make it pretty balanced compared to the advantages other splats get when they use martial arts. Apparently the reason they can't use them in animal forms was because play testing made it clear that it was broken (I guess from some protean advantages received from using charms in animal form?) so they are definitely looking out for that kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:32:07-08:00","id":1291693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291688#post1291688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going off topic is a proud forum tradition when lunars are involved.<br /> <br /> But on topic, I'd think we should wait to see the strength and stamina charms first before we really get into how good being able to combo native charms and martial arts are. But I trust the current set of Devs to make it pretty balanced compared to the advantages other splats get when they use martial arts. Apparently the reason they can't use them in animal forms was because play testing made it clear that it was broken (I guess from some protean advantages received from using charms in animal form?) so they are definitely looking out for that kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real issue is seeing what options Lunars have. There only seems to be two. Animals with DBT, or MA with DBT or evocations, or ranged with evocations unless DBT can't be used with MA in which case it does add more complexity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:39:54-08:00","id":1291694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RosePlancton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291658#post1291658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know. Most of the answer to Clownpiece seems off topic to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's probably worth saying in context to the thread. Clownpiece was saying that one of the narrative purpose of the Solar Exalted is to return and tip the balance of the world to either salvation or destruction. They do this because their power is so much greater than anyone else's in the setting at the moment. Just look at Solar Circle Sorcery as an example. Since it is totally unfair that sorcerers are the only people who get to have that kind of impact and everyone else is a chump, Dawns must be similarly more powerful, and the combat rules should support this. That's why Solars need to be as much better at fighting as Ligier is more powerful than Octavian.<br /> <br /> <br /> Except that's all built off of a series of shaky setting conceits that are mostly propped up by bad 2e ideas. Firstly, Sorcery actually IS a very special thing, that's why it's the only thing in the whole game that a Supernal ability does not give you access to. You need to be Essence 5 to summon Ligier, no shortcuts. Judging by the essence values of characters we have seen, it will take decades at least, or, more likely, centuries for a Solar to reach that point. So if Solars are going to tip the balance NOW they need to do it without even knowledge of celestial circle sorcery.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that summoning Ligier is an insanely dangrous task that shouldn't even be attempted by an Essence 1 Solar if they did have access to it. You need to make a (Wits + Occult) roll against his Resolve, and Occult does not have tricky non-charm dice adders or ways to lower resolve for this like the social trees do. If you fail this roll on a third circle summoning, you do not get the chance to banish the demon back to Hell like you do with lesser spirits. If you flub that very difficult roll, Ligier has been unleashed unbound upon the world.<br /> <br /> So, you see, the ability to summon Ligier should not be the measuring stick of Solar power. The rest of Solar Sorcery isn't even that much more powerful than Celestial. Rain of Doom can destroy a city but Cantana of Empty Voices can kill everyone inside it so it's not like an insane step up in power.<br /> <br /> <br /> But that's actually okay, because Solars don't NEED to be able to summon Ligier to tip the scales. They are more powerful fighters than Full Moons, better sorcerers than No Moons, etcetera, but not by an insane degree, and certainly not more powerful than a lot of current Lunars. Leviathan would roll any Essence 1 Dawn. That's okay though, the introduction of 60 Dawn/Dusk/Slayers into the world is a huge deal anyway. The scale is ripe to be tipped in any direction, and even the introduction of 60 new Sidereals or Lunars would do it, but Solars are even more powerful than that!<br /> <br /> So if Lunars end up being almost as good as Solars at using MA, especially if it's in their own unique ways, then that's totally fine. Lunars do not need to suck at MA compared to Solars. What we should be looking at is does the combination of Lunar charms and MA break the game, or become too powerful. We've accepted that comboing MAs and native charms with Evocations and sorcery can work, so maybe this is okay. Or maybe there's some effects that things like dicecaps and Simple charms just make easy to balance. Or maybe neither of those things and we should petition the developers to maybe change it? I'm still undecided, I'll make a chapter about it in my personal review thread at the end of the KS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291693#post1291693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The real issue is seeing what options Lunars have. There only seems to be two. Animals with DBT, or MA with DBT or evocations, or ranged with evocations unless DBT can't be used with MA in which case it does add more complexity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like to offer that Strength charms might be more slanted towards melee fighting than dexterity, if for no other reason than the incorrect-but-genre-accepted notion that dexterity is for range and strength is for melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-24-2019, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:58:10-08:00","id":1291700,"title":"","content":"I don't think that'll be the case. The ranged dex trees seem kind of lacking. At the very least, outside of the projectile attacks most of the moves worked for both ranged and melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T20:02:12-08:00","id":1291701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291700#post1291700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that'll be the case. The ranged dex trees seem kind of lacking. At the very least, outside of the projectile attacks most of the moves worked for both ranged and melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, interesting. So why the idea that ranged is much better than melee?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T20:15:10-08:00","id":1291704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291701#post1291701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, interesting. So why the idea that ranged is much better than melee?</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that ranged is it's own concept. I think the only MA it combines with is rightous devil but if I remember correctly, combining those charms gets expensive fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T20:23:36-08:00","id":1291706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291704#post1291704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that ranged is it's own concept. I think the only MA it combines with is rightous devil but if I remember correctly, combining those charms gets expensive fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes. Also I've been told that RD is a very broken style to begin with so if that's true then maybe it's not so bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T21:38:35-08:00","id":1291719,"title":"","content":"As someone who worked on Attribute exalts a lot I'll chime in.<br /> <br /> The reason why ranged attacks are lacking is because... most of your charms work with ranged attacks and close-up combat. Aside from the range extenders there isn't many vanilla effects beyond that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T00:52:09-08:00","id":1291741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291648#post1291648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if that was excessive or not but I just really hate the idea of us ever even remotely going near the old 2E standard of 'only solars or things made by tweaking a solar exaltation matter nobody else can compete and how the hell did they lose in the first place then but please try to ignore that plot hole'</div> </div> </div> </div>See, though, that's not what I'm arguing for in the slightest. I'm talking about things going the OTHER way - the usurpation becoming a joke because, well, of course they lost, they're only a tiny bit better than anyone else after all. The usurpation was, as I see it, a genuinely heroic act by the dragonblooded and sidereals. It was the right thing to do. The solars weren't just mad with power, they were mad with power and better than everyone else, and that's terrifying! All the worst of humanity magnified to such a degree that it was going to destroy the world. The usurpation was necessary and very very hard to pull off, and came at immense cost as the world was forever diminished, but they pulled it off. Now this power is suddenly, all in one moment, unleashed again into the world. This is the defining moment of the era. 2E was not a bad setting because solars were the only ones allowed to be important (actually solars were very dull in it too. 2E was, in every sense, the Infernals edition of Exalted) it was a bad setting because it tried to reduce a world of mystery, magic and human struggles down to the dullest explanations possible, and turn a game that should be about the three kingdoms and sengoku jidai and nights master into essence 8 clowns hitting each other with magitech balloons. Solars were untouchable because of shitty mechanics, but even if they weren't it would have still been a bad edition, and it does not mean the answer is to cut them down to size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T01:13:28-08:00","id":1291742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291639#post1291639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TLDR: There is a lot going on that makes it possible for Solars to currently have a huge chance of making huge setting shaking changes and its not them being OP super exalts that nobody else is able to even remotely compete with in any way like it was in 2 ED. They are the strongest but its not such a huge margin that other exalts might as well just stop showing up to work because the <i>real</i> exalts are back now and its going to be their way or the highway. If they were really <i>that</i> great then how did they get dunked on at the absolute height of their power in the first place and chucked into the Jade Prison despite having a bunch of the Lunars on their side and all the resources and wonders of the First Age at their beck and call (and there being 300 of them instead of getting cut in half to donate to the creation of Abyssal and Infernal exalts)?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, see, you're working backwards here. You're missing one of the most important things in the setting, actually. That tyranny gets toppled in the end. The primordials (or &quot;enemies of the gods&quot;, now, not that theres any problems with getting away from the bizarre primordial focus of older editions) made Creation. They made it all. Humanity, the gods, the elemental dragons, every little blade of grass or raiton was theirs to make and rule. And the exalted beat them. This was not a war they had a good chance of winning. In fact, they had a very slim chance of winning it at all - but they won. And then everyone turned to look at the solars, the best amongst them, and said &quot;Yep! These guys should be in charge&quot; because hey, isn't the best option to have the best people in charge? And it did work, for a while, but they never stopped being human. A human life stretched out of over thousands of years, driven to challenge itself and losing anything to challenge... the Great Curse is kind of an excuse by the developers, really. It's something put in to stop you cheating and saying &quot;but MY solar wouldnt be like that, they wouldnt be corrupt or mad!&quot; because without the Great Curse that's what the majority of players would have done. Anyway, the world is now ruled by tyrants that, each and every one of them, is immensely, earth-shatteringly powerful. The dragonblooded and sidereals still rose up against them. And beat them. They didn't have a big chance of doing so. They very, very easily could have lost completely and then that's it, the world is doomed forever. Now they're in charge, and while they aren't as bad as the solars before them, they are still corrupt tyrants, that no-one has been able to stop from ruling the world. Oh shit, guess who just broke out of the jade prison?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T01:44:51-08:00","id":1291747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291648#post1291648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if that was excessive or not but I just really hate the idea of us ever even remotely going near the old 2E standard of 'only solars or things made by tweaking a solar exaltation matter nobody else can compete and how the hell did they lose in the first place then but please try to ignore that plot hole'</div> </div> </div> </div>Without the intention of saying or implying that you shouldn't have posted that, I don't disagree with the spirit of it, the reason I tried to restrain myself from something similar is that, really, for the 7 or so years 3e has publicly been in development and publishing, it's already been a solved problem. <br /> <br /> The developers and all the community in general has come to a pretty decent understanding of where proper balance is, which includes Solars being very directly powerful in an area of specialism, and feeling like the can genuinely be called &quot;the mightiest&quot;, but also a setting that's intended to be replete with challenges to them, and NPCs with lots of agency and potential as allies and rivals.<br /> <br /> So when we've come to that, it feels a bit like, what's the point of re-running those 2008-2012 arguments again? Where the Solars are emphasised as being in a categorically different tier of power from arguments that were purported to be rooted in the making the setting's history of Usurpation and Wyld Hunt and the themes of the Solar Exalted and game setting make sense, but were actually rooted on, or heavily conditional to, the weak or poorly playtested core mechanical assumptions of 2e?<br /> <br /> Especially when those have the potential to eat a thread where Sandact is trying to do something productive about mechanics which are still in the works, and could potentially make a difference there. Usurpation and power tier topics eat threads like the Lunars in-joke we'll probably never have to make again, now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T01:51:12-08:00","id":1291750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291742#post1291742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, see, you're working backwards here. You're missing one of the most important things in the setting, actually. That tyranny gets toppled in the end. The primordials (or &quot;enemies of the gods&quot;, now, not that theres any problems with getting away from the bizarre primordial focus of older editions) made Creation. They made it all. Humanity, the gods, the elemental dragons, every little blade of grass or raiton was theirs to make and rule. And the exalted beat them. This was not a war they had a good chance of winning. In fact, they had a very slim chance of winning it at all - but they won.<u><b> And then everyone turned to look at the solars, the best amongst them, and said &quot;Yep! These guys should be in charge&quot;</b></u> because hey, isn't the best option to have the best people in charge? And it did work, for a while, but they never stopped being human. A human life stretched out of over thousands of years, driven to challenge itself and losing anything to challenge... the Great Curse is kind of an excuse by the developers, really. It's something put in to stop you cheating and saying &quot;but MY solar wouldnt be like that, they wouldnt be corrupt or mad!&quot; because without the Great Curse that's what the majority of players would have done. Anyway, the world is now ruled by tyrants that, each and every one of them, is immensely, earth-shatteringly powerful. The dragonblooded and sidereals still rose up against them. And beat them. They didn't have a big chance of doing so. They very, very easily could have lost completely and then that's it, the world is doomed forever. Now they're in charge, and while they aren't as bad as the solars before them, they are still corrupt tyrants, that no-one has been able to stop from ruling the world. Oh shit, guess who just broke out of the jade prison?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is most definitely not a thing in 3rd edition, though. What we have been told of the first age makes a ton of mentions to various civil wars among the chosen in the age of dreams. And what we have been told doesn't make it seem like it was just solar lead factions exclusively like it was in 2nd edition that were taking part in the fighting. In particular the back story of the solar-lunar bond from the first lunar preview explicitly mentions a <i>lunar lead</i> coalition going to war with a faction lead by a solar trying to claim dibs on ruling Creation by dint of being the last living high general from when the host was united against the creators and the fight ended in the sides calling truce instead of lunar defeat (with the bond being a sort of political marriage made to seal the deal). It also mentions in a different part of the preview that lunars actively countered the solar portion of the deliberative from collecting too much power to themselves so even in the final dream of the first age solars weren't in <i>complete</i> control (though it also implies they did have the most still of any host). Hardly the kind of stuff that would be going on if everyone just meekly agreed 'yeah solars are totes the best lets just do what they say like good little 2nd rates'.<br /> <br /> Edit: Didn't see that other post, yeah I'll stop now. Unless you are interested in taking it to another thread ClownPiece?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-25-2019, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T02:22:15-08:00","id":1291755,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm not sold on this. For starters, most of the MA-using Solars I've seen pick a MA do so to have a short, self-contained charm set which fits their concept. They also usually combo it with native defenses and the odd offense which allows comboing. Solar Stealth, Dodge, Melee, Athletics, Brawl and Resistance all offer combo's which quite frankly blow away anything shown so far for Lunars, and which also have to be balanced with all Martial Arts. Also, the increased cost for MA charms and MA ability dots is far from trivial when you wish to combine two or three Martial Arts. Something which will also become more and more prevalent as more will be released. Martial Arts is after all the ever-expanding Charm Tree...<br /> <br /> Finally, the Dawns I've seen until now have all gone for the Solar's native offense charms, not MA. But that is due to the current lack of high end options which leverage supernal and the aforementioned lack of easily combined MA's in order for that choice to truly shine and compete with the native charms. The Dawn focusing on Martial Arts is not in a good place <i>compared to their other options due to lack of content. Not due to Lunars. </i>That, however, will change in due time and is no way indicative of Lunars being better MA's.<br /> <br /> They dabble and combine MA charms from likely a single style with their native charms, and, yes, they will really be good at it, a true master. The Dawn Solar Master of the Blade, to pick one example, will be able to combine Single Point, Violet Bier, Steel Devil, some swordy SMA and his native Melee, Dodge or Resistance, the multipliers and other goodies from Athletics and so on. I'm sorry, but I have no doubt whatsoever which character will play and feel like the undisputed, transcendental master of Martial Arts, and which will not.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Lunar combat charms revealed so far, well, they obviously lack the sheer depth, breath and power of the Solar options. Ok, we've only seen Dexterity, but this is still a core part of their dodge and the accuracy part of their offensive trees, as well as pulling duty as their stealth tree. Taken as self-contained, and lacking supernal, I don't think anyone here can argue what we've seen is more powerful than Solars, right?<br /> <br /> It is obviously meant to be filled out with Martial Arts and/or shapeshifting, and those two are mutually exclusive! Yes, the Lunar will be flexible and have an answer for most situations, but they won't ever have the sheer power or focus of a Solar. Will they have powerful combos between MA and native charms? I'm sure they will! Same as with their animal forms and their native charms. Solars still have more, if only because of how laser focused and powerful their trees are. Add Supernal and no other splat has a larger selection to synergize and combine ridiculously powerful effects. They will also be able to do this with MA, even if perhaps to a lesser extent right now (and that is debatable).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","user":"Angwe","date":". 02-25-2019, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T02:41:29-08:00","id":1291758,"title":"","content":"One of the tricky bits about Supernal seems to be that it's hard to balance around other splats not getting it, hence published trees don't go to Essence 5. I don't really feel like SMA is a good fit to fill this gap though; it's mainly there to do strange proprietary Sidereal type MA powers to extent their capabilities, not stuff that really feels right to me to Supernal / High Essence Solars, plus it's dependent on Sidereal tutors etc. Some &quot;Celestial MA, but designed by Sidereals to take on Supernal Solar strengths&quot; could fill that gap, a la Immaculate Styles, but I'm not sure that would feel right for Solars either (it's OK for DBs to have 5 super, iconic MA, but I'm not sure about for Solars, given the focus on how both diverse and individual and yet plain their expression of power are meant to be).<br /> <br /> But there doesn't seem to be a good consensus about if Solars who take MA primary are weak compared to other Abilities as primary, even without many Supernal options?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T02:49:38-08:00","id":1291759,"title":"","content":"Actually, is it even confirmed that supernal will let them learn SMA early? It might end up like sorcery where supernal occult still doesn't let you get sorcery early.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:00:48-08:00","id":1291762,"title":"","content":"In terms of talking about power levels and the Usurpation, I think it's important to note that:<br /> <br /> A)The Usurpation-era Solars included a ton of elders who'd lived for thousands of years. Not hundreds, but I'm sure dozens. And probably most of them had lived hundreds of years. Whereas most of the Dragonblood had only lived a hundred or so years. There was a massive difference in essence and experience.<br /> <br /> B)Today, your average Dynastic adventurer in the threshold has been exalted 10-20 years. Your average Legion officer or Shikari maybe 40? A Satrap may well have been Exalted for well over a century.<br /> Your average Solar has been exalted for... about a year. An exceptionally old Solar has been exalted five years. Canonically, the only Solars with Essence 3 are going to be those who predate the return, like Yurgen Kaneko, Samea and Filial Wisdom.<br /> There's a massive difference in essence and experience.<br /> <br /> So, a group of Essence 2-3 Dragonblood has to be a beatable but challenging encounter for a group of Essence 1 Solars. A group of Essence 4-5 Dragonblood has to be a beatable but challenging encounter for a group of Essence 3 Solars.<br /> Because that's what they're fighting, and it needs to not feel like a cakewalk.<br /> <br /> But just because an Essence 4 Dragonblood is a tricky fight for an Essence 3 Solar, doesn't mean that 10 Essence 6 Solars didn't require an ambush by 100 Essence 2-3 Dragonblood, most of whom died fighting.<br /> <br /> Tldr; Dragonblood being a challenge for Solars in the Time of Tumult, doesn't mean the Usurpation was a cakewalk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, the Dawns I've seen until now have all gone for the Solar's native offense charms, not MA.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true for me as well. I've seen other Castes take Martial Arts, but not actually Dawns.<br /> From what I can remember, in 3rd ed, I've seen, PC-wise:<br /> 2 Dawns, 1 Zenith, 1 Twilight, 1 Night, and 1 Eclipse using Melee<br /> 1 Zenith and 1 Eclipse using Martial Arts<br /> 1 Twilight using Archery<br /> 1 Night and 1 Eclipse using Brawl<br /> 1 Night using Brawl+Steel Devil (but the Steel Devil's turned out to be a bit weak, honestly)<br /> 1 Eclipse using Thrown (a little)<br /> <br /> Melee just dominates. It's way more popular than anything else. Dawns like it for the overall power and the daiklaives (as opposed to fighting unarmed), everyone else likes it because it combines attack and defence (the Eclipse's base Parry is 7! 7! Before charms! My Parry with Tiger Style is 4) for less XP than, say, Brawl+Dodge.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what point this makes about Lunars and MA, but it's certainly interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:10:30-08:00","id":1291764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291758#post1291758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the tricky bits about Supernal seems to be that it's hard to balance around other splats not getting it, hence published trees don't go to Essence 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's the reason they don't go up to 5. Some Supernal trees do, including Melee and Brawl (which are very strong). Stuff like War (before Miracles, only up to 3), I think lacks higher-essence charms just because the writers wrote 22 charms and then... didn't have any more ideas, basically.<br /> (At the time.)<br /> I don't think lack of Essence 5 charms is a balance factor for Supernal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there doesn't seem to be a good consensus about if Solars who take MA primary are weak compared to other Abilities as primary, even without many Supernal options? </div> </div> </div>I think you can build some brutal combos with Crane/Tiger/Snake/Ebon Shadow/White Reaper/Fire/Earth/Wood/Mantis (ie the unarmed styles).<br /> <br /> But it requires you to buy a lot of abilities. Even with Solar XP, it's just... a lot of XP.<br /> <br /> I'm doing Snake/Fire/Earth/Wood. I put 12 of my starting dots, 4 freebies, and 4 merit points, just in having 5 for my punching ability and being able to buy those charms (and I can't even buy all the charms from those styles, as I don't have 5 dots in all of them).<br /> But this is for a very high-experience game (it's replacing a character who died), so I can afford it.<br /> <br /> Most low-XP characters are going to be put off by the cost.<br /> <br /> Whereas, say, a Melee user can just buy Melee, done. Attack, Defence, guarding others, a wide variety of weapons, a big and powerful charm tree.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think being the master of martial arts is a strong but very, very expensive choice, compared to other methods of fighting. So if you want, say, a Samurai who is at home not only on the battlefield, but also at court, you don't have enough dots left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:22:40-08:00","id":1291767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291762#post1291762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true for me as well. I've seen other Castes take Martial Arts, but not actually Dawns.<br /> From what I can remember, in 3rd ed, I've seen, PC-wise:<br /> 2 Dawns, 1 Zenith, 1 Twilight, 1 Night, and 1 Eclipse using Melee<br /> 1 Zenith and 1 Eclipse using Martial Arts<br /> 1 Twilight using Archery<br /> 1 Night and 1 Eclipse using Brawl<br /> 1 Night using Brawl+Steel Devil (but the Steel Devil's turned out to be a bit weak, honestly)<br /> 1 Eclipse using Thrown (a little)<br /> <br /> Melee just dominates. It's way more popular than anything else. Dawns like it for the overall power and the daiklaives (as opposed to fighting unarmed), everyone else likes it because it combines attack and defence (the Eclipse's base Parry is 7! 7! Before charms! My Parry with Tiger Style is 4) for less XP than, say, Brawl+Dodge.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what point this makes about Lunars and MA, but it's certainly interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think melee is also much more popular because it's evoked in a lot more tropes and archetypes than anything else. Badass samurai duellist? Melee. Giant Conan-esque barbarian thug? Melee. Suave rakish dandy? Melee. Knight of the Round Table? Melee. Swift and sneaky knife fighter? Melee. Etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Whereas archery is nowhere near as omniapplicable concept wise, Solar thrown feels as though it's tailored only to stealth assassins (and don't get me started on the lack of kamehameha available). Brawl is inherently limited in popularity by the existence of MA as a lot of unarmed combatants will be using that instead. I'm not sure the choices you're seeing are necessarily about mechanics at all but much more about what feels cool and thematic to players. Melee is helped by the way the charm tree splits IMO though, giving meaningfully different feeling builds whereas at least to me it feels like there's only really one way to play with Solar thrown and two to play with archery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:23:53-08:00","id":1291769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291750#post1291750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is most definitely not a thing in 3rd edition, though. What we have been told of the first age makes a ton of mentions to various civil wars among the chosen in the age of dreams. And what we have been told doesn't make it seem like it was just solar lead factions exclusively like it was in 2nd edition that were taking part in the fighting. In particular the back story of the solar-lunar bond from the first lunar preview explicitly mentions a <i>lunar lead</i> coalition going to war with a faction lead by a solar trying to claim dibs on ruling Creation by dint of being the last living high general from when the host was united against the creators and the fight ended in the sides calling truce instead of lunar defeat (with the bond being a sort of political marriage made to seal the deal). It also mentions in a different part of the preview that lunars actively countered the solar portion of the deliberative from collecting too much power to themselves so even in the final dream of the first age solars weren't in <i>complete</i> control (though it also implies they did have the most still of any host). Hardly the kind of stuff that would be going on if everyone just meekly agreed 'yeah solars are totes the best lets just do what they say like good little 2nd rates'.<br /> <br /> Edit: Didn't see that other post, yeah I'll stop now. Unless you are interested in taking it to another thread ClownPiece?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's much to be gained from a thread pointing out that solars actually are the strongest and best at everything. The corebook does a fine job of this already, if that didn't convince people then there's no way I will. That said, I don't think the focus on making lunars more and more important does much for the setting, or for lunars honestly. You have to start inventing a lot of very flimsy excuses. Why weren't the lunars shoved in the jade prison? Why didn't they make a separate jade prison just to hold them? Why is the Age of Sorrows so massively diminished? Why is there a Realm at all? And so on, and so forth. 400 almost-solars are far more significant than 150 actual solars, but we look out across Creation and see a fallen and dying world, which really just makes the lunars look lazy and incompetent. Yeah they totally COULD be making warstriders and factory cathedrals and raising cities and so on, they just haven't been... for some reason. Because of the Realm? But the Realm's borders don't extend that far - Mahalanka, for instance, is over 3000 miles away from the nearest satrapy, and Mahalanka isn't even that far east! The majority of Creation is land that the lunars should be ruling in First Age paradises, the gods shouldn't be tyrants ignoring their duties to rule over people, the wyld hunt shouldn't be a significant and powerful force, and yet... Is it the sidereals keeping them down? But the sidereals only have 100 total, and the precious few who can actually kill the lunars are too old and important to be sent down to potentially die in a pointless battle in Creation. Besides, they have very important duties outside of this. So what's keeping them down? Why is this an Age of Sorrows? Maybe they just... really are not as good, at all, as those solars were, and the return of these lost god-kings is a huge fucking deal.<br /> <br /> I refuse to learn this infernal forum software so I'm quoting this manually:<br /> <br /> &quot;But just because an Essence 4 Dragonblood is a tricky fight for an Essence 3 Solar&quot;<br /> <br /> This is completely untrue, both in-setting and mechanically. An essence 3 solar that cares about combat in any way is going to run circles around Mnemon or Berit or anyone else. Not just dawns, either. Every PC I've played that's hit essence 3 - only one was a Dawn, the Twilight had very little investment at all - has, in play, absolutely destroyed several DBs alone. Even when the DBs were optimised to kill them. Wyld Hunts are insanely dangerous even with sidereal support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:32:19-08:00","id":1291771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291769#post1291769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah they totally COULD be making warstriders and factory cathedrals and raising cities and so on, they just haven't been... for some reason. Because of the Realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it's because their Craft charms aren't that powerful.<br /> I mean, I <i>like</i> their craft charms. They're a lot more interesting than Solar or Dragonblood craft charms. But I don't think they're very <i>powerful</i>. I mean, Solars can pretty easily get to the point where Craft XP is essentially irrelevant. I've got 50 gold and 130 silver sitting on my sheet right now. Lunars can't really do that.<br /> And an Essence 5 Lunar with all the craft charms takes 2 months to make an artefact, while a Solar can do it in a week (and I have).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But just because an Essence 4 Dragonblood is a tricky fight for an Essence 3 Solar&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is completely untrue, both in-setting and mechanically. An essence 3 solar that cares about combat in any way is going to run circles around Mnemon or Berit or anyone else. Not just dawns, either. Every PC I've played that's hit essence 3 - only one was a Dawn, the Twilight had very little investment at all - has, in play, absolutely destroyed several DBs alone. Even when the DBs were optimised to kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit confused here.<br /> <br /> I thought your point was that Solars are supposed to be the best, and you were annoyed that this isn't being reflected mechanically. But now you're saying that Solars <i>are</i> absolutely amazing at combat? What's the issue you're annoyed about then?<br /> <br /> Edit: Deleted my last paragraph, I understand it now. Not the paragraph above though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-25-2019, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:34:57-08:00","id":1291772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291771#post1291771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm also confused by this, weren't you just saying DBs aren't that dangerous to Solars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dangerous for the Wyld Hunters, not Huntees.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:35:53-08:00","id":1291773,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. /10char","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:56:59-08:00","id":1291777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291771#post1291771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, it's because their Craft charms aren't that powerful.<br /> I mean, I <i>like</i> their craft charms. They're a lot more interesting than Solar or Dragonblood craft charms. But I don't think they're very <i>powerful</i>. I mean, Solars can pretty easily get to the point where Craft XP is essentially irrelevant. I've got 50 gold and 130 silver sitting on my sheet right now. Lunars can't really do that.<br /> And an Essence 5 Lunar with all the craft charms takes 2 months to make an artefact, while a Solar can do it in a week (and I have).<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm a bit confused here.<br /> <br /> I thought your point was that Solars are supposed to be the best, and you were annoyed that this isn't being reflected mechanically. But now you're saying that Solars <i>are</i> absolutely amazing at combat? What's the issue you're annoyed about then?<br /> <br /> Edit: Deleted my last paragraph, I understand it now. Not the paragraph above though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can still make artifact 5s and have all the moonsilver in the world, along with celestial circle sorcery. Sure, you're not making Kavara with that, but you can still make warstriders and all sorts of other works of immense might that the Realm has a preciously small supply of, ever-dwindling. What's 2 months in a span of 1500 years?<br /> <br /> My point is that solars being the best doesnt just mean beating up DBs, it also means being stronger than the other celestials, because of the problems that start to emerge when you pull other celestials up to Solar level, or just shy of it. I know very well what a Dawn is capable of. If a Full Moon is almost as good as that, then let's stop for a moment and think about those... let's be conservative and say the castes are divided up equally, including casteless. 100 full moons. It's more than this, but we're being conservative here. Including a load of old and very powerful ones. A legion doesn't stand a chance against them! But, you may say, but the Realm have X and Y artifice that - SO DO LUNARS! And unlike the Realm, they can make more to replace it! And unlike the Realm, they reincarnate and will return, while mass warfare genuinely and substantially depletes the Dragonblooded of the Realm. Someone said earlier that the Shogunate was millions of DBs, which is a farcical number with no basis, but there were definitely far more than we have just now. That's after the Realm has spent the past 800 years aggressively building up as much as it can, another event that doesn't make any sense with 100 full moons around to cull them. The only way that this setting makes even the slightest bit of sense to arrive at the point its at is if the lunars really can't just beat the Realm, which means that those Full Moons really are a big step below what a Dawn is, because we know what a Dawn can do (or, at least, I know, as I'm beginning to suspect that people talking about the system have never played a game of it and seen what a Dawn is actually like) and the thought of 100 of them just... running around, fighting the Realm, how is there a Realm? How did it ever take off? Remember, the Realm was not founded until AFTER the balorian crusade ended. The fae were gone, fucked off. A ton of new lunars were incarnating into the world - this is mentioned in the lunar preview, you may recall. The Silver Pact had an explicit goal of destroying the Shogunate and the Realm was its successor. How could 400 almost-solars... how could 100 almost-dawns bungle that so hard? You see? Making lunars almost-dawns makes them look bad, because now there's no excuses for this.<br /> <br /> (as a side note, this could actually work if you went with the old lore that the lunars all ran away to the wyld and there werent 400 of them and a load of them are old, mad monstrosities, but the 3e lore is very clear that the Silver Pact is competent, driven and the elder lunars are active and perfectly sane)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T04:02:10-08:00","id":1291778,"title":"","content":"Please do not forget, the Lunars can't beat the Realm <i><b>and</b></i> the Bronze Faction Sidereals arrayed behind them (who are the majority faction, IIRC) who can basically see the future. And only because the only other group of equally-ish powered Exalted and the might of the Largest Empire on Creation (with thousands (?) of their own Exalted) is arrayed against them, is the Silver Pact fighting to a very advantageous draw.<br /> <br /> Thats how strong the Lunars are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T04:03:11-08:00","id":1291779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291694#post1291694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's probably worth saying in context to the thread. Clownpiece was saying that one of the narrative purpose of the Solar Exalted is to return and tip the balance of the world to either salvation or destruction. They do this because their power is so much greater than anyone else's in the setting at the moment. Just look at Solar Circle Sorcery as an example. Since it is totally unfair that sorcerers are the only people who get to have that kind of impact and everyone else is a chump, Dawns must be similarly more powerful, and the combat rules should support this. That's why Solars need to be as much better at fighting as Ligier is more powerful than Octavian.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, you see, the ability to summon Ligier should not be the measuring stick of Solar power. The rest of Solar Sorcery isn't even that much more powerful than Celestial. Rain of Doom can destroy a city but Cantana of Empty Voices can kill everyone inside it so it's not like an insane step up in power.<br /> <br /> But that's actually okay, because Solars don't NEED to be able to summon Ligier to tip the scales. They are more powerful fighters than Full Moons, better sorcerers than No Moons, etcetera, but not by an insane degree, and certainly not more powerful than a lot of current Lunars. Leviathan would roll any Essence 1 Dawn. That's okay though, the introduction of 60 Dawn/Dusk/Slayers into the world is a huge deal anyway. The scale is ripe to be tipped in any direction, and even the introduction of 60 new Sidereals or Lunars would do it, but Solars are even more powerful than that! </div> </div> </div>Clownpiece's argument does not seems to be about what kind of change any solar will bring in short term after reappearing but about the way as a player you feel being a solar PC makes you someone who changes the context through your solar particularity. Pointing this out about solar circle sorcery does not change that. And as you point it out, in fact, the kind of power he needs for the solars doesn't need to be that much more powerful, at least in short term use, for it to be felt as a solar player.<br /> Another problem here is that I don't think that comparing solar powers against lunars' or whatever in a competitive way is what makes things matters the most in that issue rather than their way of being significant for each other and in stories (and maybe their setting too).<br /> <br /> I'm not a huge fan of the solars being the most powerful things in the world to such an extent that nothing else than them matters and, according to what he said, it seems Clownpiece either. (I think that the dawns are not that bad either at telling solars' stories except maybe a dawn martial artist.) I also don't think that there is no other way to make solar martial artists matter than making of them the absolute best in a way nullifying the interest of any other exalt martial artist fighting against them. In fact I have the feeling that wordings like &quot;much greater than&quot;, &quot;much more powerful than&quot; in non that quantitative measurable things are a little bit lacking when taken too litteraly and used to make points in such a competitive way about such complex effectivities.<br /> I have the feeling that there is a &quot;solars are the most awesome even for us but not capable to beat one of us head-on without really working a lot for it&quot; thing in celestial exalts and it kind of express itself in a good way in combat solars charms. A good example is those about bigger closed intervals than any other exalt with maximum numerical outcomes being better than the others, but with such a sensitivity that it lets a huge amount of possibilities for any fight to become fair most of the time when fighting against any other celestial exalt equipped (intentionally or not) to fight against them while not impeding solars' ability to produce under some conditions the biggest outcomes. I have the feeling that this way of expressing solars' awesomeness mostly disappear when solars are practicing martial arts, the mastery effects in known martial arts not having this thing enough and being too often lacking. It gives off a feeling of &quot;what's the point of a solar martial artist then&quot; when compared to the other celestial exalts.<br /> <br /> I hope it's readable again, I wrote it without any help this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T04:13:36-08:00","id":1291782,"title":"","content":"Part of the issue with how powerful Lunars are/how do we explain why they haven't just made Creation their bitch is the way Lunars have been retconned into importance. Every time the Lunars are rewritten then get more important, more influential, more relevant to the history and state of Creation, which is good, no Exalt type should be irrelevant. However the setting doesn't actually meaningfully change as part of this, everything is basically the same just now we're told it would be so different if it wasn't for Lunars, but anyone who's been playing Exalted for any length of time knows that just isn't true because it was all the same when Lunars weren't written to be doing all this stuff, and that creates a heck of a disconnect in trying to justify the current state of affairs.<br /> <br /> I'd be really interested in what someone totally new to Exalted as on 3e and without any knowledge, reference to or access to older material made of Lunars, and the setting in general, to be honest. It seems sometimes that there's a ton of assumptions brought over from previous editions which isn't always beneficial to understanding the game as it is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T04:18:12-08:00","id":1291783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FODOR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291782#post1291782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the issue with how powerful Lunars are/how do we explain why they haven't just made Creation their bitch is the way Lunars have been retconned into importance. Every time the Lunars are rewritten then get more important, more influential, more relevant to the history and state of Creation, which is good, no Exalt type should be irrelevant. However the setting doesn't actually meaningfully change as part of this, everything is basically the same just now we're told it would be so different if it wasn't for Lunars, but anyone who's been playing Exalted for any length of time knows that just isn't true because it was all the same when Lunars weren't written to be doing all this stuff, and that creates a heck of a disconnect in trying to justify the current state of affairs.<br /> <br /> I'd be really interested in what someone totally new to Exalted as on 3e and without any knowledge, reference to or access to older material made of Lunars, and the setting in general, to be honest. It seems sometimes that there's a ton of assumptions brought over from previous editions which isn't always beneficial to understanding the game as it is now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Show a new player this new setting and ask them to guess which splat is the one in the corebook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T05:52:47-08:00","id":1291798,"title":"","content":"I really, really like this edition's Lunars, they are appropriately powerful, but honestly, I truly can not understand how anyone thinks Solars are still not a whole tier more powerful than them.<br /> <br /> Solar Circle Sorcery is not just <i>marginally </i>more powerful. The step up from Celestial to Solar is <i>huge</i>. From the workings to the spells, really, there's no comparing them, and yes, Lunars can do Solar workings, but the speed difference <i>matters</i>. When it comes to combat Solars just have so, so, <i>so</i> many ways of reverting the game back to a sustainable perfect or die or just plain making a mockery out of the possibility of defeat. Lunars simply can't reach that level, and we've seen enough of their charms now that I feel pretty confident making that statement. I've seen several Solars played who would be more than comfortable facing a Wyld Hunt on their own, and rightly so.<br /> <br /> Not all, but some of their Charms sets also have a scale that Lunars simply can't attain. Lore destroys <i>cities.</i> If you are a Spirit, no matter how powerful, Occult simply owns you, Bureaucracy can take over any organization and forget about returning the favor, Socialize goes to downright scary places and arguably lunars better than Lunars if you keep to human forms, etc. The Solars are still the undisputed leaders of the pack, and I've seen in actual play how blisteringly fast a Solar Circle can transform some backwater into a regional superpower. The tools for <i>that </i>kind of dominance I simply can't see in the Lunar charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T05:59:19-08:00","id":1291799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bboat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291783#post1291783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Show a new player this new setting and ask them to guess which splat is the one in the corebook</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually funny story, the original concept before 1e dropped was going to be that DBs were the corebook splat. They\u2019re weaker so they had to work together against bigger foes in classic TTRPG fashion, it also it wouldn\u2019t even be revealed that Solars were not actually anathema until the Solar splatbook later on. So you\u2019d have the whole player base discover in real life that Solars and Lunars are not body snatching demons. I think that idea was ultimately scrapped because pulling a fast one on your players might not be well received, and making playable Solars who\u2019s powers are a step above your current beloved PCs would make it seem like okay, now you can play one of the good exalts if you buy this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T06:09:58-08:00","id":1291801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291798#post1291798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really, really like this edition's Lunars, they are appropriately powerful, but honestly, I truly can not understand how anyone thinks Solars are still not a whole tier more powerful than them.<br /> <br /> Solar Circle Sorcery is not just <i>marginally </i>more powerful. The step up from Celestial to Solar is <i>huge</i>. From the workings to the spells, really, there's no comparing them, and yes, Lunars can do Solar workings, but the speed difference <i>matters</i>. When it comes to combat Solars just have so, so, <i>so</i> many ways of reverting the game back to a sustainable perfect or die or just plain making a mockery out of the possibility of defeat. Lunars simply can't reach that level, and we've seen enough of their charms now that I feel pretty confident making that statement. I've seen several Solars played who would be more than comfortable facing a Wyld Hunt on their own, and rightly so.<br /> <br /> Not all, but some of their Charms sets also have a scale that Lunars simply can't attain. Lore destroys <i>cities.</i> If you are a Spirit, no matter how powerful, Occult simply owns you, Bureaucracy can take over any organization and forget about returning the favor, Socialize goes to downright scary places and arguably lunars better than Lunars if you keep to human forms, etc. The Solars are still the undisputed leaders of the pack, and I've seen in actual play how blisteringly fast a Solar Circle can transform some backwater into a regional superpower. The tools for <i>that </i>kind of dominance I simply can't see in the Lunar charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Solars are a tier above for sure. They\u2019ve got Supernals for everything, except sorcery, so they can master in a few months or years what it takes any other exalt decades or centuries to even attempt. That\u2019s not even including their Mastery keywords.<br /> <br /> But pointing to the ability to summon Ligier is, however unintentionally, misleading. It\u2019s not an ability that will affect Creation for decades at least, barring PC super advancement but PCs can be essence 5 before they leave high school age. Also even for Solar circle sorcery it is ungodly dangerous to attempt for even an experienced Solar. Having Spirit Caging Mandala would help you maybe a bit, but Ligier stands a good chance of bisecting you before you even cast it. Once you have him you have to try and rend down his impressive essence while wrestling with him in the cage and at low essence especially your motes can drain fast. <br /> <br /> Solar Lore IS a much better example, but even that is much much less powerful than having the Green Sun as your thrall, and has a lot more options for other major players to counter it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T06:11:29-08:00","id":1291804,"title":"","content":"TBH, were I the writer, I wouldn't mention Sidereals at all in the Core, except maybe cryptic hints of mysterious advisors and old masters. Have hints in the DB book, have fiction where people wonder why the Maidens don't have Exalts, or Solars who remember their First Age lives hanging out with skinwalkers and astrologer-sifus, but no explanation.<br /> Then reveal it in Sidereals.<br /> <br /> But then, I like that kind of thing. Not everyone does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T06:13:38-08:00","id":1291805,"title":"","content":"On Solar vs Lunar effects...<br /> <br /> I think training is a good example.<br /> <br /> A Solar can train people up to competency in a month. In another week, they're expert warriors.<br /> <br /> A Lunar... can't. They can train people to be a bit better in a month. With another, they can give them perfect morale. But it's just not in the same wheelhouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T07:03:00-08:00","id":1291811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291805#post1291805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Solar vs Lunar effects...<br /> <br /> I think training is a good example.<br /> <br /> A Solar can train people up to competency in a month. In another week, they're expert warriors.<br /> <br /> A Lunar... can't. They can train people to be a bit better in a month. With another, they can give them perfect morale. But it's just not in the same wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll have see though. We're still missing the other 60% of the charmset. Evaluating it now is a bit premature. Also, a lunar can grant an army mutations which more than balances the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-25-2019, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T11:03:05-08:00","id":1291884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291764#post1291764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's the reason they don't go up to 5. Some Supernal trees do, including Melee and Brawl (which are very strong). Stuff like War (before Miracles, only up to 3), I think lacks higher-essence charms just because the writers wrote 22 charms and then... didn't have any more ideas, basically.<br /> (At the time.)<br /> I don't think lack of Essence 5 charms is a balance factor for Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291764#post1291764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I think being the master of martial arts is a strong but very, very expensive choice, compared to other methods of fighting. So if you want, say, a Samurai who is at home not only on the battlefield, but also at court, you don't have enough dots left.</div> </div> </div> </div>If not due to lack of high Essence 4-5 MA Charms (and that's fairly irrelevant), and more due to expense of combining styles, what do you reckon would be a solution to this...? (If it does need a solution). More synergistic options, cheaper access to Charms, etc.? Could SMA even present a solution to that sort of problem, if it's much consistent with how it's been presented in previous editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T11:19:29-08:00","id":1291888,"title":"","content":"Solars can turn people into warriors.<br /> <br /> Lunars can turn people into <i>BEARS</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T11:34:37-08:00","id":1291890,"title":"","content":"Well, I found it a bit odd that...<br /> <br /> In playtesting, the devs (at that time) said they found that MA was really, really powerful when combined with multiple styles.<br /> <br /> So they made players buy each ability seperately, at great expense (I mean, to get all the charms it's 19xp if favoured for each second style, plus the cost of buying the charms themselves. That's a lot to not even get more dice). And you have to buy a 4pt merit (which you have to buy whether you're combining styles or not).<br /> <br /> Also, in playtesting, the devs (at that time) said they found that people didn't want to buy MA, because native charms were more attractive for the cost. So they gave people special XP which you could spend on MA (or sorcery), so you could buy native charms and MA. (And later let you use it to buy dots too.)<br /> <br /> This always seemed... a bit illogical to me, tbh.<br /> <br /> So, my solution would be to a)ditch the Merit, and b)give a steep discount on going into other styles (making it free, like it was in 2nd ed, might be a bit too much).<br /> <br /> I'd also suggest c)don't let people buy MA with Solar/Lunar/Dragon XP.<br /> <br /> Lunar XP, after all, was one of the arguments for MA being the One True Build for Lunars.<br /> <br /> And certainly, I bought up all of Tiger Style basically as an easy side-thing which didn't stop me buying charms as well. NIce, but maybe is a bit too good?<br /> <br /> I should say though, the Solar XP do currently help to mitigate the cost of being a Martial Arts master. But giving people special XP to mitigate a cost seems over-complicated.<br /> <br /> <br /> I imagine the above opinions are very unpopular, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-25-2019, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T11:44:56-08:00","id":1291893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291888#post1291888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars can turn people into warriors.<br /> <br /> Lunars can turn people into <i>BEARS</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elite warriors are more useful for making an expansionistic empire.<br /> <br /> Bearmen are cooler.<br /> And also more useful for tribes of nomadic tundra and forest dwellers.<br /> <br /> Solars have more charms for creating mighty civilisations.<br /> <br /> Lunars have more charms for allowing humans to adapt to the environment they live in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T11:47:05-08:00","id":1291895,"title":"","content":"Certainly doesn't seem crazy at all and quite sensible put like that, but isn't one of the benefits of Solar XP for MA intended to be strongly encouraging some combat dabbling for social and intellectual focused characters through MA? <br /> <br /> Where in theory again this is the best way for social characters to dabble in combat abilities, due to set up providing a complete combat package, but with some specific limitations per MA and complexity in combining MAs that mean you're not too powerful compared to focused characters. I may be off base with this though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T12:18:07-08:00","id":1291901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291890#post1291890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my solution would be to a)ditch the Merit, and b)give a steep discount on going into other styles (making it free, like it was in 2nd ed, might be a bit too much).<br /> <br /> I'd also suggest c)don't let people buy MA with Solar/Lunar/Dragon XP.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> why do you hate the idea of noncombat characters being able to attain a reasonable level of combat competence without having to waste their charm xp on combat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T12:23:27-08:00","id":1291902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291759#post1291759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, is it even confirmed that supernal will let them learn SMA early? It might end up like sorcery where supernal occult still doesn't let you get sorcery early.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asked in the 'ask the devs' thread and it turns out that current thinking (subject to change, of course) is that SMA are going to be like sorcery and not something you can get early with martial arts as your chosen supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T12:24:44-08:00","id":1291903,"title":"","content":"Am i correct in thinking that one of the main weaknesses of trying to be the &quot;ultimate solar martial artist&quot; is that the best martial art styles are the Sidereal ones which we haven't got access too yet? Personally ive always assumed that the reason most current MA styles cap at essence 3 is that the SMA styles are meant to be the essence 3-5 ones that push you too the top of MA power. It seems kinda contradictory if a solar was able to be the strongest martial artist without knowing the strongest styles. If that is the case then it kinda solves the problem of choosing MA as your supernal as you have something to spec into now and as Lunars don't get to use them solves the problem of them being potentially better at martial arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T13:20:31-08:00","id":1291917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291893#post1291893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Elite warriors are more useful for making an expansionistic empire.<br /> <br /> Bearmen are cooler.<br /> And also more useful for tribes of nomadic tundra and forest dwellers.<br /> <br /> Solars have more charms for creating mighty civilisations.<br /> <br /> Lunars have more charms for allowing humans to adapt to the environment they live in.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that but wings or hide 5 are very strong merits. Wings 5 gives archers an entirely new way to attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T13:26:35-08:00","id":1291920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargle18446</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291903#post1291903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i correct in thinking that one of the main weaknesses of trying to be the &quot;ultimate solar martial artist&quot; is that the best martial art styles are the Sidereal ones which we haven't got access too yet? Personally ive always assumed that the reason most current MA styles cap at essence 3 is that the SMA styles are meant to be the essence 3-5 ones that push you too the top of MA power. It seems kinda contradictory if a solar was able to be the strongest martial artist without knowing the strongest styles. If that is the case then it kinda solves the problem of choosing MA as your supernal as you have something to spec into now and as Lunars don't get to use them solves the problem of them being potentially better at martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>SMA should not be the &quot;true path&quot; for solars. That's just forcing every st to use sidereals in only one way. Solars can't teach them and can't create them and from what vance has recently said solars do not get to supernal SMA. <br /> <br /> Normal MA needs to be good on it's own and for the most part it is. Rightous devil and shining point are really good for what they do. It just needs to be supplimented with native charms but so do a lot of things. The only problem is that the system is overly complicated with the extra xp you invest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T13:38:39-08:00","id":1291927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291769#post1291769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think there's much to be gained from a thread pointing out that solars actually are the strongest and best at everything. The corebook does a fine job of this already, if that didn't convince people then there's no way I will. <b>That said, I don't think the focus on making lunars more and more important does much for the setting, or for lunars honestly.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect you have an insufficient understanding of the issue that has plagued Lunars over two editions, which is, roughly, &quot;why do they exist at all?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;They're the reason the Realm only rules a big chunk of the world instead of all of it&quot; is better than both the &quot;rawr, barbarians! Try to differentiate your circle by using different weapons!&quot; and &quot;let's have them go on a long plan to alter societies so that they don't need Exalted... and give them no charms suitable to this task, and no real reason to <i>do</i> that task&quot; treatments of the past. And part of that is giving Lunars the ability to throw their weight around to that degree.<br /> <br /> One should remember the Lunars are intended to be <i>nearly</i> as powerful as Solars, but that power expresses itself in different ways. There remain things no Lunar, of any essence, is going to be able to do easily that a Solar could do... but that doesn't mean that any Solar should effortlessly curbstomp any given Lunar, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2334,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","user":"Aliasi","date":".  part doesn't mean all, silly Ali! 02-26-2019, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T13:40:38-08:00","id":1291928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291902#post1291902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Asked in the 'ask the devs' thread and it turns out that current thinking (subject to change, of course) is that SMA are going to be like sorcery and not something you can get early with martial arts as your chosen supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feels like this is probably a good idea. It doesn't seem to make so much sense to have these gated weird elder powers for Sidereals which are more loosely focused on combat, into Solar access at low essence with a supernal combat ability. <br /> <br /> If Solars don't have the essence to power them, assuming something like sutras, they can become a trap build (looks impressive on paper and too attractive in weird power not to buy, just not really viable), and distract from more viable options, or if that's not the case, they can easily drift into becoming an open ur-power subject to having a special tutor, etc.<br /> <br /> Plus, not sure about having Solars being able to buy Sidereal secret MA which Sidereals may have to wait until late game to buy. Feels like that would be a downer for Sidereal players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T13:43:39-08:00","id":1291930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291893#post1291893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Elite warriors are more useful for making an expansionistic empire.<br /> <br /> Bearmen are cooler.<br /> And also more useful for tribes of nomadic tundra and forest dwellers.<br /> <br /> Solars have more charms for creating mighty civilisations.<br /> <br /> Lunars have more charms for allowing humans to adapt to the environment they live in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess how I would try to phrase it is:<br /> <br /> Solars absolutely have a relative advantage in being great sorcerous king heroes. (This is how it should be as well. For all that I totally get that people don't want to feel that when they play their Solar sole wandering yojimbo Jedi Knight type they're doing something &quot;wrong&quot; since Solars &quot;should be&quot; leaders. But they've still gotta have that relative advantage.).<br /> <br /> If anyone is going to build the Tower of Babel, metaphorically speaking, it's going to be them.<br /> <br /> In the bigger picture, then, keys might be whether the other Exalted have the tools to come at them obliquely to exploit the gaps in all the ways in which their grand projects Tower of Babel (to extend the metaphor for glorious and great works generally), are not a good idea. Further to exploit all the gaps that being a lord of powerful magical civilization and master of abilities does not give them an absolute advantage in. Further again have the tools to appropriate up or twist or neutralize the products of the Solar's power so that they do not serve his will so faithfully and even that actually they how they operate in the world add to your goals and detract from his.<br /> <br /> Those are all ways that they can compete if you can't challenge on a direct basis in the terms that your opponent is setting them, and without being directly superior in an ability. Which the Celestials and the Dragonblooded absolutely should have (albeit as an uphill struggle!). Or put another way, in a case by case expression of abilities they should probably not win against a Solar, but in their ability to employ a winning strategy against him that avoids competing on an ability for ability basis, much more should be possible. (O<u>f course this is not really at all what the measure of their success as splats should be about, but ideally should totally be possible</u>).<br /> <br /> I don't have a lot of trust in how much we can work this out in a kind of &quot;white room&quot; setup. If we're going to try and &quot;white room&quot; anything, to do it with more tractable elements like combat. (So big part of why we end up talking about that?).<br /> <br /> (But again this is all a tangent to thread topic.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:03:29-08:00","id":1291936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291928#post1291928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Feels like this is probably a good idea. It doesn't seem to make so much sense to have these gated weird elder powers for Sidereals which are more loosely focused on combat, into Solar access at low essence with a supernal combat ability.<br /> <br /> If Solars don't have the essence to power them, assuming something like sutras, they can become a trap build (looks impressive on paper and too attractive in weird power not to buy, just not really viable), and distract from more viable options, or if that's not the case, they can easily drift into becoming an open ur-power subject to having a special tutor, etc.<br /> <br /> Plus, not sure about having Solars being able to buy Sidereal secret MA which Sidereals may have to wait until late game to buy. Feels like that would be a downer for Sidereal players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and it makes it to were its definitely going to be harder to get them. You have to find a Sidereal, hope they aren't some youngling like you who doesn't even know one themselves, convince them to pass unto you the secrets of the most awesome trump card they have, and have legit high level essence because your MA supernal isn't going to cut it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:20:40-08:00","id":1291947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291607#post1291607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I thought the meta was that Solars were already supposed to be very viable and comparable with Celestial Martial Arts against a Brawl / Melee specialist already in 3e? If so, they don't really *need* a power boost from SMA, and also probably shouldn't get one (as Solar with SMA overpowering a Brawl Solar is at least as bad as underpowering them!).</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need (and shouldn't get) a power boost relative to similarly top-tier Solar Brawl; but they can't fall <i>too</i> far behind.<br /> <br /> This is a problem if people want SMA-using Solars to be noticeably worse at SMA than Sidereals, who <i>themselves</i> are supposed to be slightly weaker than Brawl Solars - at that point, even accounting for the versatility of SMA, it becomes tricky to avoid a situation where the SMA using Solar is actually noticeably weaker in a fight than a Brawl one, which goes against the idea that SMA is this big valuable deal for Solar martial artists.<br /> <br /> There are various ways around this, but most of them require sacrificing some ground on the three points I mentioned above. Historically... Epimetheus is <i>sort of</i> right in the sense that SMA was always &quot;Solars are flatly worse than Sideraels at it and also pay bazillion XP, so if SMA was remotely balanced no Solar would seriously consider learning it except for flavor reasons.&quot; Of course, the corollary to this is that there has always been unbalanced SMA (so the answer to &quot;why would a Solar want to learn this&quot; has historically been &quot;well, these are actually notably stronger than any published Solar charms.&quot;)<br /> <br /> That latter part isn't going to carry over into 3e (obviously, since it was an error), but without it, if you want the story of a Solar finding an SMA tutor to make sense, you need to grapple with these questions more seriously.<br /> <br /> (Although I suppose it bears mentioning that 3e <i>has</i> introduced another splat that supposedly uses SMA as well as Sidereals do - we'll see what that means. It's possible that there's widgets or options we're not seeing that allow Sidereals, Getimians, and Solars (plus any other hypothetical &quot;secondary&quot; users like Solars) to all use SMA in their own ways without stepping on each other's toes. We don't know if Getimians use SMA the same way Sidereals do, just that it's at least arguable that they're as good at it as Sidereals are.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-25-2019, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:27:46-08:00","id":1291951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291799#post1291799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually funny story, the original concept before 1e dropped was going to be that DBs were the corebook splat. They\u2019re weaker so they had to work together against bigger foes in classic TTRPG fashion, it also it wouldn\u2019t even be revealed that Solars were not actually anathema until the Solar splatbook later on. So you\u2019d have the whole player base discover in real life that Solars and Lunars are not body snatching demons. I think that idea was ultimately scrapped because pulling a fast one on your players might not be well received, and making playable Solars who\u2019s powers are a step above your current beloved PCs would make it seem like okay, now you can play one of the good exalts if you buy this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to this a bit, imagine if the Great Houses were written like the Vampire clans of teh late 90s. I woudl actually go so far to say as Exalted would have been consdiered knock-off L5R meets Vampire and would not nearly have been so successful.<br /> <br /> Also imagine if the default setting was the world-dominating empire as the PCs. And how much issues Exalted has had <i>as is</i> at times for imperial apolgia.<br /> <br /> I am one to think had DBs would have been first, Exlated would have gone the way of Trinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:27:59-08:00","id":1291952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291917#post1291917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say that but wings or hide 5 are very strong merits. Wings 5 gives archers an entirely new way to attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, Elite Warriors are, overall, probably more useful than Regular Troops with Wings. A winged regular archer has 4 dice to hit; a Tiger Warrior has 11.<br /> <br /> (Obviously we're talking about story, not mechanics, but these dice pools represent the difference in skill between Tiger Warriors and regular soldiers. And I am talking about trained soldier beastmen, not just any 14-year old kid. Whereas, in the Solar Empire, even the 14-year old kids are amazing warriors.)<br /> <br /> And wings isn't so useful at, say, defending a walled city from barbarian raiders; you're probably going to want to stand behind your battlements anyway, rather than fly above the enemy where you're easy to hit (in your light armour, because medium armour's too heavy and ill-fitting for you to fly around in).<br /> <br /> But of course, at the same time... you can do all sorts of interesting things with Winged troops. Scouting, raiding, flying straight over walls, and just generally moving your army around much faster.<br /> <br /> If you're interested in traditional expansion of a fortified Empire, Solars are stronger.<br /> <br /> If you're interested in asymetric warfare and guerilla strangeness, better to go with beastmen.<br /> <br /> However, the really interesting thing is when you get a Lunar and a Solar working together, and have Winged Elite Warriors!<br /> <br /> (I'd also suggest, besides Wings and 5-pt Hide, very interesting ones for warfare are gills for aquatic warfare and defence against the Realm, burrower for seige warfare and ambushes, centaur form for general speed, echolocation for night fighting, pheromones for terrifying the enemy or seducing them, spinnarets for all sorts of shenanigans. Things like carapace and natural weapons you can just make stuff for. )<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:29:56-08:00","id":1291953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargle18446</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291903#post1291903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i correct in thinking that one of the main weaknesses of trying to be the &quot;ultimate solar martial artist&quot; is that the best martial art styles are the Sidereal ones which we haven't got access too yet? Personally ive always assumed that the reason most current MA styles cap at essence 3 is that the SMA styles are meant to be the essence 3-5 ones that push you too the top of MA power. It seems kinda contradictory if a solar was able to be the strongest martial artist without knowing the strongest styles. If that is the case then it kinda solves the problem of choosing MA as your supernal as you have something to spec into now and as Lunars don't get to use them solves the problem of them being potentially better at martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fair to me.<br /> <br /> Not sure about having them Supernal, but just making them available to buy at Essence 4+ (or 3+, whenever they start), if you get a Sidereal mentor of course, seems appropriate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:47:13-08:00","id":1291965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291952#post1291952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tbh, Elite Warriors are, overall, probably more useful than Regular Troops with Wings. A winged regular archer has 4 dice to hit; a Tiger Warrior has 11.<br /> <br /> (Obviously we're talking about story, not mechanics, but these dice pools represent the difference in skill between Tiger Warriors and regular soldiers. And I am talking about trained soldier beastmen, not just any 14-year old kid. Whereas, in the Solar Empire, even the 14-year old kids are amazing warriors.)<br /> <br /> And wings isn't so useful at, say, defending a walled city from barbarian raiders; you're probably going to want to stand behind your battlements anyway, rather than fly above the enemy where you're easy to hit (in your light armour, because medium armour's too heavy and ill-fitting for you to fly around in).<br /> <br /> But of course, at the same time... you can do all sorts of interesting things with Winged troops. Scouting, raiding, flying straight over walls, and just generally moving your army around much faster.<br /> <br /> If you're interested in traditional expansion of a fortified Empire, Solars are stronger.<br /> <br /> If you're interested in asymetric warfare and guerilla strangeness, better to go with beastmen.<br /> <br /> However, the really interesting thing is when you get a Lunar and a Solar working together, and have Winged Elite Warriors!<br /> <br /> (I'd also suggest, besides Wings and 5-pt Hide, very interesting ones for warfare are gills for aquatic warfare and defence against the Realm, burrower for seige warfare and ambushes, centaur form for general speed, echolocation for night fighting, pheromones for terrifying the enemy or seducing them, spinnarets for all sorts of shenanigans. Things like carapace and natural weapons you can just make stuff for. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing prevents lunars from learning or creating more training charms on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:49:38-08:00","id":1291969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291895#post1291895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly doesn't seem crazy at all and quite sensible put like that, but isn't one of the benefits of Solar XP for MA intended to be strongly encouraging some combat dabbling for social and intellectual focused characters through MA?<br /> <br /> Where in theory again this is the best way for social characters to dabble in combat abilities, due to set up providing a complete combat package, but with some specific limitations per MA and complexity in combining MAs that mean you're not too powerful compared to focused characters. I may be off base with this though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's intended, but that is a beneficial effect.<br /> <br /> Though, I will say in response to Aluminiumtrioxid, that until you get into Essence 3 at least, dabbling in combat abilities is fine with 5 in a Combat Ability and an excellency. That'll actually be fine for combat for ages. You won't be a combat master, but when you're rolling, say, 20 dice (assuming Dex 4) with your staff or sword, and Parrying at Defence 10, for about 5-6 rounds, you'll only need to worry about Exalted combatants, and that's what your party's Dawn is for.<br /> Hey, our social Lunar did fine for ages just using her Dex excellency, high stats, and a Daiklaive.<br /> <br /> When you get higher you do need to invest in some charms, but at that point you have the XP to spare.<br /> <br /> But, you know, charms are more interesting than just spamming dice pools, and you may be facing high-difficulty enemies, so there is value in having the MA on top of your more conceptual charms.<br /> It's a bit weird though, in terms of effects...<br /> <br /> Dawns, in my experience, rarely touch MA, because they're spending their charm XP on Melee (and, I guess hypothetically, Brawl or Archery or Thrown, but I've never seen that. Have seen a Dawn with a ton of War and Resistance and a bit of Melee and Archery). Solar XP goes on buying up Attributes, Abilities, or Evocations for their magic weapon.<br /> There's not really much point spending Solar XP on Martial Arts because it's not compatible with your other stuff.*<br /> <br /> *I suspect a build where you spend all your charm XP on Awareness, Athletics, Dodge and Resistance charms, and your Solar XP on your actual combat ability of Martial Arts, may actually be a stronger way to build a combat character. If combat is all you care about.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers, in my experience, rarely touch MA, because they need that Solar XP for spells. They'll go with something cheap, like Melee (good defence), or an ability that complements their combat spells (so... maybe still Melee, or maybe Brawl).<br /> <br /> Crafters, in my experience, want to use the high-quality weapons and armour they've made, so are generally packing a Melee and/or Archery weapon with the big armour they've forged, that MA often restricts. Or they may be a First Age Crafter, so then it's sorcery anyway. And they may make themselves a magic weapon and want to buy evocations. But most likely, their Solar XP goes on more Craft Abilities.<br /> (Or they might use MA. I've just not seen it.)<br /> <br /> But social characters, investigators, and stealthy thieves sometimes use Martial Arts. They may not care about the armour restrictions because they want to walk around talking to people, same with weapons.<br /> Though most social characters I've seen... still don't use Martial Arts actually, and spend their Solar/Lunar Xp on dots.<br /> <br /> The characters I've actually seen use Martial Arts in 3rd ed are a Zenith, an Eclipse, a Night, and a pseudo-Changing Moon. I've never seen a Dawn go near it.<br /> <br /> And I don't think it's weird that people who don't want to carry tons of armour and weapons with them want to use Martial Arts. But I do find it weird that it's not something that Dawns go for.<br /> <br /> I'm not suggesting a particular solution here. I just think it's interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-25-2019, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:55:44-08:00","id":1291973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291965#post1291965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing prevents lunars from learning or creating more training charms on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh.... I suspect that Wolf-Pack Training is deliberately worse than Tiger Warrior Training (though, actually some Lunar charms work really well in conjunction with Solar charms, as they give different benefits, so a Lunar and Solar working together can make a really awesome army), and that making a bunch of custom upgrades to make them as good at training soldiers quickly as Solars, isn't really something that's supposed to be doable.<br /> <br /> I think Clownpiece is somewhat over-exaggerating Solars' place in the setting, but they're not entirely wrong; there should be stuff that Solars are the best at, that Lunars can't replicate without a great deal of difficulty (in this case, training elite soldiers the old fashioned way), just as there's stuff Lunars are better at. And I think stuff for creating non-magical (once created) infrastructure, learning, organisations, etc, should definitely be part of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:23:02-08:00","id":1291988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291951#post1291951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also imagine if the default setting was the world-dominating empire as the PCs. And how much issues Exalted has had <i>as is</i> at times for imperial apolgia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I can't imagine the &quot;How do you feel knowing now that you were the REAL bad guys all along?!?&quot; being met by anything other than &quot;We fucking <i>weren't</i>!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291947#post1291947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That latter part isn't going to carry over into 3e (obviously, since it was an error), but without it, if you want the story of a Solar finding an SMA tutor to make sense, you need to grapple with these questions more seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't one of the draws of SMA that they can do really messed up stuff? Like Boarder of Kaleidoscopic Logic Style let you battle against your opponents using Virtues and Willpower and stuff. If there are things like that, even if they're not strictly speaking straight more powerful than CMA I can definitely see a lure to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291969#post1291969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't think it's weird that people who don't want to carry tons of armour and weapons with them want to use Martial Arts. But I do find it weird that it's not something that Dawns go for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually funny, the only duplicate Dawn Supernal I've ever seen was MA. The first alternated Single Point and White Reaper depending on how many foes they faced, and the second combined Crane and Steel Devil. Apart from that I've seen a Brawl, Melee, and Archery one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:33:07-08:00","id":1291990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291973#post1291973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Clownpiece is somewhat over-exaggerating Solars' place in the setting, but they're not entirely wrong; there should be stuff that Solars are the best at, that Lunars can't replicate without a great deal of difficulty (in this case, training elite soldiers the old fashioned way), just as there's stuff Lunars are better at. And I think stuff for creating non-magical (once created) infrastructure, learning, organisations, etc, should definitely be part of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And not just for setting reasons either, although them too. The much trotted around Solar motto is &quot;Everything you can do, I can do better.&quot; but the flip side of that coin is that very nearly anything a Solar can do every other Exalt can do too, at least in theme. The only thing that sets them apart a lot of the time is magnitude. All Exalts have charms for running faster, jumping higher, feats of strength, attacking multiple times in an action, shaping sorcery, convincing people, I could go on for a while here. One of the very few things that makes Solars special is that their charms can jack those abilities up to another level.<br /> <br /> Without that you're just a bland version of the other guys who can't shapechange, or slip between the threads of fate, or use Awareness charms to kill somebody's spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:38:20-08:00","id":1291996,"title":"","content":"I'm not exactly thrilled with either the tone or the direction of this thread. But I feel like its an important topic, and I want to throw in my 2 cents. A range of thoughts and concerns have been brought up with various levels of legitimacy, and I think they should be addressed. In part, because several important factors have been brought up and have started to cross with each other namely the pure mechanical question of how balanced that Lunars being able to combo martial arts charms with their own native charms and whether that will break these charms, the second is the question of whether it is balanced relative to the solars (and consequently, what is the proper relationship between the splats in terms of power level), and lastly how the balance relates to the setting as a whole (which is frankly, a far removed discussion from the purpose of this thread, but still a discussion worth having).<br /> <br /> So first, are Full-Moon combos (as I choose to call them) a serious problem balance wise? I'm not that worried about it. However, the reason that I am not particularly concerned is that I suspect that with the ever-expanding list of combos available to martial-artists the game will produce some 'unstoppable' combos or bizarre interactions as a matter of course. This is not an invitation to throw all such concerns to the wind, especially for highly idiosyncratic (and thus hard to combo) styles like Righteous Devil Style getting access to the accuracy and action economy of Lunar trees. As a matter of principle, I agree with Chung's perspective on exception-based rule-systems, but that should not be a paralyzing fear from designing a few more tools for everyone with each splat. We should measure the risks of breakage against the positive good it provides. It seems to me that without being allowed to make such combos martial arts would be a cripplingly poor option for most Lunars, and that would really suck for a great number of players.<br /> <br /> Second, is this balanced against the Solars in such a way that it allows said Solars to still be the masters of martial arts? This I confess, I do not know. I don't doubt that overall the solars are overall still more powerful combatants, though whether they are specifically the best martial artists is difficult to say. It will probably definitively not once Solars have Sidereal Martial Arts theoretically available. I will say that as a matter of pragmatism, the desire to narrow the gaps between the Exalt tiers will result in some combinations of what other Exalts are capable of to 'spike' above Solars in particular areas, even if Solars remain on a higher tier in general. It's worth remembering that with their broader Evocations, SMA combos, and mastery effects it strikes me as unlikely that Solars remain worse martial artists for long, even if we stipulate that Lunars are better at the moment.<br /> <br /> I will say I feel like a lot of people are forgetting the power of Supernal advantage combined with Mastery effects. People have correctly pointed out that until the advent of SMAs, Supernal Martial arts isn't super appealing and I tend to agree. A Martial Artist Solar taking the long view should probably be Resistance Supernal instead, since its highly tuned for combat already and combines well with MAs since it covers some of their main weaknesses. Plus Essence 1 gets you to the crucial form-charm for many builds as well as a nice little kit of combat powers, to begin with. I don't know that this makes them better 'martial artists' necessarily, but it assuages and concerns I have about the Solars as combatants more generally. <br /> <br /> The last big point of contention is how powerful Solars should be compared to the other splats as a matter of setting. I will confess that this is where I am most opinionated, even if its the most removed from the topic at hand. However, it strikes me that a lot of the people concerned that the Solars, and particularly the Dawn caste, being considered unimportant because they can't casually puree the other splats have a somewhat stilted view of what makes the solars such a force to be reckoned with, even at their limited numbers. The key factor is that, even if they are only marginally the best Exalt at something, they are marginally better at all such things, and thus they can act as a force-multiplier for one another.<br /> <br /> Consider if the solars were only Twilights and Zeniths, while they would be able to gather an enormous number of supporters or launch nukes at-will they would be assassinated almost immediately by their rival factions. However, in a circle the World's Greatest Sorceror (with nukes) is being backed up by the toughest bodyguard, his enemies being scouted and intercepted by an unrivaled spy, their Zenith rallies gods and men alike to their cause, and an unparalleled adventurer is helping them unearth powerful occult knowledge and spells. This is a Twilight-centric example of the same idea. You might imagine that a No-moon in some sort of Wizard-duel with a Twilight is a similarly close affair to how we talk about Full-moon v Dawn, with the Twilight having more raw power, but the Lunar having some additional charm-synergies and flexibility that they could potentially leverage for a win in the right situation.<br /> <br /> The Dawn-centric version of the same thought experiment is likely similar. When attempting to white-room a Full-moon it might be a 60-40 split favoring the Solar. But when their respective allies pour their resources to advantage their side (assuming a 'white world' with similar availability and risks to both sides), you end up with the better warrior with better morale and tutelage (Zenith), the better equipment (Twilight), better info and sabotage on their opponents (Night), and better Eclipse! (More seriously, the eclipse could also adventure for lost treasure or provide support for the others in a bunch of ways). In the 'white world duel,' the Dawn will likely smash the Full-moon, maybe even 2 Full moons that the circle supported. This goes for any endeavor.<br /> <br /> Note that this isn't like the cooperation of the Dragonblooded, where cooperation allows them to collectively create effects they aren't capable of individually. Solars each raise each other's abilities permanently in their core-competency the aid of a Twilight helps the Dawn solo a behemoth, and the materials the dawn provides access to do something similar to the Twilight. You might be able to get away with replacing a Dawn with a Full-Moon in a circle without too much disruption, but you can't replace all the Solars to get a similar effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:58:00-08:00","id":1292001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291973#post1291973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhhh.... I suspect that Wolf-Pack Training is deliberately worse than Tiger Warrior Training (though, actually some Lunar charms work really well in conjunction with Solar charms, as they give different benefits, so a Lunar and Solar working together can make a really awesome army), and that making a bunch of custom upgrades to make them as good at training soldiers quickly as Solars, isn't really something that's supposed to be doable.<br /> <br /> I think Clownpiece is somewhat over-exaggerating Solars' place in the setting, but they're not entirely wrong; there should be stuff that Solars are the best at, that Lunars can't replicate without a great deal of difficulty (in this case, training elite soldiers the old fashioned way), just as there's stuff Lunars are better at. And I think stuff for creating non-magical (once created) infrastructure, learning, organisations, etc, should definitely be part of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it won't be equal but i can see something like 7-9 dice + mutations. Mostly from reshaping people to be at their peak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T16:30:24-08:00","id":1292005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291947#post1291947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't need (and shouldn't get) a power boost relative to similarly top-tier Solar Brawl; but they can't fall <i>too</i> far behind.<br /> <br /> This is a problem if people want SMA-using Solars to be noticeably worse at SMA than Sidereals, who <i>themselves</i> are supposed to be slightly weaker than Brawl Solars - at that point, even accounting for the versatility of SMA, it becomes tricky to avoid a situation where the SMA using Solar is actually noticeably weaker in a fight than a Brawl one, which goes against the idea that SMA is this big valuable deal for Solar martial artists.<br /> <br /> There are various ways around this, but most of them require sacrificing some ground on the three points I mentioned above. Historically... Epimetheus is <i>sort of</i> right in the sense that SMA was always &quot;Solars are flatly worse than Sideraels at it and also pay bazillion XP, so if SMA was remotely balanced no Solar would seriously consider learning it except for flavor reasons.&quot; Of course, the corollary to this is that there has always been unbalanced SMA (so the answer to &quot;why would a Solar want to learn this&quot; has historically been &quot;well, these are actually notably stronger than any published Solar charms.&quot;)<br /> <br /> That latter part isn't going to carry over into 3e (obviously, since it was an error), but without it, if you want the story of a Solar finding an SMA tutor to make sense, you need to grapple with these questions more seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a tricky issue - I have to admit, my personal preference is that I just really don't care about the image of Sidereals being martial arts sifus to the Solars who make them stronger at MA than they would otherwise be.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer just to go the route of having Solars with Celestial MA just be on a level with Brawl anyway, which frankly IMO they should be anyway, without any of the kind of complexities SMA being important to the development of Solar Exalted martial arts specialists introduces. I'm not really a fan of the idea that Solars who use MA should be weaker without a Sidereal sifu than Solars who Brawl so that they can have a story of finding a Sidereal to be their sifu and become as powerful as a Solar who uses Brawl. (And if Solars with Celestial styles are already as strong as Brawl Solars, then there's no room for that &quot;Finding a sifu to learn SMA and this is a valuable big deal&quot; story to even make sense because you literally can't offer them any more power without putting them above Brawl Solars, which would be a really bad move. So it becomes a kind of thing of being able to pursue flavourful out of character magic which doesn't leverage a lot of strength.).<br /> <br /> When I look back at the 1e Sidereals version of SMA, the idea that Solars use them does not feel to me like it was ever really been a core part of what SMA was originally written to be, rather than more of an allowed thing, but without mechanical thought about making it work, and even then as an afterthought in the Player's Guide*. Sidereals as sifus to Solars, rather than more general mysterious advisers, hasn't really ever felt, an important part of their relationship. (The most iconic expression of that Sidereal-Solar sifu-student relationship is probably a few words written by Mike Goodwin on our message boards ages ago, which sold it really well... but it never had any serious mechanical support for how it would work within a solid rules environment.). <br /> <br /> So that's my bias. If they can find a way to make it work, then great for the folks who want to see it work, I'm just not too attached to it.<br /> <br /> *Specific section for historical reference stuff!: <br /> <br /> p239: &quot;<i>Solar Initiation Into the Blossoming Lotus: By dint of practice and meditation, Solar and Abyssal Exalted can learn Charms of the Blossoming of the Perfected Lotus, the Sidereal initiation, the ultimate circle of martial arts. However, they do not do so easily. As normal, they cannot learn without a tutor. Even with a tutor, their strong connection with forces in Creation slows their learning, and the study time is quadrupled. In addition, the pay 15 experience points per Charm or 13 if they favor the MA Ability. As form, these Exalted cannot learn the Form Charms or above of any Sidereal MA tree until they have mastered a Celestial style entirely.<br /> <br /> If this seems extreme, consider that it is easy compared to the difficulties the Dragon-Blooded face learning the Celestial-level martial arts. Celestials need not learn special Charms or undergo years of grueling tutelage. The greatest hurdle is the fact that they must find Sidereals willing to tutor them. There are practically none of these, for the Sidereals guard the secrets of their techniques jealously. Any Sidereal who taught techniques to a Celestial would be under the gravest legal risk and generally seen as a trait to the Five-Score Fellowship's innermost secrets. Non-Sidereal individuals who have learned Sidereal martial arts will be marked for death by the Sidereals as a group. The Gold Faction has not yet taught its Solar proteges in the Cult of the Illuminated's training camps Charms of this type, but they are always weighing the option</i>&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T17:18:16-08:00","id":1292020,"title":"","content":"I mean, one last thing (hopefully) on the SMA tangent (which is a faaar future question really), it may be pretty important for the developers will be a deep consideration of Sidereal MA away from the how they have drifted in fan consciousness to &quot;Sidereal power level breaking ultra MA that Solars want!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Originally I think maybe the vibe was that their original presentation where Jenna M just seemed to think that SMA she'd built were like that because this is just the level *all* elder high Essence Charms would be pitched at, and she did not think that SMA were necessarily particularly effective and even perhaps less effective than what Solars would have at that level. SMA were just the Sidereals way to get there, including more weird Sidereal factor than comparable Solar magic would have.<br /> <br /> So really it's maybe more like getting back to that, with a better conception of what balance means and the scale the system is built to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T18:18:35-08:00","id":1292039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292005#post1292005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd prefer just to go the route of having Solars with Celestial MA just be on a level with Brawl anyway, which frankly IMO they should be anyway, without any of the kind of complexities SMA being important to the development of Solar Exalted martial arts specialists introduces. I'm not really a fan of the idea that Solars who use MA should be weaker without a Sidereal sifu than Solars who Brawl so that they can have a story of finding a Sidereal to be their sifu and become as powerful as a Solar who uses Brawl. (And if Solars with Celestial styles are already as strong as Brawl Solars, then there's no room for that &quot;Finding a sifu to learn SMA and this is a valuable big deal&quot; story to even make sense because you literally can't offer them any more power without putting them above Brawl Solars, which would be a really bad move. So it becomes a kind of thing of being able to pursue flavourful out of character magic which doesn't leverage a lot of strength.).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I may be in the minority, but I think that a Solar who learns and masters an SMA should be distinctly more powerful than the solar who uses brawl, mostly because the level of investment is that much higher. The main reason that I say this is basically just the sheer level of investment and restrictions that is required to be a Solar SMA user compared to Brawl (or anything else, really). The SMA user has at least gotten to their essence legitimately instead of supernal shortcuts, has mastered at least 1 style (probably more), bought at least 2 abilities up to 5 (MA1 and SMA1), bought a 4 dot merit, bought a 5 dot merit (at least) for the willing sifu, probably something else we don't even know about for the Initiation into the Blossoming Lotus. Furthermore, unlike brawl SMAs have usually excluded the use of armor (and often weapons if you want to have really crazy combos), so the brawl user can be using heavy armor, smash fists, and maybe a shield of some sort ()<br /> <br /> However, I still don't want their power to be the reality-shattering nonsense it was before. Moreover, SMAs are probably more narrowly-applicable or have some other caveats that make Solar Brawl a more reliable choice. But seriously given how much SMAs require, both in investment and opportunity cost, it's hard to argue from my perspective that they should still be in some way weaker than punching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T21:02:32-08:00","id":1292064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292005#post1292005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is a tricky issue - I have to admit, my personal preference is that I just really don't care about the image of Sidereals being martial arts sifus to the Solars who make them stronger at MA than they would otherwise be.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer just to go the route of having Solars with Celestial MA just be on a level with Brawl anyway, which frankly IMO they should be anyway, without any of the kind of complexities SMA being important to the development of Solar Exalted martial arts specialists introduces. I'm not really a fan of the idea that Solars who use MA should be weaker without a Sidereal sifu than Solars who Brawl so that they can have a story of finding a Sidereal to be their sifu and become as powerful as a Solar who uses Brawl. (And if Solars with Celestial styles are already as strong as Brawl Solars, then there's no room for that &quot;Finding a sifu to learn SMA and this is a valuable big deal&quot; story to even make sense because you literally can't offer them any more power without putting them above Brawl Solars, which would be a really bad move. So it becomes a kind of thing of being able to pursue flavourful out of character magic which doesn't leverage a lot of strength.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but what many people are effectively advocating is that a Solar who learns SMA should be, overall, <i>less</i> powerful than a Solar who just learns non-SMA martial arts. Pre-errata 2e went this route - obviously SMA in 2e was broken and mechanically dysfunctional, but 13 / 15 XP a charm wasn't a serious offer, it was &quot;haha, fuck you for wanting this.&quot; The second part of the relevant sidebar you quoted even half-heartedly acknowledges this (though it's flat-out wrong, of course, when comparing it to Terrestrials learning CMA, which didn't require nearly as exclusive a tutor, didn't charge remotely such absurd XP, and required some level of barriers for balance reasons because it was supposed to be <i>more</i> powerful than DB native charms rather than <i>less</i>.) Like most of the screwups in 2e, it was probably written by someone who only vaguely understood the underlying mechanics; and it was later errataed to sane XP cost.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point is: If you're going to allow Solars to learn SMA from a Sidereal tutor, it should at least be a sane, reasonable option for it. Spending XP through the nose for &quot;versatility&quot; doesn't make any sense at all (especially in a world with both sorcery and evocations, not to mention Sorcerous Workings and regular martial arts to diversify yourself with using the same XP.) Obviously SMA can't actually make a Solar stronger than a, well, Solar, that's a given, but if it's going to be an option then it can't be an actively <i>bad</i> place to spend your XP.<br /> <br /> Regarding your other quote, I don't see how you could interpret that to mean Solars learning SMA wasn't a big deal. It implies that Sidereals were willing to <i>murder</i> over it. (Granted, Sidereals have sometimes been portrayed as perhaps a bit too murder-happy.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I may be in the minority, but I think that a Solar who learns and masters an SMA should be distinctly more powerful than the solar who uses brawl, mostly because the level of investment is that much higher. </div> </div> </div>This is also an option (sort of), provided the &quot;investment&quot; balances out overall. But in practice it's pretty unworkable - first, SMA has to primarily be designed for use by Sidereals, limiting what you can do to fine-tune its balance for Solars to the extent that this would require. Second, what the &quot;investment&quot; means varies a lot from game to game depending on how long the game goes on and so forth, which could lead to weird issues. Third, you have to ask if the investment part is fun.<br /> <br /> The reality is that balance isn't some precise science or anything like that - as long as the wheels aren't falling off the game, it's the <i>feel</i> that matters as much as anything else. You can make SMA feel powerful for both Sidereals and Solars without really having it break the game or be a strictly-mechanically-superior option to Solar Brawl. My objection is that the mechanical design does send a message in terms of how the game &quot;feels&quot; and its overall thematics - if the message is &quot;Solars shouldn't be learning SMA&quot;, then you've lost the thread of why Sidereals were able to teach it to them in the first place.<br /> <br /> (And it's also bad design because it amounts to ugly back-and-forth between different writers and developers - ie. one person said Solars can learn SMA, and another plainly didn't like that, that so they made it possible but with costs or limitations that would make it a punishing experience in actual play. This was almost certainly the story of the 13/15 XP cost, say. Aaand I'm sure it's how some people in this thread feel. But the mechanics should try and make the stories the game offers play out smoothly and in a fun fashion - if the game says &quot;Solars can learn SMA, and it's a big deal for them&quot;, then it has to at least <i>feel</i> like a triumph for a Solar to learn it. If it's as heavy-handed as costing 13 XP a pop for charms that are weaker than your native ones, players are going to notice and not have much fun following that route.)<br /> <br /> As long as SMA used by Solars is roughly within eyeball distance of going with native Solar charms, though, the <i>exact</i> differences won't matter, especially if eg. SMA has a lot of pop-off-the-page powerful feeling stuff that's actually more brittle than it looks at first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-26-2019, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T22:21:59-08:00","id":1292075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292064#post1292064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is also an option (sort of), provided the &quot;investment&quot; balances out overall. But in practice it's pretty unworkable - first, SMA has to primarily be designed for use by Sidereals, limiting what you can do to fine-tune its balance for Solars to the extent that this would require. Second, what the &quot;investment&quot; means varies a lot from game to game depending on how long the game goes on and so forth, which could lead to weird issues. Third, you have to ask if the investment part is fun.<br /> <br /> The reality is that balance isn't some precise science or anything like that - as long as the wheels aren't falling off the game, it's the <i>feel</i> that matters as much as anything else. You can make SMA feel powerful for both Sidereals and Solars without really having it break the game or be a strictly-mechanically-superior option to Solar Brawl. My objection is that the mechanical design does send a message in terms of how the game &quot;feels&quot; and its overall thematics - if the message is &quot;Solars shouldn't be learning SMA&quot;, then you've lost the thread of why Sidereals were able to teach it to them in the first place.<br /> <br /> (And it's also bad design because it amounts to ugly back-and-forth between different writers and developers - ie. one person said Solars can learn SMA, and another plainly didn't like that, that so they made it possible but with costs or limitations that would make it a punishing experience in actual play. This was almost certainly the story of the 13/15 XP cost, say. Aaand I'm sure it's how some people in this thread feel. But the mechanics should try and make the stories the game offers play out smoothly and in a fun fashion - if the game says &quot;Solars can learn SMA, and it's a big deal for them&quot;, then it has to at least <i>feel</i> like a triumph for a Solar to learn it. If it's as heavy-handed as costing 13 XP a pop for charms that are weaker than your native ones, players are going to notice and not have much fun following that route.)<br /> <br /> As long as SMA used by Solars is roughly within eyeball distance of going with native Solar charms, though, the <i>exact</i> differences won't matter, especially if eg. SMA has a lot of pop-off-the-page powerful feeling stuff that's actually more brittle than it looks at first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that I disagree with your conception of 'balance' but there are a bunch of reasons SMAs could be a 'strictly better' mechanical option in some senses, while still being not an obviously-always-correct choice. For instance, a Solar SMA master squaring off against a Solar Brawl Master, naked in a white room with just vanilla charms might heavily favor the SMA user. However, when we consider the fact that the Brawl master will have had more experience to invest in dedicated defenses (i.e. dodge &amp; resistance), auxiliary abilities (Stealth, Athletics, etc.), artifacts, evocations, spells/workings (conceivably), or familiars/followers/steeds (admittedly no one I know has ever considered mounted brawl). This is not even touching on whether or not the player feels like diversifying into abilities that are non-combat in order to interact with the game in ways that don't involve personally killing something, or purchasing non-cannon expansions in Brawl. <br /> <br /> Basically, there are a lot of ways the Brawl player could spend those resources to make them better (or at least different enough to be incomparable) at their core-competency of 'combat' beyond what the SMA user is capable of. However, the SMA user might still have specialized tactics or advantages that it could use to beat the Brawler if is able to leverage them effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T00:28:32-08:00","id":1292088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292001#post1292001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it won't be equal but i can see something like 7-9 dice + mutations. Mostly from reshaping people to be at their peak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, more mutation points, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T02:32:40-08:00","id":1292098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291969#post1291969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I will say in response to Aluminiumtrioxid, that until you get into Essence 3 at least, dabbling in combat abilities is fine with 5 in a Combat Ability and an excellency. That'll actually be fine for combat for ages. You won't be a combat master, but when you're rolling, say, 20 dice (assuming Dex 4) with your staff or sword, and Parrying at Defence 10, for about 5-6 rounds, you'll only need to worry about Exalted combatants, and that's what your party's Dawn is for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Hey, if you want to play a non-combat character, just pick an ability score that reflects being one of Creation's greatest warriors&quot; is oft-repeated but, in my opinion, also tremendously wrong-headed advice.<br /> <br /> But then again, I also think the somewhat popular view that &quot;actually, everybody should just have 5s in everything without thinking about what that means, because your REAL SKILL is charms anyway&quot; is gameline cancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T02:41:50-08:00","id":1292100,"title":"","content":"Well... I mean, yes, I agree with you, but I'm not sure what that has to do with buying MA with Solar XP, which is the point you brought up I was responding to.<br /> <br /> Generally, the first two charms need 2 or 3 in the Ability, and then you start needing 4 or 5 to get a style's charms anyway.<br /> <br /> And honestly, often the first charm or two aren't really worth as much as buying 8/10xp's worth of Ability dots anyway. (If it's not favoured, it's probably worth getting 1 charm for the excellency.)<br /> <br /> Now, if Martial Arts trees were all rewritten so you could buy half the tree's charms with an Ability of 3, then I could see it.<br /> <br /> But as it is, anyone who's spending their Solar XP on buying Martial Arts is pretty quickly going to have 4 or even 5 in their Martial Arts ability.<br /> <br /> I was going to start the game with Snake 3 for my Lunar doctor, but realised I could only buy 2 charms (one of which is pretty meh anyway).<br /> <br /> My Zenith monk is an occultist and investigator who started with Dex 2 and no combat abilities at all. His regular XP's been on Investigation, Integrity, Occult and Craft charms.<br /> I've been spending his Solar XP on various abilities and Tiger Style (another PC had it, so taught him). I had to buy up to 4 pretty quickly in order to get the form. I deliberately avoided having 5 dots for ages because it felt wrong, but I had all this Solar XP, and couldn't buy quite a few of the charms without it, so ended up with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T03:16:43-08:00","id":1292103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292064#post1292064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, my point is: If you're going to allow Solars to learn SMA from a Sidereal tutor, it should at least be a sane, reasonable option for it. Spending XP through the nose for &quot;versatility&quot; doesn't make any sense at all (especially in a world with both sorcery and evocations, not to mention Sorcerous Workings and regular martial arts to diversify yourself with using the same XP.) Obviously SMA can't actually make a Solar stronger than a, well, Solar, that's a given, but if it's going to be an option then it can't be an actively <i>bad</i> place to spend your XP.<br /> <br /> Regarding your other quote, I don't see how you could interpret that to mean Solars learning SMA wasn't a big deal. It implies that Sidereals were willing to <i>murder</i> over it. (Granted, Sidereals have sometimes been portrayed as perhaps a bit too murder-happy.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree that definitely however SMA *is* telegraphed for Solars when it's properly and fully described needs to be followed up by mechanics.<br /> <br /> (As discussed I'm actually OK with &quot;These secret super style are not built for Solar Exalted, and though you can learn them, it is perhaps not your best option&quot;. Transcending your natural *level* through MA through tutelage of the Sidereals as an important element for Dragonblooded, probably yes, for Solars, probably not so much.<br /> <br /> It's basically what seems to happen with Immaculate MA and I'm OK with that, and it avoids two-tier Solar MA where SMA tutored Solars are better than merely Celestial MA using Solars, or two-tier Solars generally where SMA tutored Solars are better than other combat focused Solars.)<br /> <br /> But whatever is shown up front should be followed through with; it's obviously not a good idea to sell players SMA as an upgrade for MA using Solars and actually find in play it's a downgrade or even they are just roughly equal to Celestial MA and more generally not particularly amazing and impressive for them.<br /> <br /> Re; this Players Guide quote, I have to admit that I read its Sidereal death squad comments very much in a spirit of &quot;Solars are not actually meant to learn this and get a tutor in your game if you don't want&quot; (though with some hilarity at the &quot;When were Sidereals not meant to be trying to slay the Solars again?&quot; aspect). To me it's strongly de-emphasizing that any &quot;Sidereals serve as as sifus to Solars&quot; is any degree a setting element that you can expect (that doubles down to me in turn on this not being very important to preserve). But you could read it as &quot;Encouragement, but with consequences&quot; alternatively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T04:16:52-08:00","id":1292106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292098#post1292098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, if you want to play a non-combat character, just pick an ability score that reflects being one of Creation's greatest warriors&quot; is oft-repeated but, in my opinion, also tremendously wrong-headed advice.<br /> <br /> But then again, I also think the somewhat popular view that &quot;actually, everybody should just have 5s in everything without thinking about what that means, because your REAL SKILL is charms anyway&quot; is gameline cancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, I get what you're saying, but having 5 dots in a combat ability does <i>not</i> mean you are one of creation's greatest warriors. It just doesn't. <br /> <br /> I do agree that having 5 dots means something. It means that you have reached the pinnacle of what mortals can do. Charms, however, are about surpassing that pinnacle. So, if you have a charm in something, then suddenly 5 dots is less of a big deal, I think? <br /> <br /> What I'm saying is, I think that you shouldn't just take 5 dots by default, but you shouldn't be afraid of them either. And if you have charms in something at all, then limiting your dots in it to portray that it's not something your character is superhumanly good at is a fools errand. That ship has sailed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T06:28:09-08:00","id":1292134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292098#post1292098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, if you want to play a non-combat character, just pick an ability score that reflects being one of Creation's greatest warriors&quot; is oft-repeated but, in my opinion, also tremendously wrong-headed advice.<br /> <br /> But then again, I also think the somewhat popular view that &quot;actually, everybody should just have 5s in everything without thinking about what that means, because your REAL SKILL is charms anyway&quot; is gameline cancer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get what you're saying, but on a practical level, you can't really get even to Essense 2 charms w/o a 5 in the skill for pretty much any combat ability. which means a dabbler will have to hit 5 by essence 3 if they don't want to become irrelevant in that aspect of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T07:16:26-08:00","id":1292150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292088#post1292088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, more mutation points, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps but I was referring to how lunars can already reshape people you could easily upgrade that to alter attributes, technically the upgrade charm to flesh sculpting art should allow it, because those are all physical in nature.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T07:20:10-08:00","id":1292152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292100#post1292100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... I mean, yes, I agree with you, but I'm not sure what that has to do with buying MA with Solar XP, which is the point you brought up I was responding to.<br /> <br /> Generally, the first two charms need 2 or 3 in the Ability, and then you start needing 4 or 5 to get a style's charms anyway.<br /> <br /> And honestly, often the first charm or two aren't really worth as much as buying 8/10xp's worth of Ability dots anyway. (If it's not favoured, it's probably worth getting 1 charm for the excellency.)<br /> <br /> Now, if Martial Arts trees were all rewritten so you could buy half the tree's charms with an Ability of 3, then I could see it.<br /> <br /> But as it is, anyone who's spending their Solar XP on buying Martial Arts is pretty quickly going to have 4 or even 5 in their Martial Arts ability.<br /> <br /> I was going to start the game with Snake 3 for my Lunar doctor, but realised I could only buy 2 charms (one of which is pretty meh anyway).<br /> <br /> My Zenith monk is an occultist and investigator who started with Dex 2 and no combat abilities at all. His regular XP's been on Investigation, Integrity, Occult and Craft charms.<br /> I've been spending his Solar XP on various abilities and Tiger Style (another PC had it, so taught him). I had to buy up to 4 pretty quickly in order to get the form. I deliberately avoided having 5 dots for ages because it felt wrong, but I had all this Solar XP, and couldn't buy quite a few of the charms without it, so ended up with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it seems like a lot of the charms should be lowered in ability/attribute just because it feels like a game story difference. Tons of trees require 5 ability at Essence 2. One thing that stuck out to me in Sidereals was that a lot of the time that didn't happen with them. They got Ability 3, Essence 3 tools, hell they got ability 3 Essence 4 charms sometimes if I remember correctly. The scaling let people pick charms up without a heavy ability commitment and it feels more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T09:34:33-08:00","id":1292190,"title":"","content":"I noticed that the prerequisites in Dragonblood are lower than for Solars, and even lower for Lunars. Lunars do have a number of charms that only need 3 dots at Essence 2 and 3.<br /> (And Lunars tend to have high ratings anyway, as they get a free dot in everything; even your worst set of attributes is probably 2/3/3. Though I guess Solars tend to have high ratings in stuff they care about, since you can start with up to 7 Abilities at 5.)<br /> <br /> I was building my Lunar, Dr Soma the Kung-fu Doctor, as a starting character (to then put her XP on top), and I started with Intelligence 4, thinking I'd have to buy it up to 5. But I've found that all the Medicine charms I want actually only need Intelligence 4. And unless I want to make Artefacts, I don't even need 5 for Crafting either. I can churn out Major projects in minutes, collect lots of Craft XP, and have lots of Craft dots, with just Int 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:03:43-08:00","id":1292201,"title":"","content":"I may be wrong but I feel that lunars ability to combine their own charms with martial arts charms redefines the mastery keyword purpose and like the OP that martial arts we'll see in later books won't necessarilly have the problems we're seeing now. We may be wrong but now we have some kind of opportunity to start to see how things are going now, I hope today's preview will help us at least a little. This lunar ability implies to me that we can't know precisely how powerful lunar martial artists at essence 4-5 will be when compared to the others nor do we know how later mastery effects for sidereals and solars will perform at those essence levels and what these martial arts will means in term of design &quot;philosophy&quot; (I don't know if I have the right to use that word here) making of the sidereal martial arts what makes the solars and the sidereals the best martial artists may or may not be the most interesting thing to me depending of that.<br /> <br /> Since I'm kind of a newbie with exalted I don't really know what sidereal martial arts exactly looks like but according to what everyone is saying it seems that it's supposed to be powerful but there is lots of way to make something powerful the same way powerful means lots of different things and lots of them don't means that essence 3-5 lunars should particularly lose more than the others because of being lunar martial artists. I sincerely hope that things will go that way and I think that it's completely feasible while having sidereals and solars having almost equal performances using normal martial arts and having powerful sidereal martial arts.<br /> <br /> What worries me the most with this &quot;martial art&quot; thing is the way always caring about how lunars charms may affect anything we'll want to create may act as a huge constraint to creativity too (mechanically speaking) in a game where there is lots of things to create already. Balancing seems surmountable to me even with lunars and I think that if the problem is as big as we think, the devs and the community will find a solution to make everything easier before the final draft appears.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291973#post1291973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Clownpiece is somewhat over-exaggerating Solars' place in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm repeating myself here but i don't think that making assumptions about how the game should be played, affecting players concerns and expectations about that should be made out of setting &quot;facts&quot; rather than just what is satisfying or not to them while playing the game and how it may be legitimate or not. I may be wrong but settings facts never affected how my players and I arbitrated and posed problems in the game, charms did, the way we used the setting did, the rules did too but not the fact that most of the exalted needs decades to attain essence 3 or 4 for example.<br /> It may be because of the fact I'm new to exalted but it looks to me a little bit too much like purism to bring this kind of thing rather than the fact that every player should be satisfied playing in a game where solars, lunars and maybe sidereals PCs are together.<br /> And if it's indirectly expressing some players concerns, I think that there is some kind of legitimacy in Clownpiece's complaints despite the fact that I also think that there is a part of catastrophizing in it. (I may be wrong but I think that there is a little bit of involuntary pretexting when he's justifying himself with setting &quot;facts&quot; too but I'll stop any ridiculous attempt at mind-reading. ^^ )<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291990#post1291990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And not just for setting reasons either, although them too. The much trotted around Solar motto is &quot;Everything you can do, I can do better.&quot; but the flip side of that coin is that very nearly anything a Solar can do every other Exalt can do too, at least in theme. The only thing that sets them apart a lot of the time is magnitude. All Exalts have charms for running faster, jumping higher, feats of strength, attacking multiple times in an action, shaping sorcery, convincing people, I could go on for a while here. One of the very few things that makes Solars special is that their charms can jack those abilities up to another level.<br /> <br /> Without that you're just a bland version of the other guys who can't shapechange, or slip between the threads of fate, or use Awareness charms to kill somebody's spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'll say is completely off topic but not being knowledgeable about Exalted, I have the feeling that thinking the solars as only being the best does not serve them that much nor does it fits enough their thematics to me. It's possible that I redefined them while reading the first book with something like a confirmation bias but the first thing I felt was not that they were being the absolute best but the most heroic, glorious and legendary one because of being about doing miraculous things rather than performing better than the lunars and the sidereals, the most powerful exigents and maybe lots of others. An example of what made me feel more and more justified in my way of seeing this was the first solar medicine charm in the book where the most important part in the text to me was not the fact that the charm was efficient but the fact that the charm was capable to heal the great contagion which almost killed everyone before. Another example which comes easily to my mind while staying easily explainable with my bad english is the difference between solar and celestial circles sorcery. But lots of those charms made me think the solars that way before looking at the new lunars charms.<br /> The idea that the solars are just the strongest is a completely legitimate interpretation to me but I have the feeling that it's clearly not the most satisfying one for my games and I think that they don't need to always be the strongest to be fun. Just working on the thematics of heroic, glorious and miraculous seems enough to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm rereading the part when I was answering to Wizard of Oz and I'm really sorry about how it looks like I'm blaming or something while I was just saying that it looks off topic to me. I completely see how respecting facts affect a party, it's just that I don't see how it concerns everyone in this topic.<br /> Going off topic is not a problem either but I feel that it's already been almost half the topic being about that. (And it was clearly not because of Wizard of Oz.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","user":"RosePlancton","date":". 02-26-2019, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:24:25-08:00","id":1292204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RosePlancton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292201#post1292201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What worries me the most with this &quot;martial art&quot; thing is the way always caring about how lunars charms may affect anything we'll want to create may act as a huge constraint to creativity too (mechanically speaking) in a game where there is lots of things to create already. Balancing seems surmountable to me even with lunars and I think that if the problem is as big as we think, the devs and the community will find a solution to make everything easier before the final draft appears.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, not including lunar books, we current have 19 MA's of which all but 3 can used unarmed and therefore combined. If we include lunars we have another 8 confirmed which all will also be unarmed styles. That'll be 24 different charms set that can be mixed together and there are likely many more to come. The idea that there wont be some overpowered interactions on par with whatever mixing Lunar and MA charms can produce seems kinda unlikely and once we get SMA it'll be even more likely. Ultimately i think its better we focus on the positives of making MA attractive to Lunars and less about what potentailly overpowered combinations because in a game as complex as Exalted its gonna happen but as long as its not game-breaking (infinite perfect defence ect) then i think we just have to deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:37:04-08:00","id":1292212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargle18446</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292204#post1292204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, not including lunar books, we current have 19 MA's of which all but 3 can used unarmed and therefore combined. If we include lunars we have another 8 confirmed which all will also be unarmed styles. That'll be 24 different charms set that can be mixed together and there are likely many more to come. The idea that there wont be some overpowered interactions on par with whatever mixing Lunar and MA charms can produce seems kinda unlikely and once we get SMA it'll be even more likely. Ultimately i think its better we focus on the positives of making MA attractive to Lunars and less about what potentailly overpowered combinations because in a game as complex as Exalted its gonna happen but as long as its not game-breaking (infinite perfect defence ect) then i think we just have to deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I think that getting rid of things which may very probably be frustrating or game-breaking (almost game-breaking too) is enough to me at least. Maybe as long as It avoids me some kind of balance paranoia too when I create things for my players but it may be me the problem here. I don't know. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T10:51:52-08:00","id":1292219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292190#post1292190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed that the prerequisites in Dragonblood are lower than for Solars, and even lower for Lunars. Lunars do have a number of charms that only need 3 dots at Essence 2 and 3.<br /> (And Lunars tend to have high ratings anyway, as they get a free dot in everything; even your worst set of attributes is probably 2/3/3. Though I guess Solars tend to have high ratings in stuff they care about, since you can start with up to 7 Abilities at 5.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a logical consequence of Solars being heavily focused on the idea of their charms representing &quot;skill&quot;, ie. you have to actually be highly skilled to use them, whereas DB charms are slightly more cheaty magic stuff. Thematically, you can have a DB who is only sort-of good with a sword but who fills the gaps with their magic, whereas that makes no sense at all for a Solar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T11:07:56-08:00","id":1292222,"title":"","content":"What does everyone think about the investment and mote cost issue behind the whole thing?<br /> <br /> For example Solars might have an MA charm that\u2019s a damage adder, adding (Strength) damage or (Strength + Stamina) with Mastery. Lunars on the other hand can just throw on a strength based damage adder and combo for a better effect at the costsmore motes and requiring a purchase of those strength charms. As a baseline that\u2019s something Solars can\u2019t do, and might lead to a more powerful effect at the cost of purchasing more charms and spending more motes. Is that a problem? Because it might be used for styles and in ways that the Solar can\u2019t also do by picking up another charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T11:52:58-08:00","id":1292229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292222#post1292222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does everyone think about the investment and mote cost issue behind the whole thing?<br /> <br /> For example Solars might have an MA charm that\u2019s a damage adder, adding (Strength) damage or (Strength + Stamina) with Mastery. Lunars on the other hand can just throw on a strength based damage adder and combo for a better effect at the costsmore motes and requiring a purchase of those strength charms. As a baseline that\u2019s something Solars can\u2019t do, and might lead to a more powerful effect at the cost of purchasing more charms and spending more motes. Is that a problem? Because it might be used for styles and in ways that the Solar can\u2019t also do by picking up another charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well one of the things it does, which is an interesting side-effect though not really related to balance directly, is that it allows Lunars to gain a lot more leverage out of individual Martial Arts than Solars. When you compare that to the fact that solars have to buy up an entirely new skill to get access to access similar combo potential. This might actually go the other direction and make the xp-power a better overall investment for the lunar. However, the Solars get a multiplicative effect by adding on multiple mastery effects, and better auxiliary charms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T13:29:11-08:00","id":1292251,"title":"","content":"I honestly think that with the charms Solars are allowed to combine with M.A. perhaps simply having a ruling that if a martial arts charm doesn't have a mastery written into the style the solar/abyssal/etc. who can gain the mastery effect can write one out for the ST to look over and okay. The only exception to this is the Immaculate styles.<br /> <br /> I think it'd help sell it a bit more on Solar power itself without the need to change anything too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T13:48:26-08:00","id":1292257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292222#post1292222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example Solars might have an MA charm that\u2019s a damage adder, adding (Strength) damage or (Strength + Stamina) with Mastery. Lunars on the other hand can just throw on a strength based damage adder and combo for a better effect at the costs more motes and requiring a purchase of those strength charms. As a baseline that\u2019s something Solars can\u2019t do, and might lead to a more powerful effect at the cost of purchasing more charms and spending more motes. Is that a problem? Because it might be used for styles and in ways that the Solar can\u2019t also do by picking up another charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite following this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, not including lunar books, we current have 19 MA's of which all but 3 can used unarmed and therefore combined. If we include lunars we have another 8 confirmed which all will also be unarmed styles. That'll be 24 different charms set that can be mixed together and there are likely many more to come. The idea that there wont be some overpowered interactions on par with whatever mixing Lunar and MA charms can produce seems kinda unlikely </div> </div> </div>With my starting Lunar I can punch people for 25 withering damage. Using... only Martial Arts charms (and not even spending WP, just some motes), not Strength charms. At that point, I'm not even sure I need Strength charms (I mean, I'll spend 2 motes for +2 damage with the Strength excellency, but it's hardly worth buying another charm).<br /> At Essence 3 I'll be able to punch them for 27... ignoring armour, and then stripping off another 3 initiative.<br /> And it could be higher, if I'd cheesed it more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a logical consequence of Solars being heavily focused on the idea of their charms representing &quot;skill&quot;, ie. you have to actually be highly skilled to use them, whereas DB charms are slightly more cheaty magic stuff. Thematically, you can have a DB who is only sort-of good with a sword but who fills the gaps with their magic, whereas that makes no sense at all for a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sure.<br /> Still, it does make Solar character sheets boring. When I was running it, I could pretty much guarentee my players had 5 in every Ability they were rolling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T17:04:09-08:00","id":1292299,"title":"","content":"To be honest, Ability prerequisites seem pretty loosely related to any Charm function and whether that Charm function seems to need skill or not - I'd scratch my head if trying to explain in detail why any of the Solar 'Essence Charged Arrow Attack' type Charms would actually *need* any particular level of skill. They just seem to be like that because that's the game design wants them to be restricted to characters who've met a certain level of investment, not because there's any obvious reason in setting why it should be so. (There's a rewrite of Exalted rules that does away with Ability pre-requisites for merely different dot based experience costs, and I'm hard pressed to think that even Solars on the page feel particularly different).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T18:05:17-08:00","id":1292311,"title":"","content":"I find it amazing how people are able to convince themselves that &quot;Man, [character type] is the BOMB&quot; is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;But broken combos!&quot; Why yes, I too enjoy Mastered Seven Points of Weakness Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike (The Combo Your Combo Could Smell Like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T20:50:55-08:00","id":1292361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292257#post1292257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not quite following this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I was groggy when I wrote that. What I mean is kind of what you were already saying. MA are often able to be combined together for bigger bonuses, but they have restrictions based off form weapons and stuff. Especially ones like Righteous Devil and Steel Devil. Lunars can always combine them with their native charms. So that's kind of something everyone else can do anyway, just with different MAs, so they kind of already have to be balanced around the idea that combining can happen. Except sometimes for forms with really specific weapons that are required.<br /> <br /> So on the one hand there's Lunars being better at MA than Solars, but only by purchasing a bunch of native charms, and even then their combos are going to run them a lot more motes and willpower. Like if a Lunar wants to deal as much damage as a Solar with a MA attack, they can pump their strength excellency in it, but then they're spending more motes so it's not really like they're better? Since the Solar might get that for free with Mastery.<br /> <br /> But also I'm not sure if those MAs that were designed with really strict form weapons weren't designed with the idea that they'd be hard to combo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T20:55:30-08:00","id":1292364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292311#post1292311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it amazing how people are able to convince themselves that &quot;Man, [character type] is the BOMB&quot; is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;But broken combos!&quot; Why yes, I too enjoy Mastered Seven Points of Weakness Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike (The Combo Your Combo Could Smell Like).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that you are mischaracterizing the concern a bit. The concern isn't 'Lunar Martial Artists are Sweet, but I would prefer them to suck' the concerns raised in this thread have been 'opening up combos with lunar native charms inevitably is going to make it much harder not to break Lunar Martial Artists in the future, if they aren't already broken now', 'lunar martial artists are going to be the one-true-build for combat-focused lunar characters, which would be sad and overcentralizing', 'this might make lunars the most powerful martial artists, which conflicts with the lore that Sidereals/Solaroids are the best martial artists', and lastly 'this might make it so that Dawn martial artists don't destroy Full-Moon Martial Artists as easily as they should'. <br /> <br /> Some of these critiques are more valid than others, certainly. But I suspect that everyone in this thread is on-board with the idea that more cool-and-viable character concepts = better game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T20:59:57-08:00","id":1292365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292311#post1292311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it amazing how people are able to convince themselves that &quot;Man, [character type] is the BOMB&quot; is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;But broken combos!&quot; Why yes, I too enjoy Mastered Seven Points of Weakness Armor-Penetrating Fang Strike (The Combo Your Combo Could Smell Like).</div> </div> </div> </div>In defense of not wanting broken comboes, it's not always for some asinine reason like the ST not wanting the PCs to be awesome. Sometimes it is 100%, but <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U1MnMA0TzGI\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> scene would have been kind of crappy if it had just started out with Luke snatching his lightsaber up and double killing the Emperor and Vader in the first 10 seconds.<br /> <br /> I personally love it when my PCs are awesome, but sometimes some foes should be worthy of getting more than a single action in a battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T21:25:10-08:00","id":1292368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292361#post1292361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry I was groggy when I wrote that. What I mean is kind of what you were already saying. MA are often able to be combined together for bigger bonuses, but they have restrictions based off form weapons and stuff. Especially ones like Righteous Devil and Steel Devil. Lunars can always combine them with their native charms. So that's kind of something everyone else can do anyway, just with different MAs, so they kind of already have to be balanced around the idea that combining can happen. Except sometimes for forms with really specific weapons that are required.<br /> <br /> So on the one hand there's Lunars being better at MA than Solars, but only by purchasing a bunch of native charms, and even then their combos are going to run them a lot more motes and willpower. Like if a Lunar wants to deal as much damage as a Solar with a MA attack, they can pump their strength excellency in it, but then they're spending more motes so it's not really like they're better? Since the Solar might get that for free with Mastery.<br /> <br /> But also I'm not sure if those MAs that were designed with really strict form weapons weren't designed with the idea that they'd be hard to combo?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been having similar thoughts, and here's my 2c. Righteous Devil Style is almost certainly meant to be its own weird thing, there are no other firewand MAs and they haven't changed that despite having several supplements where they could have added them. Therefore, it seems to me that its likely that Righteous Devil Style is supposed to be isolated, and thus the one we should watch most carefully for breakage.<br /> <br /> Single-point style, however, is in a slightly different spot - despite the fact that to my knowledge there are no compatible styles as of yet (I guess you can technically use steel devil, and dual wield from draw or something, or pull a Taki and have one readied and the other). It's going to get the Violet Bier of Sorrows (unless we interpret 'it uses swords' to mean straight swords exclusively, which would seem odd, though defensible), which has historically been a powerful style. On a meta level, I also see it as unlikely that there's never another 'katana style'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T21:35:27-08:00","id":1292372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292368#post1292368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been having similar thoughts, and here's my 2c. Righteous Devil Style is almost certainly meant to be its own weird thing, there are no other firewand MAs and they haven't changed that despite having several supplements where they could have added them. Therefore, it seems to me that its likely that Righteous Devil Style is supposed to be isolated, and thus the one we should watch most carefully for breakage.<br /> <br /> Single-point style, however, is in a slightly different spot - despite the fact that to my knowledge there are no compatible styles as of yet (I guess you can technically use steel devil, and dual wield from draw or something, or pull a Taki and have one readied and the other). It's going to get the Violet Bier of Sorrows (unless we interpret 'it uses swords' to mean straight swords exclusively, which would seem odd, though defensible), which has historically been a powerful style. On a meta level, I also see it as unlikely that there's never another 'katana style'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We won't even know for at the very least 2 years unless lunars and exigents go much faster than DBs did.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T21:48:41-08:00","id":1292373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292372#post1292372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We won't even know for at the very least 2 years unless lunars and exigents go much faster than DBs did.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair, though I wouldn't count out an MA supplement at some point either (not VBoS, but another katana style). The real point is that styles compatible with SPSitVS are likely inevitable in ways that RDS is not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T22:05:48-08:00","id":1292379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292299#post1292299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, Ability prerequisites seem pretty loosely related to any Charm function and whether that Charm function seems to need skill or not - I'd scratch my head if trying to explain in detail why any of the Solar 'Essence Charged Arrow Attack' type Charms would actually *need* any particular level of skill. They just seem to be like that because that's the game design wants them to be restricted to characters who've met a certain level of investment, not because there's any obvious reason in setting why it should be so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. Wuxia and xianxia when they're fantasy genres are based on lots of elements from chinese mythology, taoism, chinese medicine, gong fu, etc which makes of skill requirements in magic an evidence in lots of cases. In those settings things like &quot;solar essence charged arrow attack charms&quot; needing skill seems easily explainable, evident and thematically necessary to me and probably lots of other wuxia and xianxia fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T23:41:16-08:00","id":1292392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RosePlancton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292379#post1292379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. Wuxia and xianxia when they're fantasy genres are based on lots of elements from chinese mythology, taoism, chinese medicine, gong fu, etc which makes of skill requirements in magic an evidence in lots of cases. In those settings things like &quot;solar essence charged arrow attack charms&quot; needing skill seems easily explainable, evident and thematically necessary to me and probably lots of other wuxia and xianxia fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also a common trope in the Hindu Vedas. And actually a good chunk of anime stories. Being really good at skills often lets you just do weird shit with that skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T23:45:40-08:00","id":1292394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292364#post1292364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'lunar martial artists are going to be the one-true-build for combat-focused lunar characters, which would be sad and overcentralizing'</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean you have to spend your lunar exp on something though and if MA's are only &quot;alright&quot; with lunars (no offensive combinations) then you'll just end up with every combat happy lunar running around with an artifact instead seeing as a) lunars can't favour MA so artifact charms cost the same and prerequisites are cheaper b) they don't care what sort of weapon it is as all weapons utilize the same charm set. Sure you can't stack artifact charms but i can't see a lunar going into two styles <i>and then</i> getting native offence charms, hell there's charms that support lunars wielding multiple artifacts anyway. Plus assuming your artifact is moonsliver (which it's gonna be) you still get to enjoy the resonant ability alongside Solars, compared to MA where you don't get Mastery.<br /> <br /> Besides lunar combat is kinda samey as they all share the same charm set regardless of if they're hitting something, shooting something or eating something as a tyrant lizard, making martial arts an attractive way to personalize your character seems reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25080,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","user":"Kargle18446","date":". 02-27-2019, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T00:36:19-08:00","id":1292401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292361#post1292361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So on the one hand there's Lunars being better at MA than Solars, but only by purchasing a bunch of native charms, and even then their combos are going to run them a lot more motes and willpower. Like if a Lunar wants to deal as much damage as a Solar with a MA attack, they can pump their strength excellency in it, but then they're spending more motes so it's not really like they're better? Since the Solar might get that for free with Mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to add to this, this also only applies to offence which is only half of combat. Solars get to combine their defensive charms with MAs as much as they want, which should (correct design assuming) be stronger than a Lunars defensive ones giving them a distinct advantage defensively compared to smaller disadvantage offensively. <br /> <br /> Alternatively if you want to go with a &quot;Stand alone&quot; style like RD, then a Solar can just grab a new dodge charm for every dexterity charm the lunar takes, meanikg while he'll definitely be worse at hitting he'll be much better at not getting hit, plus if hes got dodge as a supernatural he'll effectivly have the essence advantage as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25080,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","user":"Kargle18446","date":". 02-27-2019, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T01:29:40-08:00","id":1292405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RosePlancton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292379#post1292379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. Wuxia and xianxia when they're fantasy genres are based on lots of elements from chinese mythology, taoism, chinese medicine, gong fu, etc which makes of skill requirements in magic an evidence in lots of cases. In those settings things like &quot;solar essence charged arrow attack charms&quot; needing skill seems easily explainable, evident and thematically necessary to me and probably lots of other wuxia and xianxia fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm well aware of the genre and its tropes; it's that I'm not sure that anyone would really feel the difference if Ability pre-requisite scores were lower though, rather than rationalize it the way that they are generally loosely used already (note upthread arguments about whether 5 really means you are the one of the best in the world and so on).<br /> <br /> I suppose some of my grumbles about drawing a distinction between Solar Charms and Dragonblooded Charms on this topic come from a dislike of a trope where Solar Charms are portrayed as the righteous, fairly won and merited products of their own skill, naturally arising from their enlightenment, while Dragonblooded elemental Ability magic or Sidereal fate fuelled Ability magic is &quot;cheaty&quot; and something unfair with an undertone that we should cheer to see these beaten by the righteous skill of the Solars. All of which I find is extremely invidious and bad idea. But that is just another tangent here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T02:10:43-08:00","id":1292411,"title":"","content":"I've only skimmed the 16(!) pages of discussion, so sorry if I'm missing something elementary; but do we actually know that Lunars can combine native and MA charms? Ex3 core goes out of its way to specify that Solars can't combine MA charms with charms from other Abilities. Are we really sure that FatG won't impose similar attack-charm restrictions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T02:19:40-08:00","id":1292414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292411#post1292411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only skimmed the 16(!) pages of discussion, so sorry if I'm missing something elementary; but do we actually know that Lunars can combine native and MA charms? Ex3 core goes out of its way to specify that Solars can't combine MA charms with charms from other Abilities. Are we really sure that FatG won't impose similar attack-charm restrictions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Charm Preview 1:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunar Charms can be freely combined with Martial Arts Charms and Evocations. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T02:24:41-08:00","id":1292416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292414#post1292414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunar Charm Preview 1:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>OK, now the whole argument makes way more sense to me. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T05:30:41-08:00","id":1292458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bboat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1291370#post1291370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ravaging. Unless you're making a tasteless rape analogy, in which case, carry on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was uncalled for. Ravishment has actually been used by the gameline as a term for when a Fair Folk fed on a person's soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T05:52:22-08:00","id":1292468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292458#post1292458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was uncalled for. Ravishment has actually been used by the gameline as a term for when a Fair Folk fed on a person's soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>The gameline has played quite fast and loose with rape in its history, something I'm glad it's left behind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24035-bboat","name":"bboat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24035_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T06:27:03-08:00","id":1292473,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Just saying Epimetheus is just using a word that's been banded around a lot in Fair Folk context to the point where it has lost meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T06:42:19-08:00","id":1292474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292473#post1292473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. Just saying Epimetheus is just using a word that's been banded around a lot in Fair Folk context to the point where it has lost meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did mean ravaging. I just mispelled it and autocorrected it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:36:20-08:00","id":1292500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292373#post1292373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair, though I wouldn't count out an MA supplement at some point either (not VBoS, but another katana style). The real point is that styles compatible with SPSitVS are likely inevitable in ways that RDS is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I just remembered that we don't know how strong the style willl be. Violet bier was more powerful than normal in 2E because it combined charms that were native brawl charms into martial arts. If those charms go back, VBoS loses quite a few of the abilities it had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:13:30-08:00","id":1292542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292500#post1292500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I just remembered that we don't know how strong the style willl be. Violet bier was more powerful than normal in 2E because it combined charms that were native brawl charms into martial arts. If those charms go back, VBoS loses quite a few of the abilities it had.</div> </div> </div> </div>VBoS was powerful because of Life Severing Blow, Blade of the Battle Maiden, Joy in Adversity Stance, and its form. I suspect all of these things would need a second pass at the balance table. I don't know that brawl really existed then, or that VBoS' combo-ability was at the root of its power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T17:02:39-08:00","id":1292645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292542#post1292542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that brawl really existed then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brawl existed back in 1e. That's the reason they returned to it in 3e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T19:11:10-08:00","id":1292678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292645#post1292645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brawl existed back in 1e. That's the reason they returned to it in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought we were discussing 2e, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T19:38:03-08:00","id":1292683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1291019-why-are-lunars-allowed-to-combine-native-charms-and-martial-arts-again?p=1292678#post1292678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought we were discussing 2e, my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might've been my bad; my understanding was that 1e had Brawl and MA as two separate Abilities, 2e merged them into one, and consequently gave Violet Bier a bit of a power boost (though it was already a very potent style in 1e), and that it might get knocked down a bit now that the divide is back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T16:18:55-07:00","id":1298215,"title":"","content":"So going back to the OP now that the text has been out for a while, what I notice is it mostly focuses on how lunar charms enhancing martial arts attacks will break them, which makes sense since the lunar attack-creating charms werent out. But now what I feel actually really breaks things is martial arts charms enhancing lunar attacks.<br /> <br /> Take Behemoth Footprint Tread with Shining Starfall Execution and Fatal Stroke Flash. Now thats a lot of damage to roll against everyone within medium range with one attack. Or if you're not worried about damage but about hitting in the first place or your storyteller feels you have to actually use your feet (unarmed) why not do it with Bleeding Crescent Strike and White Reaper Form for double 9s on the attack roll and double 10s on damage on top of the attack and damage enhancers lunar have natively?<br /> <br /> So if anything needs to be nerfed about lunar martial arts I think charms like this in the lunar charmset need to specify they have to use Brawl on the attack roll or things get out of hand very fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 03-20-2019, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T00:10:16-07:00","id":1298277,"title":"","content":"I actually found that I dropped a lot of martial arts charms I was going to combo, in favour of Lunar charms; they're 20% cheaper, and often better.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say there aren't any broken combos out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T02:43:22-07:00","id":1298286,"title":"","content":"Is Behemoth's Footprint Tread actually good? It looks like the sort of charm you break out for the classic lone elder squatting in a First Age ruin whose expected to engage 5 PCs at once but outside of that &quot;I decisive <b>everyone</b> within medium range!&quot; is a pretty controversial tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T03:41:04-07:00","id":1298290,"title":"","content":"It is limited to people standing on the ground/floor so lunar buddies who know its comming can avoid it without too much trouble, and if you're in a duo-game with a solar mate they're going to be safe riding on your back (which they can now be even with you doing MA thanks to the Centaur mutation), so your party can usually be safe with a bit of cooperation. After that its down to how worried you are about collateral damage, but yeah I'd say slaying entire wyld hunts with a single attack is a good trick to have up your sleeve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T04:35:55-07:00","id":1298299,"title":"","content":"Presumably they need to move up a range band, otherwise everyone who matters can thwart this attack by jumping.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T06:18:09-07:00","id":1298307,"title":"","content":"There will be cases where a Martial Arts Charm will be better than a native Lunar Charm, or even do something which is not in their set. This, of course, is working as intended because otherwise, why by Martial Arts? It's not cheap for Lunars either.<br /> <br /> But, in this particular case it is probably too much. Mind you, we're talking Fatal Stroke Flash here. That Charm is too much, period, no matter what you combine it with. Most of the broken crap combo's I've seen in Martial Arts start with FSF, so hey, there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T06:55:14-07:00","id":1298312,"title":"","content":"That is a hilarious combo, but I will point out that it will probably kill your allies as often as your enemies. <br /> <br /> I will say though that I most worried/excited for combos that incorporate charms from Single Point Style or Righteous Devil, as those were quite clearly designed to be self-contained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T07:25:00-07:00","id":1298319,"title":"","content":"Yeah, definitely. I think combo-ing Tiger or Crane with Lunar charms is fine; they're expected to be combined with other styles when you have the XP for it anyway. There might be a few specific examples (someone, Sandact maybe, pointed out Snake's clash defence combined with a re-roll charm could be really good), but generally they should be fine.<br /> <br /> There might also be some things where you can combine Black Claw with Manipulation charms in a way you couldn't with Presence charms, but I don't think it's a big thing.<br /> <br /> On Righteous Devil, I'd say it's not too bad, because you can't combo it with Strength charms. And losing the Mastery is hefty for a couple of Righteous Devil charms (but I think just a couple). But there are some very good Dex charms to put with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow. I play a Snake-Totem kung-fu doctor, and if I could go back, I probably wouldn't have given her Martial Arts at all, just Dex and Strength charms to help her inflict her poison on people. A lot of the snake charms do things that other charms could have done anyway, for less XP.<br /> But I knew that was likely to happen when I made a Lunar character before the Lunar book came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}